{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/507138-would-exigents-suffer-the-great-curse","id":507138,"title":"Would Exigents suffer the Great Curse?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted","Exigents"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-05-07T13:46:33-07:00","id":507138,"title":"Would Exigents suffer the Great Curse?","content":"The Great Curse was the death curse of the Primordials after they were killed by the Exalted, and the cause of the collapse of the First Age as a result of it influencing the Solar, Lunar, Sidereal and Dragon Blooded. But what about the Exalted who came about after the end of the Primordial War? Would they suffer their own curse, despite not existing when the curse was originally laid? Or is the curse pervasive and insidious enough to infect an Exigent even long after the original event?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2034-jaytee","name":"JayTee","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2034_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1805"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-07T14:00:27-07:00","id":507171,"title":"","content":"I think an argument can be made for either way. This is, of course, pure speculation since I don't think it's more than an outline yet.<br /> <br /> At the moment, I kinda see it as a kinda badly mixed paint. The Great Curse splashed off the Unconquered Sun and onto the Solars, and maybe some &quot;spilled&quot; onto the Flame of Exigence. And when the Exigence is parceled out to a given god, different levels of the &quot;stain&quot; of the Great Curse come with it.<br /> <br /> I'm sure when the book comes out, I'll be totally wrong. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm a Woman, I'm a GM. <i>Of course</i> I'm Evil.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/424-dawaterrat","name":"DaWaterRat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar424_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"572"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-07T14:03:56-07:00","id":507175,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JayTee</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/507138-would-exigents-suffer-the-great-curse#post507138\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Great Curse was the death curse of the Primordials after they were killed by the Exalted, and the cause of the collapse of the First Age as a result of it influencing the Solar, Lunar, Sidereal and Dragon Blooded. But what about the Exalted who came about after the end of the Primordial War? Would they suffer their own curse, despite not existing when the curse was originally laid? Or is the curse pervasive and insidious enough to infect an Exigent even long after the original event?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd say yes, with maybe a few exceptions. I tend to see the curse as a perpetual pattern set upon the world that would target something along the lines of &quot;All chosen of the gods&quot;. The mentioned exceptions would fall upon those Exalts that are chosen of Other (like say, Liminals, if the Dark Mother isn't a God).<br /> <br /> As an addendum, I wouldn't see Infernals or Abyssals as being exempt from this either, as the curse would probably see them as (mutated/mutilated) chosen of Sol - their exaltations are still <i>of</i> him, even though they are not <i>from</i> him.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:lucida sans unicode\">Bearer of the legacy of Trauma Bear<br /> Need a dice-roller? Check out <a href=\"http://bit.ly/dicemat\" target=\"_blank\">Dicemat</a>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/43-fata-ku","name":"Fata-Ku","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar43_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2240"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-07T14:07:51-07:00","id":507176,"title":"","content":"A resounding &quot;maybe.&quot;<br /> <br /> Some Exigents existed and fought during the Primordial War, I thought. Some of those Exigents might have been &quot;one-shot Exaltations&quot; that were snuffed when their wielder died; others could have rebirth mechanics somehow.<br /> <br /> It really depends and there is no one universal answer, because each Exigent is its own individual splat with a proprietary individual Charmset. &quot;Exigent&quot; is a convenient catch-all term for every Exalt uplifted by a god or gods via infusing their nature with the Exigence at some point in time, but that's the sum total of what all Exigents have in common.<br /> <br /> So, maybe.<br /> <br /> They probably should have some kind of Limit mechanic even if it wasn't caused by Primordial death-throes though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-07T14:20:31-07:00","id":507213,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zelbinnean</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/507138-would-exigents-suffer-the-great-curse?p=507176#post507176\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They probably should have some kind of Limit mechanic even if it wasn't caused by Primordial death-throes though.</div> </div> </div> </div>I know the Great Curse is staying, but do we know if Limit is (as it was in 2e I mean)? I seem to remember the devs and writers commenting that it was a less-than-desirable behaviour mechanic.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:lucida sans unicode\">Bearer of the legacy of Trauma Bear<br /> Need a dice-roller? Check out <a href=\"http://bit.ly/dicemat\" target=\"_blank\">Dicemat</a>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/43-fata-ku","name":"Fata-Ku","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar43_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2240"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-07T15:04:01-07:00","id":507254,"title":"","content":"IIRC, they said there would be limit breaks but that they'd work differently.<br /> <br /> Which, without virtues, they'd have to.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-07T15:33:03-07:00","id":507279,"title":"","content":"That's true, I personally don't see the Limit track going anywhere, and I think Exigents should have their own personal moments of mythic hubris with a particular twist that suits their individualized nature.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-07T15:33:48-07:00","id":507282,"title":"","content":"Yeah, whether it takes the form of Limit, Resonance, Clarity, or whatever else, it's a safe bet that some form of personality/behavioral mechanic awaits Exigents and other new Exalted.* As far as the Great Curse itself, I could see things going either way.<br /> <br /> * Heck, splats in general. I don't think anybody expects, say, PC Fair Folk to lack such a thing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalted_3E:What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">The EX3 What We Know Wiki</a>, courtesy of Marin and JMobius<br /> <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com\" target=\"_blank\">Nishkriya, the EX3 Freelancer Quotes Tracker</a>, courtesy of Anathema and Moonwolf<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The White Wolf Forum Archive</a>, courtesy of The Dark Wizard and Sanctaphrax (see <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/PhilippeSaner?u=159709\" target=\"_blank\">its Patreon</a>) <hr />Arrghus: There's also the Shepherd of the North Star, busily guiding the one thing in all the heavens that <i>doesn't move</i>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","name":"Gaius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-07T15:49:12-07:00","id":507296,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zelbinnean</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/507138-would-exigents-suffer-the-great-curse?p=507176#post507176\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Some Exigents existed and fought during the Primordial War, I thought. Some of those Exigents might have been &quot;one-shot Exaltations&quot; that were snuffed when their wielder died; others could have rebirth mechanics somehow.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think that if they fought in the Primordial War, it's at least possible that the Curse affected the Flame of Exigence itself, and then descends upon all Exigents.<br /> <br /> I do hope that if they are Cursed, their book has guidelines/help for STs to design a unique manifestation of that for each character.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">She/Her. I am literal-minded and write literally. If I don't say something explicitly, please never assume I implied it. The only exception is if I try to make a joke.</span></span></span></div> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">My point of view may be different from yours but is equally valid.</span></span></span><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1x1ycoxJF0G9niMt5D3Pp7owZ7tw8AJvL?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted-cWoD-ArM url mega-library</a>. Exalted <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/663334-random-name-generator\" target=\"_blank\">name-generators</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","name":"Erinys","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar896_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4235"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-07T16:58:44-07:00","id":507391,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Erinys</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/507138-would-exigents-suffer-the-great-curse?p=507296#post507296\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think that if they fought in the Primordial War, it's at least possible that the Curse affected the Flame of Exigence itself, and then descends upon all Exigents.<br /> <br /> I do hope that if they are Cursed, their book has guidelines/help for STs to design a unique manifestation of that for each character.</div> </div> </div> </div>Really cool ideas here!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-07T21:37:31-07:00","id":507633,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Fata-Ku</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/507138-would-exigents-suffer-the-great-curse?p=507175#post507175\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As an addendum, I wouldn't see Infernals or Abyssals as being exempt from this either, as the curse would probably see them as (mutated/mutilated) chosen of Sol - their exaltations are still <i>of</i> him, even though they are not <i>from</i> him.</div> </div> </div> </div>Personally, I see both splats having the Curse removed by their Yozi/Neverborn creators. Since with Urges/Resonance to keep them in check, you don't need them going (even more, in some cases) insane on top of that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Life before Death, Strength before Weakness, Journey before Destination.&quot;<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#0000FF\">&quot;I will protect those who cannot protect themselves&quot;</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4172-marros56","name":"Marros56","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4172_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"143"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-07T21:58:09-07:00","id":507672,"title":"","content":"Even if Exigents aren't &quot;Cursed&quot; they'll still have some sort of mechanic (like Alchemical Clarity) that fills the same role. I am certain Liminals will have something similar.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-07T22:07:08-07:00","id":507677,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Marros56</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/507138-would-exigents-suffer-the-great-curse?p=507633#post507633\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Personally, I see both splats having the Curse removed by their Yozi/Neverborn creators.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Yozis didn't issue the Great Curse - even they don't have the power to revoke it; <i>at best</i>, they <i>maybe</i> convinced the Neverborn to do it for them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-07T22:55:06-07:00","id":507723,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JayTee</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/507138-would-exigents-suffer-the-great-curse#post507138\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Great Curse was the death curse of the Primordials after they were killed by the Exalted, and the cause of the collapse of the First Age as a result of it influencing the Solar, Lunar, Sidereal and Dragon Blooded. But what about the Exalted who came about after the end of the Primordial War? Would they suffer their own curse, despite not existing when the curse was originally laid? Or is the curse pervasive and insidious enough to infect an Exigent even long after the original event?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> From what I understood, the Great Curse affected the EXALTATIONS, not the exalts themselves. And those were limited in number. One of the things about abyssals and infernals is that they no longer have the curse; it was 'forgiven' in order to prevent it from making them less effective servants, and instead other limiters were in effect. However when those exalts die, their exaltations will never have the curse on them any more. They've been forgiven. Mostly this is useful to the Deathlords since they don't have to take a new abyssal to get 'forgiven' every time the bastard gets ganked. But this lends credence to the fact that it took even the Primordials the energy of their impossible deaths to lay the curse on those who slain them. They can't even re-curse abyssals if they were to be 'redeemed'; they can't muster up the power/auspicious moment to do so, unless one of the Yozi's were to let themselves get killed-killed.<br /> <br /> So as far as I can see, unless the thing that made the Exigent an exalt was already cursed, they wouldn't have one.<br /> <br /> [Edit] It's far more likely they have some other, similarly limiting mechanic based on their exalting factor. Probably focused around the God/spirit's purview. Or perhaps they (the gods) have the ability to urge them (The Exigents) like how the infernals are, since they (The infernals) thematically have a demon attached to their soul, if I remember anything close to correctly. [/Edit]","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1401,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1401-rungok","user":"rungok","date":". 05-08-2015, 01:58 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1401-rungok","name":"rungok","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1401_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"141"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-08T10:08:43-07:00","id":508179,"title":"","content":"Infernals are cursed. The Urge was added to them by twisting and manipulating the Curse. Autochthon and Gaia are both mentioned as possibly being able to lift the Curse, so it's possible the Yozis could to, but they didn't choose to.<br /> <br /> Abyssals had the Curse removed from their exaltations, so if any one of them redeems and becomes a Solar, they would remain cured. Once an exaltation is cured it becomes immune to the Curse. Likewise, if a particular Dragon-Blood was cured, all their Dragon-Blooded descendants would be immune to the Curse as well.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">She/Her. I am literal-minded and write literally. If I don't say something explicitly, please never assume I implied it. The only exception is if I try to make a joke.</span></span></span></div> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">My point of view may be different from yours but is equally valid.</span></span></span><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1x1ycoxJF0G9niMt5D3Pp7owZ7tw8AJvL?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted-cWoD-ArM url mega-library</a>. Exalted <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/663334-random-name-generator\" target=\"_blank\">name-generators</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","name":"Erinys","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar896_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4235"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-08T10:32:27-07:00","id":508186,"title":"","content":"Abyssal redemption being a get-out-of-curse-free card is frankly super boring and much less evocative than trading the monster you know for the one you don't.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-08T10:43:21-07:00","id":508195,"title":"","content":"Redemption is not in any way meant to be easy or &quot;free.&quot; It's also so vague that the ST has free reign to make it as hard as they want. There's no guarantee the Abyssal even survives it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">She/Her. I am literal-minded and write literally. If I don't say something explicitly, please never assume I implied it. The only exception is if I try to make a joke.</span></span></span></div> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">My point of view may be different from yours but is equally valid.</span></span></span><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1x1ycoxJF0G9niMt5D3Pp7owZ7tw8AJvL?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted-cWoD-ArM url mega-library</a>. Exalted <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/663334-random-name-generator\" target=\"_blank\">name-generators</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","name":"Erinys","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar896_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4235"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-08T11:12:41-07:00","id":508206,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Erinys</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/507138-would-exigents-suffer-the-great-curse?p=508195#post508195\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Redemption is not in any way meant to be easy or &quot;free.&quot; It's also so vague that the ST has free reign to make it as hard as they want. There's no guarantee the Abyssal even survives it.</div> </div> </div> </div>I am really against the notion that being &quot;redeemed&quot; puts you in an unambiguous, objectively better state. I never said anything about difficulty or survival. The fact is, I don't think a character should be able to &quot;earn&quot; themselves out of something like the Great Curse. You're no longer a horrible Resonance monster; great. Being a good enough person to be redeemed in UCS's eyes doesn't mean you should be out of the cloying, subconscious hubristic taint inherited by all other Exalts since the dawn of Creation's humanocentric epoch.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-08T11:24:41-07:00","id":508211,"title":"","content":"I do see your point as a thematic concept.<br /> <br /> I see it party as a thematic reward for the redemption itself -- a ray of hope representing the concept of redemption in a larger sense. An Abyssal who went through the process of Redemption has, arguably, done more to earn Solar Exaltation than a person who was Chosen by Sol for mortal excellence. Not that normal Solars didn't earn it, necessarily, but that the former Abyssal has gone through a huge amount of effort and soul-searching and maybe dangerous quests or something, and tried to change themselves on a fundamental level as a person, to reach that state. They aren't necessarily a better person morally because emulating a Solar doesn't have much morally attached to it. But they have repaired their self and their exaltation, a significant feat in an age where nearly everything else is going down the toilet fast.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">She/Her. I am literal-minded and write literally. If I don't say something explicitly, please never assume I implied it. The only exception is if I try to make a joke.</span></span></span></div> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">My point of view may be different from yours but is equally valid.</span></span></span><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1x1ycoxJF0G9niMt5D3Pp7owZ7tw8AJvL?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted-cWoD-ArM url mega-library</a>. Exalted <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/663334-random-name-generator\" target=\"_blank\">name-generators</a>.","edited":{"userid":896,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","user":"Erinys","date":". 05-08-2015, 02:37 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","name":"Erinys","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar896_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4235"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-08T18:55:03-07:00","id":508622,"title":"","content":"I'd likely impose a similar limit to when I wrote homebrew Assumption Charms for Fair Folk venturing into Autocthon or Malfeas, that they'd be subject to the ideals of the power that was granted/had acquired their Exigence, and would acquire Limit if they acted against those ideals. Assuming that Limit and Limit Breaks are still a thing, those that would be applicable to them would probably be based upon their patron... and would likely be built to suit. Might even be based on a similar mechanic to NWoD's Virtue and Vice mechanic.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Crunch isn't a hobby; it's a calling.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1959-hexmeister-vic","name":"Hexmeister Vic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1959_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"764"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-08T19:22:38-07:00","id":508633,"title":"","content":"I wonder if, even absent the Great Curse, the &quot;dirty bomb Exigents&quot; might tend to have a limit and limit break mechanic of mental instability, to reflect them being bizarre &quot;aberrations&quot; cobbled together from ill-fitting and weirdly synergistic essences.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">She/Her. I am literal-minded and write literally. If I don't say something explicitly, please never assume I implied it. The only exception is if I try to make a joke.</span></span></span></div> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">My point of view may be different from yours but is equally valid.</span></span></span><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1x1ycoxJF0G9niMt5D3Pp7owZ7tw8AJvL?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted-cWoD-ArM url mega-library</a>. Exalted <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/663334-random-name-generator\" target=\"_blank\">name-generators</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","name":"Erinys","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar896_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4235"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-08T19:25:16-07:00","id":508635,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zelbinnean</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/507138-would-exigents-suffer-the-great-curse?p=508206#post508206\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I am really against the notion that being &quot;redeemed&quot; puts you in an unambiguous, objectively better state. I never said anything about difficulty or survival. The fact is, I don't think a character should be able to &quot;earn&quot; themselves out of something like the Great Curse. .</div> </div> </div> </div>They don't &quot;earn&quot; themselves out of being Cursed. An Abyssal starts out uncursed. Saying they get Cursed somehow after becoming a Solar again is obscenely silly.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>SWTOR Referal: <a href=\"http://www.swtor.com/r/JQ2nqy\" target=\"_blank\">http://www.swtor.com/r/JQ2nqy</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/414-gallus","name":"Gallus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar414_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"886"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-08T20:06:27-07:00","id":508654,"title":"","content":"Well, maybe they shouldn't be &quot;uncursed&quot;. Maybe the curse is dormant. Maybe the curse is twisted into resonance.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-08T20:30:24-07:00","id":508667,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/507138-would-exigents-suffer-the-great-curse?p=508654#post508654\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, maybe they shouldn't be &quot;uncursed&quot;. Maybe the curse is dormant. Maybe the curse is twisted into resonance.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hunh. Hadn't really looked at it like that, but yeah. I dig the idea. The Great Curse is meant to bring the Exalted to ruin, and is then twisted around to also bring Creation as a whole to ruin.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalted_3E:What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">The EX3 What We Know Wiki</a>, courtesy of Marin and JMobius<br /> <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com\" target=\"_blank\">Nishkriya, the EX3 Freelancer Quotes Tracker</a>, courtesy of Anathema and Moonwolf<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The White Wolf Forum Archive</a>, courtesy of The Dark Wizard and Sanctaphrax (see <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/PhilippeSaner?u=159709\" target=\"_blank\">its Patreon</a>) <hr />Arrghus: There's also the Shepherd of the North Star, busily guiding the one thing in all the heavens that <i>doesn't move</i>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","name":"Gaius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-08T21:19:39-07:00","id":508745,"title":"","content":"Exactly. To be honest, with the Great Curse as the final death-curse of the Primordials, their great revenge, I feel like they shouldn't be able to lift it, or at least not easily.<br /> Twisting it into a blight on the Creation that betrayed them, a new vector for the curse, seems more appropriate.<br /> <br /> But mainly it's just so I can say that one of my current Eclipse PCs is the reincarnation of his former Moonshadow PC, with someone who got cleansed in the middle, without having to say he has no Limit track.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-08T21:20:57-07:00","id":508746,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Erinys</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/507138-would-exigents-suffer-the-great-curse?p=508195#post508195\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Redemption is not in any way meant to be easy or &quot;free.&quot; It's also so vague that the ST has free reign to make it as hard as they want. There's no guarantee the Abyssal even survives it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Being redeemed with a final sacrifice seems most appropriate for tragic anti-heroes anyway.<br /> Like Darth Vader.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-09T00:02:11-07:00","id":508805,"title":"","content":"I don't really see why everyone needs a pseudo-Limit mechanic even without the Great Curse (Alchemical Clarity, Fair Folk have... I don't remember, Bedlam or something?)<br /> <br /> late 2E even said that un-Cursed Exalts still have a Limit track, I never understood the point of that bit...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5488-goldfaction","name":"goldfaction","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"90"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-09T01:23:28-07:00","id":508817,"title":"","content":"Because magic attacks that drove people insane generally worked by giving Exalts limit. Not because they exacerbated the Great Curse per-se, just because it was the easiest way to model insanity-inducing attacks.<br /> <br /> I don't think everyone one <i>needs</i> a limit track, for the game to work, but Grabowski wanted it to be a game of flawed and tragic heroes, and so decided all Exalted need some mechanic to enforce this. If they still go with that logic, there's not a particular reason Exigents should be less affected than other Exalts. If they don't. then there's no need to give Solars limit.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-09T01:51:36-07:00","id":508835,"title":"","content":"*shrug*<br /> <br /> WW/OP games have a long history of including splat-specific personality/behavioral mechanics like that. Just kind of a signature that can inject some extra texture into a splat. When they work well, they can help create interesting and engaging gaming experiences, especially when encouraging or facilitating players to do fun and interesting things they might not otherwise do.<br /> <br /> The issue I could reasonably see someone taking is that... Well, I'm not sure about the historical Exalted hit-to-miss ratio. &gt;.&gt; All forms of Limit Break (Solars, Lunars, Sidereals, DBs) just really didn't do much for me, Abyssal Resonance seemed pretty decidedly unfun, and Raksha Bedlam seemed to be in a race with them for the bottom.* On the other hand, I think Alchemical Clarity was well-received, and <s>Torment</s> Acts of Villainy (let's be honest) got plenty of praise for being a lot of fun.<br /> <br /> I know Vance has written the rules for EX3 Solar Limit, so I'm interested in seeing what he's done. I imagine he won't have forgotten that a mechanic being unfun for the character isn't the same as a mechanic being unfun for the <i>player</i>. That feels like the biggest problem these things wind up having.<br /> <br /> * To those unacquainted, your character's Virtue dots basically were your Limit Tracks. Yes, Raksha had 4 different &quot;Limit&quot; tracks, each one no greater than 5 in length. They emptied when spending Virtue channels (including a Lure that forced you to spend one at certain times) or spending Willpower against mental influence, and possibly some other circumstances I can't recall. When emptied, each one brought on its own unpleasant and persistent condition that only went away when you destroyed several meaningful things/relationships/etc. your character had built up (except Valor, which involved fleeing from fights, feeling like a slap on the wrist by comparison). And they weren't mutually exclusive, either: you could absolutely go through all of them at the same time.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalted_3E:What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">The EX3 What We Know Wiki</a>, courtesy of Marin and JMobius<br /> <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com\" target=\"_blank\">Nishkriya, the EX3 Freelancer Quotes Tracker</a>, courtesy of Anathema and Moonwolf<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The White Wolf Forum Archive</a>, courtesy of The Dark Wizard and Sanctaphrax (see <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/PhilippeSaner?u=159709\" target=\"_blank\">its Patreon</a>) <hr />Arrghus: There's also the Shepherd of the North Star, busily guiding the one thing in all the heavens that <i>doesn't move</i>.","edited":{"userid":558,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","user":"Gaius","date":". 05-09-2015, 04:55 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","name":"Gaius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-09T02:07:47-07:00","id":508839,"title":"","content":"I generally enjoyed Solar limit breaks. Lunar limit breaks were also fine, but too short so often had little effect (once I limit broke while carrying half the party on my back while flying across a desert, so decided to drop down and go to sleep in an abandoned, demon-cursed city, stranding them there. That was fun. But generally the scene-long length of them, and the fact that they are caused by the Moon, so often happen when the PCs have gone to bed, rather than in the middle of an exciting scene, means they're normally not very significant). I've played 5 or 6 DB games, and have seen a DB limit break a total of once (a high valour girl whose player rolled limit a lot more than the rules really demanded of her).<br /> Resonance, on the other hand, was severely debilitating unless you were playing a loyalist, in which case it was relatively insignificant.<br /> <br /> Clarity was good though, because part of the point of playing an Alchemical is trying to maintain your humanity when you are, in fact, a golem and not human at all. It worked pretty well at making that a significant (but not crippling) issue.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-09T04:34:16-07:00","id":508859,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Resonance, on the other hand, was severely debilitating unless you were playing a loyalist, in which case it was relatively insignificant. </div> </div> </div>Or a boon. You could intentionally answer to your mortal name for a series of scenes, then intentionally vent your resonance to carry a shadowland around you. Or build Intimacies to people, and vent your resonance to kill them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-09T04:58:58-07:00","id":508864,"title":"","content":"Hmmm... did the intimacies have to be positive?<br /> But yes, the Shadowland was definitely a boon. And of course, if you look like a terrifying monster and plants drop dead around you... who cares? You are a terrifying monster out to destroy life.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-09T06:18:56-07:00","id":508877,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gallus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/507138-would-exigents-suffer-the-great-curse?p=508635#post508635\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> They don't &amp;quot;earn&amp;quot; themselves out of being Cursed. An Abyssal starts out uncursed. Saying they get Cursed somehow after becoming a Solar again is obscenely silly.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not a fan of this because I think not even the Yozis or Neverborn should have the power to casually rescind their own death-curse. Twist it to better suit the servants of their diminished forms, sure, but removing it is beyond even their ken or power, just by the nature of the circumstances surrounding the &quot;casting&quot; of the curse to begin with. <br /> <br /> In 3e terms, to give an (unnecessary) mechanical analogy, it'd be like all the Primordials, both dead and diminished, working together to levy a great sorcerous working at once, a confluence of spiteful power that could never again be equaled.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-09T07:09:18-07:00","id":508897,"title":"","content":"I agree with you Zelbinnean, you've put it better than me.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-09T08:03:51-07:00","id":508975,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>goldfaction</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/507138-would-exigents-suffer-the-great-curse?p=508805#post508805\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">late 2E even said that un-Cursed Exalts still have a Limit track, I never understood the point of that bit...</div> </div> </div> </div>The in-universe explanation is that Autochthon designed them with a mental defense against insanity-inducing Primordial magic. Before the Great Curse, limit was ony a thing inflicted by insanity-inducing magics, and when you hit limit break you just temporarily lost a dot of permanent Willpower.<br /> <br /> I feel that if the Great Curse is truly impossible to cure, then that sucks all the hope out of the setting. I know the default assumption is supposed to be that the world crumbles into shit and everyone dies, but I want the PCs to be able to avert that!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">She/Her. I am literal-minded and write literally. If I don't say something explicitly, please never assume I implied it. The only exception is if I try to make a joke.</span></span></span></div> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">My point of view may be different from yours but is equally valid.</span></span></span><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1x1ycoxJF0G9niMt5D3Pp7owZ7tw8AJvL?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted-cWoD-ArM url mega-library</a>. Exalted <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/663334-random-name-generator\" target=\"_blank\">name-generators</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","name":"Erinys","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar896_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4235"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-09T08:06:18-07:00","id":508977,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Erinys</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/507138-would-exigents-suffer-the-great-curse?p=508975#post508975\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I feel that if the Great Curse is truly impossible to cure, then that sucks all the hope out of the setting. I know the default assumption is supposed to be that the world crumbles into shit and everyone dies, but I want the PCs to be able to avert that!</div> </div> </div> </div>The Primordials can't casually rescind it for their own ends != the Great Curse is impossible to cure.<br /> <br /> Also the notion that &quot;if we can't cure the Great Curse, there is no hope&quot; - that is not even remotely approaching good logic.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-09T10:23:15-07:00","id":509085,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zelbinnean</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/507138-would-exigents-suffer-the-great-curse?p=508977#post508977\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also the notion that &quot;if we can't cure the Great Curse, there is no hope&quot; - that is not even remotely approaching good logic.</div> </div> </div> </div>Could you go more in to this? I've always been under the impression that this is true, because eventually it will undermine every good thing the Exalted do.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2034-jaytee","name":"JayTee","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2034_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1805"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-09T10:31:24-07:00","id":509090,"title":"","content":"Keep in mind my idea of &quot;hope&quot; is to restore just rule and civilization, long-term, to at least a chunk of the world.<br /> <br /> On a short-term local scale, your PC can't have a happy ending unless they die before going crazy. If they live long enough to go crazy, they will ruin every bit of good they did before. They can't make any lasting improvement to the world.<br /> <br /> Geoff Grabowski was explicit that the default ending is for all the Exalted to keep fighting each other while the Deathlords and Fair Folk tear Creation apart underneath them, until nothing is left.<br /> The only way to maybe have a chance to stop that is to get the Exalted working together against these threats to Creation, because without Solar and Lunar allies, the Sidereals and Terrestrials have been unable/unwilling to defend the world (partly due to their own Curse).<br /> But Solars and Lunars, allowed to take over, will just do the very things that the Bronze Faction deposed them for: tear Creation apart (due to the Curse).<br /> <br /> I just personally don't like that being the default.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">She/Her. I am literal-minded and write literally. If I don't say something explicitly, please never assume I implied it. The only exception is if I try to make a joke.</span></span></span></div> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">My point of view may be different from yours but is equally valid.</span></span></span><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1x1ycoxJF0G9niMt5D3Pp7owZ7tw8AJvL?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted-cWoD-ArM url mega-library</a>. Exalted <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/663334-random-name-generator\" target=\"_blank\">name-generators</a>.","edited":{"userid":896,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","user":"Erinys","date":". 05-09-2015, 01:45 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","name":"Erinys","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar896_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4235"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-09T13:31:13-07:00","id":509217,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Erinys</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/507138-would-exigents-suffer-the-great-curse?p=509090#post509090\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Geoff Grabowski was explicit that the default ending is for all the Exalted to keep fighting each other while the Deathlords and Fair Folk tear Creation apart underneath them, until nothing is left.<br /> The only way to maybe have a chance to stop that is to get the Exalted working together against these threats to Creation, because without Solar and Lunar allies, the Sidereals and Terrestrials have been unable/unwilling to defend the world (partly due to their own Curse).<br /> But Solars and Lunars, allowed to take over, will just do the very things that the Bronze Faction deposed them for: tear Creation apart (due to the Curse).<br /> <br /> I just personally don't like that being the default.</div> </div> </div> </div>That is indeed a pretty awful default in my opinion. Really because it takes away the fact that a lot of people will make immoral choices if it benefits them and theirs, or if there is no consequence for doing so.<br /> <br /> At the same time, monstrous actions are made less monstrous if you can just say &quot;oh I was cursed this whole time,&quot; or if the monstrousness was attributable to the curse, even if you didn't know about the curse. <br /> <br /> This isn't meant to be a knock against D&amp;D, but &quot;the curse is really the problem, not human nature&quot; sounds much more like the kind of reasoning you might find in a D&amp;D module, versus where White Wolf usually sets the blame: on beings both more and less than human, who are still bound by the imperfect foibles that define the human condition even with all their superhuman power. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JayTee</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/507138-would-exigents-suffer-the-great-curse?p=509085#post509085\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Could you go more in to this? I've always been under the impression that this is true, because eventually it will undermine every good thing the Exalted do.</div> </div> </div> </div>I recall it's been said that the First Age didn't<i> just </i>end due to the Great Curse. It ended because people in power who were removed from humanity were corrupted by their removal from power and lack of humanity. <br /> <br /> Did the Curse help this? Probably, almost assuredly.<br /> <br /> Is it reasonable to think that even without the Curse, living for 4000 years and having the power to reshape memories with a poem or fling sunfire from your sword that can scorch gods into non-existence or dipping your hand into raw Possibility and drawing forth a silver mine and the people to work it radically skews your perspective and personal moral compass? Definitely. <br /> <br /> By the same token, it's very possible the Usurpation would have happened even if there was no Great Curse. Making a bunch of Exalted effectively lower-class citizens under the rule of a few, with no way to break that glass ceiling, is going to create generations of resentment.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-09T13:36:00-07:00","id":509221,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zelbinnean</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/507138-would-exigents-suffer-the-great-curse?p=509217#post509217\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I recall it's been said that the First Age didn't<i> just </i>end due to the Great Curse. It ended because people in power who were removed from humanity were corrupted by their removal from power and lack of humanity.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's also been literally said that as soon as the Solars were dead and no longer affected by the Curse, almost all of them realized the terrible things they'd done, repented for their sins and went to Lethe, with the sole exception of the twelve who became the Deathlords. In other words, only twelve of the Solars really <i>meant</i> to do any of those bad things.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/598-couch","name":"Couch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar598_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"330"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-09T13:42:27-07:00","id":509225,"title":"","content":"Interesting, I have heard the opposite to be true, that the Great Curse was almost wholly responsible for the fall of the First Age and events that lead to the Usurpation.<br /> <br /> I think I prefer that over &quot;humanity is innately doomed by their own hand&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2034-jaytee","name":"JayTee","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2034_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1805"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-09T13:47:47-07:00","id":509227,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Couch</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/507138-would-exigents-suffer-the-great-curse?p=509221#post509221\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's also been literally said that as soon as the Solars were dead and no longer affected by the Curse, almost all of them realized the terrible things they'd done, repented for their sins and went to Lethe, with the sole exception of the twelve who became the Deathlords. In other words, only twelve of the Solars really <i>meant</i> to do any of those bad things.</div> </div> </div> </div>That kind of automatic moral absolution is truly terrible and does nothing good for the setting.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JayTee</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/507138-would-exigents-suffer-the-great-curse?p=509225#post509225\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Interesting, I have heard the opposite to be true, that the Great Curse was almost wholly responsible for the fall of the First Age and events that lead to the Usurpation.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh?<br /> <br /> I just.....I don't like that. It's such an easy out excuse for bad behavior. Or it comes across that way to me.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JayTee</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/507138-would-exigents-suffer-the-great-curse?p=509225#post509225\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think I prefer that over &quot;humanity is innately doomed by their own hand&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>It doesn't have to be quite that dramatic. Though I prefer that very-powerful humans will express the flaws of normal humans, except on a much bigger scale due to their power, is pretty appropriate. It re-orients the &quot;win condition,&quot; such as it is, from finding the equivalent to an an epic level Breach Enchantment, to fundamentally changing worldwide cultural behavior.<br /> <br /> I prefer that kind of story in Exalted. Again, the former just feels too D&amp;D to me. I enjoy D&amp;D, but I go to it for very different themes than Exalted. D&amp;D is much more morally-absolute in a lot of ways. &quot;All orcs are evil. Why? Because they're orcs, duh!&quot; - this is canon, baseline D&amp;D.<br /> <br /> But &quot;actions have consequences&quot; becomes somewhat less meaningful if you can just say &quot;oh all that bad shit I did? That was because I was cursed. I'm a really nice guy actually.&quot; That's such a cop out.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":3420,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","user":"Zelbinnean","date":". 05-09-2015, 04:50 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-09T14:01:38-07:00","id":509230,"title":"","content":"<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zelbinnean</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/507138-would-exigents-suffer-the-great-curse?p=509227#post509227\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh?<br /> <br /> I just.....I don't like that. It's such an easy out excuse for bad behavior. Or it comes across that way to me.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah, I never saw it as something that excused bad behavior, it was just the insidious cause.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zelbinnean</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/507138-would-exigents-suffer-the-great-curse?p=509227#post509227\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But &quot;actions have consequences&quot; becomes somewhat less meaningful if you can just say &quot;oh all that bad shit I did? That was because I was cursed. I'm a really nice guy actually.&quot; That's such a cop out.</div> </div> </div> </div>Focusing on this part because it's the most relevant to my personal viewpoints.<br /> <br /> Actions still have consequences if your evil acts are caused by the Great Curse. You still have to make amends with people you wronged, who wont be inclined to believe you that &quot;It wasn't really me.&quot; You still have to fix what you broke, if possible, or try to replace it. If you killed someone innocent in the grip of the Curse, you have to deal with the fact that it was your hand that did the deed and suffer the fallout for it. The consequences still happen, they're just different, not less.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2034-jaytee","name":"JayTee","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2034_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1805"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-09T14:07:52-07:00","id":509232,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JayTee</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/507138-would-exigents-suffer-the-great-curse?p=509230#post509230\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Actions still have consequences if your evil acts are caused by the Great Curse. You still have to make amends with people you wronged, who wont be inclined to believe you that &quot;It wasn't really me.&quot; You still have to fix what you broke, if possible, or try to replace it. If you killed someone innocent in the grip of the Curse, you have to deal with the fact that it was your hand that did the deed and suffer the fallout for it. The consequences still happen, they're just different, not less.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's very true, you're right. <br /> <br /> I guess it's less &quot;actions don't have consequences&quot; so much as it is &quot;I didn't intend for these actions&quot; or something like that.<br /> <br /> I still don't like having the possibility of making it so the Exalted would all live in rainbow gumdrop land harmony with each other forever if not for that big mean Curse that was so terribly inflicted on them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-09T14:24:54-07:00","id":509241,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zelbinnean</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/507138-would-exigents-suffer-the-great-curse?p=509232#post509232\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's very true, you're right.<br /> <br /> I guess it's less &quot;actions don't have consequences&quot; so much as it is &quot;I didn't intend for these actions&quot; or something like that.<br /> <br /> I still don't like having the possibility of making it so the Exalted would all live in rainbow gumdrop land harmony with each other forever if not for that big mean Curse that was so terribly inflicted on them.</div> </div> </div> </div>A true utopia (defined as solving all the problems of the setting forever) is probably impossible, if only because the constant threat of the Wyld, the Underworld and Malfeas, not to mention the new dangers that might be added in the new edition. That said, assuming that the Curse is cured and the Exalted unite once more, most of their troubles will be external, rather than internal. Conflict will still be a thing, but it just wont be Exalt vs Exalt.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2034,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2034-jaytee","user":"JayTee","date":". 05-09-2015, 05:41 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2034-jaytee","name":"JayTee","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2034_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1805"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-09T14:43:44-07:00","id":509249,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JayTee</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/507138-would-exigents-suffer-the-great-curse?p=509230#post509230\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ah, I never saw it as something that excused bad behavior, it was just the insidious cause.</div> </div> </div> </div>I very much dislike it as the insidious cause.<br /> <br /> A major part of the appeal of Exalted is that it's very humanistic in its morality. If you want to do good by others, you need to decide for yourself what doing good by others means, and think about the consequences of your actions, rather than there being an objective moral code you can follow. You can still be what others would consider a good guy, but it's not simple or easy.<br /> <br /> Then you suddenly have the Curse, which even if you don't think it dooms Creation to ruin, still imposes an inhuman destructive bent on the Exalted. It takes away from the idea that you have to decide what you're going to do with your power by saying &quot;oh, but sometimes you'll just act a certain way anyway and there's no decision&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/598-couch","name":"Couch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar598_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"330"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-09T14:50:31-07:00","id":509251,"title":"","content":"I doubt that curing the Curse would guarantee it. It would remove the guaranteed &quot;YOU LOSE&quot; sign currently posted in the setting.<br /> <br /> If the Curse was not part of the setting, and the excesses of the Exalted were due entirely to human failings, then what? What then depends on how the ST and players view human nature, I guess.<br /> <br /> You can decide that humans are so flawed, or Exaltation is fundamentally so warping, that Exalted are fundamentally incapable of handling the power responsibly, and Creation's pretty much doomed, as above. The best you can hope for is to replace human rule with something at least competent, but judging by the options available so far (gods and Yozis) things aren't looking good.<br /> <br /> The other, more hopeful option (and also my assumption in the event that the Curse existed but gets cured) is that human nature is flawed and Exaltation warps people, but they can still, <b><i>potentially</i></b>, find a way to build a society that's self-sustaining, can defend Creation, and won't create the same abuses that messed up the First Age. It won't look anything like democracy or equality for all humans, but it could potentially be just or benevolent at least to some extent and from some views.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Interestingly, right now as the setting is, both Sidereal factions' plans are doomed: both support Cursed Exalted rulers whose glaring flaws they're unable to deal with, neither is trying to find the source of the insanity, and the current status quo is depicted as unable to defend Creation adequately from Deathlords, Fae, etc. The Gold Faction at least recognize the lastr fact, which makes them look way less idiotic in my eyes.<br /> <br /> But if the setting were presented in which the Great Curse didn't exist, and things were written so that the Dragon-Blooded and Sidereals were, actually capable of preserving Creation without Celestial help (<i>without, uh, making Lunars useless again. don't know if that can be done</i>) then it only comes down to which sort of Exalted is most likely/able to build a better society that encourages wise rule, and least likely to go back to abusing their power?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">She/Her. I am literal-minded and write literally. If I don't say something explicitly, please never assume I implied it. The only exception is if I try to make a joke.</span></span></span></div> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">My point of view may be different from yours but is equally valid.</span></span></span><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1x1ycoxJF0G9niMt5D3Pp7owZ7tw8AJvL?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted-cWoD-ArM url mega-library</a>. Exalted <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/663334-random-name-generator\" target=\"_blank\">name-generators</a>.","edited":{"userid":896,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","user":"Erinys","date":". 05-09-2015, 06:09 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","name":"Erinys","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar896_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4235"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-09T14:51:24-07:00","id":509253,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JayTee</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/507138-would-exigents-suffer-the-great-curse?p=509241#post509241\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A true utopia (defined as solving all the problems of the setting forever) is probably impossible, if only because the constant threat of the Wyld, the Underworld and Malfeas, not to mention the new dangers that might be added in the new edition. That said, assuming that the Curse is cured and the Exalted unite once more, most of their troubles will be external, rather than internal. Conflict will still be a thing, but it just wont be Exalt vs Exalt.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't see that as reasonable given that Exalts are still human beings with human personalities. I think the Primordial War only worked because of the giant external threat, and the First Age showed that absent such a threat that couldn't easily be controlled, human excesses would dominate over sound, selfless policy (which is human nature).<br /> <br /> I don't want to get rid of the human aspect, or whitewash the fact that all Exalts certainly wouldn't be Lawful Good Paladins even if the Curse was cured. And actually that statement from Solar ghosts says exactly that, which is why I find it abhorrent.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-09T14:51:45-07:00","id":509254,"title":"","content":"The Great Curse is, and never was, an excuse for bad behaviour. What it did was <i>magnify</i> it. Add in comiscally reinformed mental instability and things are going to get bad. The Curse created a perfect s***storm of ego and crazy that led to a genocide and apocolypse. Yes, humans of done terrible things, but humans also never lived in a state of minimal global want. Without the Curse things would have never gotten as bad as they did.<br /> <br /> I'm also not sure how one comes to he the conclusion that the lifting of the Curse from Abyssals was done &quot;casually&quot;. Maybe it was as easy as the Neverborn(singular or plural) who leveled it upon thier death saying, &quot;No more.&quot; Maybe it wasn't. There is no information one way or the other so far as I am aware. Which was/is likely intentional.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>SWTOR Referal: <a href=\"http://www.swtor.com/r/JQ2nqy\" target=\"_blank\">http://www.swtor.com/r/JQ2nqy</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/414-gallus","name":"Gallus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar414_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"886"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-09T15:05:21-07:00","id":509259,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zelbinnean</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/507138-would-exigents-suffer-the-great-curse?p=509253#post509253\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't see that as reasonable given that Exalts are still human beings with human personalities. I think the Primordial War only worked because of the giant external threat, and the First Age showed that absent such a threat that couldn't easily be controlled, human excesses would dominate over sound, selfless policy (which is human nature).<br /> <br /> I don't want to get rid of the human aspect, or whitewash the fact that all Exalts certainly wouldn't be Lawful Good Paladins even if the Curse was cured. And actually that statement from Solar ghosts says exactly that, which is why I find it abhorrent.</div> </div> </div> </div>This feels too cynical to me. Like, I get that the Exalted are human and they have human passions, but I like to believe that eventually they'll overcome these divisions and work together. I dunno, maybe I'm just naively optimistic about this kinda thing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2034-jaytee","name":"JayTee","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2034_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1805"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-09T15:13:17-07:00","id":509263,"title":"","content":"I'm normally the misanthropic pessimist in any conversation about humanity 'cause I think 90% of humans are completely selfish and almost entirely devoid of compassion. But! I also see that as purely a cultural malaise, not something that we can't improve upon. Humans are capable of being very selfless and kind.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">She/Her. I am literal-minded and write literally. If I don't say something explicitly, please never assume I implied it. The only exception is if I try to make a joke.</span></span></span></div> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">My point of view may be different from yours but is equally valid.</span></span></span><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1x1ycoxJF0G9niMt5D3Pp7owZ7tw8AJvL?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted-cWoD-ArM url mega-library</a>. Exalted <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/663334-random-name-generator\" target=\"_blank\">name-generators</a>.","edited":{"userid":896,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","user":"Erinys","date":". 05-09-2015, 06:15 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","name":"Erinys","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar896_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4235"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-09T15:17:04-07:00","id":509265,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gallus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/507138-would-exigents-suffer-the-great-curse?p=509254#post509254\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm also not sure how one comes to he the conclusion that the lifting of the Curse from Abyssals was done &quot;casually&quot;. Maybe it was as easy as the Neverborn(singular or plural) who leveled it upon thier death saying, &quot;No more.&quot; Maybe it wasn't. There is no information one way or the other so far as I am aware. Which was/is likely intentional.</div> </div> </div> </div>In the absence of any detail, it comes across (to me) as very casual. Like &quot;we got these Exaltations now so let's just unplug the curse module and....ok Deathlords, go for it, we'll be over here wailing in agony some more.&quot; Yeah, that's tongue in cheek, but I have no evidence that it was hard for them to rescind their curse, so in the absence of evidence, that is my assumption.<br /> <br /> If those details don't matter to the setting (and they probably don't, in the same way as 2e got way too absorbed in pointless ancient history), then I don't see a lot gained from &quot;redeemed Abyssal is free from curse&quot; unless it's just supposed to be ironic that you have to go through being the Anti-Life Equation to turn into an unburdened Solar. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JayTee</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/507138-would-exigents-suffer-the-great-curse?p=509259#post509259\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This feels too cynical to me. Like, I get that the Exalted are human and they have human passions, but I like to believe that eventually they'll overcome these divisions and work together. I dunno, maybe I'm just naively optimistic about this kinda thing.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't want to say it's naive, but it is optimistic, and frankly, it seems to run counter to basically all examples of what actually happens when people wield great power IRL. Creation's humans are functionally identical to real humans in terms of behavior, and Exalted are fundamentally humans, so I don't expect them to generally act different from humans. The Exalted are also set apart from humanity and more powerful than mortals, and I can't imagine class privilege <i>not </i>forming for them, even without the actual intent to do so or the impetus from the Curse. <br /> <br /> I mean, for every Solar who is Captain America and exhibits those really iconic good-guy personality traits, you are going to have Red Skulls and Thanoses and probably even Ultrons, who will do terrible things under the justification of something good.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-09T15:19:46-07:00","id":509266,"title":"","content":"My (admittedly limited) understanding of socioeconomics has lead me to believe that people only really do bad things when they're already in a bad situation (poverty, oppression, etc) or are under irrational beliefs with no basis in fact (racism, sexism, etc)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2034-jaytee","name":"JayTee","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2034_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1805"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-09T15:23:01-07:00","id":509267,"title":"","content":"Do you count class prejudice as one of those irrational beliefs?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">She/Her. I am literal-minded and write literally. If I don't say something explicitly, please never assume I implied it. The only exception is if I try to make a joke.</span></span></span></div> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">My point of view may be different from yours but is equally valid.</span></span></span><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1x1ycoxJF0G9niMt5D3Pp7owZ7tw8AJvL?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted-cWoD-ArM url mega-library</a>. Exalted <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/663334-random-name-generator\" target=\"_blank\">name-generators</a>.","edited":{"userid":896,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","user":"Erinys","date":". 05-09-2015, 06:26 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","name":"Erinys","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar896_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4235"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-09T15:23:42-07:00","id":509268,"title":"","content":"Irrational belief in the importance of money, probably.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2034-jaytee","name":"JayTee","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2034_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1805"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-09T18:00:58-07:00","id":509345,"title":"","content":"There have been tons of Emperors and dictators who've done bad things to people because they could, because they had the power and they enjoyed it. Not all did, but plenty did.<br /> You could argue that it's an irrational belief that some people are worth more than others, but frankly, that's entirely rational.<br /> I mean, if you're not punished for it by society, selfishness is rational. Altruism is irrational. Kindness is irrational. Love is irrational.<br /> <br /> At the end of the day, sometimes evil is irrational, but a lot of the time it's perfectly rational, and its good which is irrational. Good only becomes rational when everyone does it.<br /> But even then, if you can get away with it, it's rational to cheat the system so you benefit, at the cost of everyone else.<br /> <br /> A lot of evil in the world is caused by bad situations or irrational beliefs, but a lot of it isn't.<br /> Also, of course, a lot of bad things are justified by people to themselves by their bad situations, but aren't really justified. For example, most poor people don't steal. Some poor people do, and justify it by saying &quot;I need to steal, because I'm poor&quot;, but they're not stealing to keep themselves alive, they're just stealing to get more fashionable clothes, or whatever.<br /> You can apply that to religion too.<br /> Take ISIS: you'd assume its purely caused by religious fanaticism. I read an article about an Islamic fanatic who joined them. Shooting Shi'ites was fine by him. But he got uncomfortable when they wanted him to execute Sunni Muslims from his hometown. He eventually left when they offered him some teenage Yazidis as sex slaves, because, as he said &quot;Isis are not true Muslims, they just use it as an excuse.&quot; Obviously fundamentalism is part of it, but I suspect the &quot;five-star jihad&quot; and forced marriages are a big part of the draw for young ISIS fighters. Islam is how they justify it to themselves.<br /> <br /> I guess white-collar crime is the best example. All those rich bankers who steal millions from people's pensions, purely because they can.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":2402,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","user":"The Wizard of Oz","date":". 05-09-2015, 09:05 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-09T19:36:09-07:00","id":509440,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Erinys</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/507138-would-exigents-suffer-the-great-curse?p=508975#post508975\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The in-universe explanation is that Autochthon designed them with a mental defense against insanity-inducing Primordial magic. Before the Great Curse, limit was ony a thing inflicted by insanity-inducing magics, and when you hit limit break you just temporarily lost a dot of permanent Willpower.</div> </div> </div> </div>I know, but I just don't see the point. Personally, I'd make un-Cursed Exalts just flatly immune to Limit-inducing magic.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I feel that if the Great Curse is truly impossible to cure, then that sucks all the hope out of the setting. I know the default assumption is supposed to be that the world crumbles into shit and everyone dies, but I want the PCs to be able to avert that! </div> </div> </div>Oh, I entirely agree, but I don't see why the Limit track has to stick around once the Curse is gone.<br /> <br /> Yes, unCursed exalts would still have human flaws... as a baseline. But without the Curse, they might be able to get around that in other ways.<br /> <br /> OOC, the Great Curse (and Virtue mechanics) are there to push characters into being mythic heroes who are both great and terrible in their deeds, rather than acting like RL modern people.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5488-goldfaction","name":"goldfaction","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"90"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-09T19:42:50-07:00","id":509446,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zelbinnean</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/507138-would-exigents-suffer-the-great-curse?p=509253#post509253\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't see that as reasonable given that Exalts are still human beings with human personalities.</div> </div> </div> </div>But Exalted's setting is a world where a lot of aspects of reality which are not really accessible to us to change are to the Exalted. I see no reason why an un-Cursed Solar couldn't eventually, in sufficient meditation on human nature and good government, create an &quot;I take all my subjects' needs into account to the greatest degree possible without contradictions&quot; Charm.<br /> <br /> For that matter, they could probably remove whatever the setting's equivalent of original sin or the flaw in human nature is...<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5488-goldfaction","name":"goldfaction","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"90"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-09T20:00:04-07:00","id":509450,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>goldfaction</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/507138-would-exigents-suffer-the-great-curse?p=509440#post509440\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I know, but I just don't see the point. Personally, I'd make un-Cursed Exalts just flatly immune to Limit-inducing magic.</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;Congrats, all the magic that induces Limit as collateral to resisting it, like <i>all UMI in the 2e system</i>, you're now passively, perfectly immune to.&quot;<br /> <br /> This is totally broken to hell and back, if you can't see that I really don't know what to tell you.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>goldfaction</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/507138-would-exigents-suffer-the-great-curse?p=509446#post509446\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For that matter, they could probably remove whatever the setting's equivalent of original sin or the flaw in human nature is...</div> </div> </div> </div>You want to let Exalts excise their humanity and only gain benefits from it?<br /> <br /> For non-Alchemicals, no. Just no. No, they couldn't. Alchemicals kind of do this with Clarity, and there are clear and intentional drawbacks to it.<br /> <br /> The &quot;flaw&quot; in human nature is nothing less than the actual notion of &quot;what it means to be human&quot; itself.<br /> <br /> Making the Exalted inherently less human and more &quot;infallible&quot; or at the very least, with cheap <i>mechanical</i> access to being capital-G Good without any kind of draw is a toxic notion that has no place in the kind of setting that Creation is supposed to be, i.e. a realistic one with a basis in how human beings actually behave. Exalted is fundamentally a story about human beings and the nature of power. Once you start removing those bits, it is no simply longer Exalted.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-10T02:09:14-07:00","id":509740,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>goldfaction</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">I see no reason why an un-Cursed Solar couldn't eventually, in sufficient meditation on human nature and good government, create an &quot;I take all my subjects' needs into account to the greatest degree possible without contradictions&quot; Charm.</div> </div> </div> </div> Charms should be actual actions and processes, and not broad, passive alterations to personality. That specific one just seems kind of dull anyway; what do you actually do with the character afterwards? <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">There have been tons of Emperors and dictators who've done bad things to people because they could, because they had the power and they enjoyed it. Not all did, but plenty did.</div> </div> </div> </div> Such as? <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">I mean, if you're not punished for it by society, selfishness is rational. Altruism is irrational. Kindness is irrational. Love is irrational.</div> </div> </div> </div> What of the neurologically ingrained need for positive contact and cooperation with other people? Dammit, I need access to a better computer to make complex posts.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-10T03:10:50-07:00","id":509761,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Such as? </div> </div> </div>You... want me to list examples of rulers who did bad things when they weren't forced into it by circumstance? You have heard of harems, right? And torture?<br /> There have been tons of rulers who've conquered as much as they can for power and loot. Now, probably their motives weren't 100% immoral: maybe they wanted to give a present (of a big empire) to their kids, maybe they needed to keep going so they didn't get killed by their underlings. But most of the time, they did it because it benefited them.<br /> If you want a more specific example, how about Stalin?<br /> During his purges, he'd have people tortured, then have actors act out the point at which they broke for his amusement. During show trials, he'd often sit behind a curtain, giggling loudly while tortured men confessed to crimes they'd never committed.<br /> <br /> Now, many Emperors/Kings/Dictators were not actually happy with their lives, at the end, so maybe it wasn't such a good idea. Stalin was miserable because his wife killed herself (because she couldn't live with such a monster). But they certainly did it.<br /> <br /> Evil exists. People have choices. Yes, many bad things are done because of ignorance, because of desperation, or even because of love (hence nepotism). But frequently people do bad things just because they enjoy it.<br /> <br /> For a more obvious, but lower down example. Take rapists. Do they get money from this to feed their families? No. Do they do it because of ideology? Not generally. They just enjoy it, and don't care about the consequences to others.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> What of the neurologically ingrained need for positive contact and cooperation with other people? Dammit, I need access to a better computer to make complex posts. </div> </div> </div>Easy. Become Emperor, and everyone will be nice to you. You can even get a whole harem of girls (or boys if that's your thing) to love you. If they're not, kill them. Job done.<br /> Or maybe you're nice to your friends and family. They give you positive contact. But a bunch of people at the bottom of the country who don't like the taxes you levied to buy your favourite daughter a new palace? Just massacre them, that'll teach them.<br /> In fact, the &quot;neurologically ingrained need for positive contact and cooperation with other people&quot; sometimes causes evil. That's part of the reason Catholic priests aren't allowed to get married, and also the reason Chinese Emperors had eunuchs. People often do bad things because they put their families and friends before others.<br /> <br /> So, to get back to Exalted, I agree with Zelbinnean. Yes, there will be Exalted heroes. And there will be Exalted villains. Even if ignorance is wiped from the map, even if the Immaculate Order's lies about Solars are gone so the DBs can work with Solars, even if all Abyssals and Infernals were transformed into Solars, even if the Great Curse was gone, even if the world was rich and prosperous... the world would not be a perfect utopia. It would a lot be better than it is now, but not perfect. Because people will still be selfish. And people will still put those close to them before those far away.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-10T04:43:01-07:00","id":509781,"title":"","content":"I have thought for a while and still think if the Great Curse destines you to show totally different and new character traits, then I think it fails as players will feel that the Curse is just unfair and imposed, rather than a natural and tragic consequence of their character's personality.<br /> <br /> At the same time, if the Great Curse only draws out and exaggerates personality traits that are already within a person's potential, then defeating the Great Curse cannot be a total and patent protection against those traits being brought out again, and then dooming the character.<br /> <br /> I don't know if you can really unite those two horns. I'd take the second, of course.<br /> <br /> This isn't, I think, such a big deal with literary antecedents to the Great Curse - rather than a curse from the dark and ancient antediluvian titans, they're either from the gods themselves as in Greek Tragedy (I think) or like the Dark Side of the Force, in both cases natural parts of the world which are viewed as partially symbolic or not clearly separable from human psychology and spirituality in the worlds those mythologies construct.<br /> <br /> I also do think with Limit Break, seeing the Limit Break as an abstract representation of the character's decisions is a better understanding than thinking and instead as an alien force that takes over and mind controls the character.<br /> <br /> Now on the other subject which came up with Jaytee's post earlier on whether people only do things which are bad because they face bad circumstances or due to irrational beliefs that can themselves be dispensed with without that act of dispensing being more dehumanising and harmful than having the belief in the first place, well.... I'm not going to dismiss that as a view (ultimately, you have to look at the evidence yourself).... but...<br /> <br /> I do think that Exalted is a setting that embraces the idea that personal and large scale tragedy can and will arise from unintended consequences of positive human qualities, like love, ambition, loyalty to family and so on.<br /> <br /> I also think it questions whether people would actually want to live in a perfectly peaceful society which has no suffering or tragedy or danger ever, because it lacks the emotional challenges which lead to suffering and tragedy and danger. (Currently it's fashionable to see no contrast between freedom and challenges in life and a more &quot;progressive&quot; problem free and worry free world, but I do think this is an overreaction to the excesses of certain kinds of Libertarian ideologues and there is a real conflict on a level.)<br /> <br /> Or perhaps that's just the vibe from what I get from Grabowski's quotes on the game plus personal projection (and personal pretentions)!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-10T04:43:52-07:00","id":509782,"title":"","content":"Also, I'd like Exigents to have the Great Curse, if everyone else does. But perhaps it varies as a function of their power, as does the Great Curse on the Exalted we know.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-10T05:29:00-07:00","id":509808,"title":"","content":"I think the issue with limit breaks and the Great Curse, is Grabowski intended them to be &quot;natural parts of the world which are viewed as partially symbolic or not clearly separable from human psychology and spirituality in the worlds those mythologies construct.&quot; He just made it a curse because then no one would argue with his view of the natural excesses of tragic, classical heroes.<br /> A curse implies that it can be &quot;cured&quot;, but reading what Grabowski has written about it (which was a while ago), I didn't get the impression that the point of the Great Curse was to be cured, that was just something that came along later. It's point was to make sure people played Solars as he envisioned them.<br /> <br /> Personally, I don't think I'd like to run a game about curing the Great Curse. Limit breaks are just too much fun.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-10T05:33:31-07:00","id":509809,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Myself, in response to Isator</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">You... want me to list examples of rulers who did bad things when they weren't forced into it by circumstance? You have heard of harems, right? And torture?</div> </div> </div> </div>I realise my tone comes off as a bit rude here.<br /> I was just dumbfounded to see Americans espousing Marxist morality. Normally I only hear Liberal, Conservative, or Christian views of morality from Americans. It threw me for a second. Perhaps I'm just racist, and need to check my assumptions (plus, I'm just assuming JayTee is American, because I assume most people here are). Assumptions make an ass out of me and you, as they say.<br /> So I apologise.<br /> <br /> And the irony of course, is I myself am a Socialist, and would generally say that the root cause of most social issues is poverty, racism, etc, and so the government should tackle these issues rather than just focusing on punishing the criminals. Yet hear I am, arguing against it! I guess, essentially, I admit that much of the evil in the world is caused by this.<br /> But not all of it. Some is just a choice.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":2402,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","user":"The Wizard of Oz","date":". 05-10-2015, 08:36 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-10T06:36:40-07:00","id":509825,"title":"","content":"Grabowski envisioned an amazingly awesome game but he also envisioned it being inherently doomed to apocalypse. That's one part of his vision I don't like.<br /> <br /> One of the issues is that, at least with Solars and Sidereals, there are two facets of the Curse. One is the limit breaking, which simulates the periodic freak-outs of classical Greek heroes and becomes absurdly dangerous when said heroes are armed with Solar Circle Sorcery and artifact megaweapons.<br /> <br /> The other facet is nebulous but more dangerous: &quot;Become gradually more tyrannical, selfish, arbitrary, and dangerous&quot; and &quot;Become gradually more hubristic, arrogant, and incapable of compromise or learning from mistakes&quot; and &quot;Be doomed to making the worst decisions at the most critical times, dooming your world.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">She/Her. I am literal-minded and write literally. If I don't say something explicitly, please never assume I implied it. The only exception is if I try to make a joke.</span></span></span></div> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">My point of view may be different from yours but is equally valid.</span></span></span><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1x1ycoxJF0G9niMt5D3Pp7owZ7tw8AJvL?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted-cWoD-ArM url mega-library</a>. Exalted <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/663334-random-name-generator\" target=\"_blank\">name-generators</a>.","edited":{"userid":896,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","user":"Erinys","date":". 05-10-2015, 09:43 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","name":"Erinys","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar896_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4235"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-10T06:48:10-07:00","id":509832,"title":"","content":"Yeah, the actual mechanics never simulated that second part in any way.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-10T06:52:35-07:00","id":509834,"title":"","content":"It's also that the limit breaks are a Big Problem, but don't have to necessarily doom the world. The second part is, IIRC explicitly on a meta-level, all about dooming the world.<br /> <br /> Exalted is full of tragedy, and individual stories can be tragedies easily enough. The entire setting has world-scale tragedies aplenty, and existential tragedies that ask tough moral questions. That's an important part of the setting.<br /> <br /> But I'm not happy with the idea that the world, as a whole, is doomed to end in nothing but tragedy and Darkness.<br /> <br /> <br /> Regarding the original question that started this thread: In past editions, Alchemicals have not been Cursed. Although they were designed and blueprinted before the Primordial War, they were not built until after it. As a result the Great Curse never struck them. This suggests that the Great Curse struck each host (type) of Exalted, not Exaltation as a cosmic principle. If this holds in 3e, then any type of Exalted created after the War ended would presumably not be Cursed. I think Liminals were first created after the Usurpation, but don't know about the others.<br /> <br /> They're still likely to have personality mechanics of some kind, because that is a White Wolf thing. For example, I wouldn't be surprised to see Liminals have a mechanic named Humanity, or to have something similar to whatever Prometheans have in nWoD which I've never read about and wouldn't recognize.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">She/Her. I am literal-minded and write literally. If I don't say something explicitly, please never assume I implied it. The only exception is if I try to make a joke.</span></span></span></div> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">My point of view may be different from yours but is equally valid.</span></span></span><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1x1ycoxJF0G9niMt5D3Pp7owZ7tw8AJvL?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted-cWoD-ArM url mega-library</a>. Exalted <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/663334-random-name-generator\" target=\"_blank\">name-generators</a>.","edited":{"userid":896,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","user":"Erinys","date":". 05-10-2015, 09:58 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","name":"Erinys","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar896_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4235"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-10T16:41:40-07:00","id":510236,"title":"","content":"That would seem likely. Exigents too might not have the Great Curse, but something equivalent instead.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-10T16:43:29-07:00","id":510237,"title":"","content":"Has it been said whether Exigents were created during or after the War?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">She/Her. I am literal-minded and write literally. If I don't say something explicitly, please never assume I implied it. The only exception is if I try to make a joke.</span></span></span></div> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">My point of view may be different from yours but is equally valid.</span></span></span><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1x1ycoxJF0G9niMt5D3Pp7owZ7tw8AJvL?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted-cWoD-ArM url mega-library</a>. Exalted <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/663334-random-name-generator\" target=\"_blank\">name-generators</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","name":"Erinys","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar896_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4235"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-10T16:48:54-07:00","id":510241,"title":"","content":"The Great Curse kind of sucks.<br /> <br /> In fact, it totally sucks. The Great Curse is fucking awful and I wish to heaven it was dropped and never picked up again because it sucks that bad.<br /> <br /> But if the Solars have to deal with it then the Exigents do too, I guess.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/117-solar","name":"Solar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar117_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1267"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-10T16:56:59-07:00","id":510243,"title":"","content":"I think one of the reasons the limit breaks don't feel like something that the character is personally responsible for, is the way the mechanics work (at least in 1e and 2e). Your limit fills up, and then the Curse just forces you to do something. It doesn't feel like giving in to a temptation, or like a gradual erosion of the character's previous morality or behavior. It doesn't feel at all voluntary.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">She/Her. I am literal-minded and write literally. If I don't say something explicitly, please never assume I implied it. The only exception is if I try to make a joke.</span></span></span></div> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">My point of view may be different from yours but is equally valid.</span></span></span><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1x1ycoxJF0G9niMt5D3Pp7owZ7tw8AJvL?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted-cWoD-ArM url mega-library</a>. Exalted <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/663334-random-name-generator\" target=\"_blank\">name-generators</a>.","edited":{"userid":896,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","user":"Erinys","date":". 05-10-2015, 08:14 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","name":"Erinys","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar896_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4235"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-10T17:03:16-07:00","id":510249,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Erinys</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/507138-would-exigents-suffer-the-great-curse?p=510243#post510243\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think one of the reasons the limit breaks don't feel like something that the character is personally responsible for, is the way the mechanics in (at least in 1e and 2e). Your limit fills up, and then the Curse just forces you to do something. It doesn't feel like giving in to a temptation, or like a gradual erosion of the character's previous morality or behavior. It doesn't feel at all voluntary.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well that's because it isn't, and never has been. The Great Curse drives your character mad whether you like it or not. It barges into whatever story you are telling and yells RUN TRAGICHUBRIS.EXE and you just kind of have to get over it, because it will keep happening (you can't cure it or even really manage it, your character doesn't even know it exists), all in the name of forcing your character to clumsily take part in some not entirely welcome genre assumptions.<br /> <br /> As someone who is bi-polar I resent the forced intrusion of some manic depression into my character's life quite fervently. If I wanted to roleplay someone who randomly felt extreme emotions and was unable to really restrict them, and who later felt stupid or ashamed about what they'd said/done without knowing why they did it, I'd sit back and recall some memories of being a teenager.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/117-solar","name":"Solar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar117_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1267"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-10T17:24:16-07:00","id":510261,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Erinys</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/507138-would-exigents-suffer-the-great-curse?p=509834#post509834\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But I'm not happy with the idea that the world, as a whole, is doomed to end in nothing but tragedy and Darkness.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think this is the always-inevitable outcome of the Great Curse tho.<br /> <br /> But this is definitely the problem with a Setting Plot Point having both specifically-defined mechanical effects and very undefined narrative effects, with seemingly no connection between the two.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-10T17:59:38-07:00","id":510273,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Solar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/507138-would-exigents-suffer-the-great-curse?p=510241#post510241\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Great Curse kind of sucks.<br /> <br /> In fact, it totally sucks. The Great Curse is fucking awful and I wish to heaven it was dropped and never picked up again because it sucks that bad.<br /> <br /> But if the Solars have to deal with it then the Exigents do too, I guess.</div> </div> </div> </div>I hate the great curse as a gameplay mechanic, because it takes control of the character away from the player (a cardinal sin, IMO)<br /> <br /> I like the great curse as a narrative plot point, because it gives the Solars a chance for redemption, the Exalted host the ability to move past the abuses of the First Age, and it opens up the possibility for the Exalted Host to enter a new golden era.<br /> <br /> Assuming it's cured.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2034-jaytee","name":"JayTee","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2034_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1805"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-10T21:03:46-07:00","id":510427,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JayTee</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/507138-would-exigents-suffer-the-great-curse?p=510273#post510273\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I hate the great curse as a gameplay mechanic, because it takes control of the character away from the player (a cardinal sin, IMO)<br /> <br /> I like the great curse as a narrative plot point, because it gives the Solars a chance for redemption, the Exalted host the ability to move past the abuses of the First Age, and it opens up the possibility for the Exalted Host to enter a new golden era.<br /> <br /> Assuming it's cured.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is a really useful format for framing opinions on the subject.<br /> <br /> I hate the great curse as a gameplay mechanic, because it commits the cardinal sin of removing a player's control over their character.<br /> <br /> I hate the great curse as a narrative plot point because it's used as an excuse to ignore the fact that the First Age was organized on political principles we know to be shitty and easily improved upon and shuts out the possibility of actually using those improvements in game.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I\u00e4! I\u00e4! Moe fthagn!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/280-valles","name":"Valles","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar280_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"677"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-10T21:05:45-07:00","id":510430,"title":"","content":"Meritocracy is a shitty political principal?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2034-jaytee","name":"JayTee","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2034_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1805"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-10T21:21:13-07:00","id":510436,"title":"","content":"The Solar Deliberative is not meritocracy. Meritocracy would be if people who demonstrated the ability to rule well were put in positions of rulership. The Deliberative is described as one where if you are a Solar, and you can be a Solar <i>for having no skills except being really good at making pastries</i>, you are now one of the guys in charge no questions asked.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/598-couch","name":"Couch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar598_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"330"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-10T21:33:49-07:00","id":510439,"title":"","content":"And are surrounded by people who have no legal recourse except your mercy, with literal license to do as you please. And can expect to be actively <i>worshiped as a deity</i>.<br /> <br /> The Deliberative is a loose structure for holding together umpty-hundred little kingdoms that form the actual social and political texture of the age, none of which is anything <i>like</i> a meritocracy.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I\u00e4! I\u00e4! Moe fthagn!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/280-valles","name":"Valles","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar280_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"677"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-10T21:38:31-07:00","id":510444,"title":"","content":"I'm going to ignore the level of unwarranted hostility in those posts, alongside the clear hateboner that seems to be going around for Solars, and just say that I'm glad that the First Age is going to be pushed back in to obscurity for 3e.<br /> <br /> Beyond that, I don't feel I have anything of value to contribute to this line of conversation that would be productive.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2034-jaytee","name":"JayTee","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2034_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1805"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-11T00:54:51-07:00","id":510499,"title":"","content":"To the degree that the Unconquered Sun, who was the ruler of Heaven, decides who merits Exaltation, and he knew during the First Age that the people he Exalted were also going to rule Creation, then one could argue the First Age was a meritocracy of sorts where one's merit was determined by the Unconquered Sun. After all, if you did not merit ruling Creation then the Unconquered Sun would never have Chosen you to rule Creation.<br /> <br /> At least that's the sort of argument I imagine would have been made by the Solars during the First Age and it wouldn't strike me as entirely wrong, especially in a 3rd edition setting where the Unconquered Sun takes a more active hand in Exalting people.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Valles</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/507138-would-exigents-suffer-the-great-curse?p=510439#post510439\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And are surrounded by people who have no legal recourse except your mercy, with literal license to do as you please. And can expect to be actively <i>worshiped as a deity</i>.</div> </div> </div> </div>To be fair, in Dreams of the First Age it said that Cults to the Celestial Exalted were against the law and Exalted who created them (including Solars) could face punishment and severe sanctions. So while a Solar might be worshiped as a deity, that would be rather unusual and highly illegal.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-11T04:08:37-07:00","id":510528,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/507138-would-exigents-suffer-the-great-curse?p=510499#post510499\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To the degree that the Unconquered Sun, who was the ruler of Heaven, decides who merits Exaltation, and he knew during the First Age that the people he Exalted were also going to rule Creation, then one could argue the First Age was a meritocracy of sorts where one's merit was determined by the Unconquered Sun. After all, if you did not merit ruling Creation then the Unconquered Sun would never have Chosen you to rule Creation.<br /> <br /> At least that's the sort of argument I imagine would have been made by the Solars during the First Age and it wouldn't strike me as entirely wrong, especially in a 3rd edition setting where the Unconquered Sun takes a more active hand in Exalting people.</div> </div> </div> </div>Meriting power in no way makes one a good person. <br /> <br /> I don't like the SunJesus portrayal insofar as it creates the implication that UCS would only Exalt capital-G Good people. During the Primordial War I imagine that people who would get the job done were Chosen, people for whom the ends could easily justify the means, which could and did involve genocide of people and species who were loyal to the Primordials. <br /> <br /> The Unconquered Sun's favor isn't a good bellweather for anything other than &quot;this person is, on some level, willing to wield terrible cosmic power.&quot;<br /> <br /> Frankly I don't think UCS scared about the quality of people who would ultimately ruled Creation. He wanted his rebellion to win. He wanted the Primordials overthrown and himself as King of Heaven. The excesses of the Exalted ultimately grew to a point where they lost his favor but it's not as if he could ever suppress the human nature of his Chosen.<br /> <br /> I don't consider the system that UCS implicitly created by empowering the greatest Exalted to be meritocracy insofar as you don't earn Exaltation based on any objective standard of merit, and can't guaranteed receiving it even if you meet some specific qualifications. It's not like mandatory statutory promotions every 12 months or anything mechanically applied like that. <br /> <br /> Being Chosen by UCS in no way implies you were Chosen because you &quot;deserve&quot; or &quot;merit&quot; rule of Creation. The Solars created the Deliberative and, at least in 2e, basically enforced its hegemony by the sword. <br /> <br /> I like what you said as an in-setting justification but not as some objective OOC statement.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-11T04:58:30-07:00","id":510551,"title":"","content":"The problem, is that if the UCS chooses exaltations, he could change who he chose. In the War, he might choose those who do whatever it takes, and then in the High First Age, choose people who are righteous and compassionate.<br /> <br /> Also, I wonder: how much does the UCS know when he's choosing people? It's not like he's omnipotent. How much does he know about then when he grants them Exaltation?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-11T05:15:10-07:00","id":510556,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/507138-would-exigents-suffer-the-great-curse?p=510551#post510551\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The problem, is that if the UCS chooses exaltations, he could change who he chose.</div> </div> </div> </div>That doesn't follow, not necessarily. If I ask you to pick a brand of chili to go in the Frito pie, you can't go and give me a jar of Alfredo sauce.<br /> <br /> Also, &quot;righteous&quot; and &quot;compassionate&quot; leaders can still make choices that damn their society, can still be mired in corruption, can still lose sight of the little people in the process of being made big. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Also, I wonder: how much does the UCS know when he's choosing people? It's not like he's omnipotent. How much does he know about then when he grants them Exaltation? </div> </div> </div>How much do you know when you fall in love?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-11T05:17:00-07:00","id":510557,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/507138-would-exigents-suffer-the-great-curse?p=510551#post510551\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The problem, is that if the UCS chooses exaltations, he could change who he chose. In the War, he might choose those who do whatever it takes, and then in the High First Age, choose people who are righteous and compassionate.<br /> <br /> Also, I wonder: how much does the UCS know when he's choosing people? It's not like he's omnipotent. How much does he know about then when he grants them Exaltation?</div> </div> </div> </div>Well we know that when he Chose Perfect Soul, it was when she smashed an alter to him and he felt a deep connection with her feelings of impotence and frustration, which resulted in him Choosing her. <br /> <br /> I understand the gods Choose but I'm hoping it's not as conscious as the word &quot;choice&quot; implies, otherwise a generally-virtuous god probably wouldn't choose assholes and that is not something I want given up; Solars as Paladins hold no interest for me. That said, Volfer, Novia, and Shen hardly sound like LG Paladins to me. <br /> <br /> Your point about lack of omnipotence is good and actually is a thing that should be brought up more. Lyta is a driven person who fights the odds and thus attracts attention but the UCS can only guess how she'll use her power. For every Karal Fire Orchid there's an Ophilis Ses, but Creation needs the former just as much as the latter. <br /> <br /> However I have always liked Exaltation as an amoral power that cares only about being wielded, unconcerned for reasons of why it's wielded or toward what ends. <br /> <br /> I think part of this might be UCS accepting that the kinds of people who are willing to wield ultimate power are the kinds of people who will, at times, use that power for non-virtuous ends and maybe he trusts that with time, they will use it only responsibly. <br /> <br /> But again he can't change human nature. Even an enlightened Jain sage who cares about all living things might be pushed into terrible excesses for the sake of all living things, when given the power to change the world.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-11T05:17:03-07:00","id":510558,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JayTee</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/507138-would-exigents-suffer-the-great-curse?p=510273#post510273\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I hate the great curse as a gameplay mechanic, because it takes control of the character away from the player (a cardinal sin, IMO)</div> </div> </div> </div>Part of the problem, imo, is that if the point of the mechanic is to get Players to roleplay the tragic hubris of their characters, then Limit should be something the Players <i>want</i> to play.<br /> As it stands, it's built more like a punishment than an opportunity.<br /> <br /> Something that the player controls (but the character doesn't) along the lines of &quot;You can spend one wp to bolster an intimacy for a time, your character is overcome and overwhelmed by it, gaining [bonus dice?] to actions that support it and ignoring everything else&quot; already seems that it would serve that purpose a lot better, and it could emulate existing Limit Breaks rather easily (being overcome with Honor = Foolhardy Contempt; being overcome with Hatred for the Realm = Berserk Anger; Overcome with Love for Living Things = Compassionate Martyrdom or Heart of Tears, etc.)<br /> <br /> (It's clearly not a perfect solution, just an example off the top of my head to get discussion going)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:lucida sans unicode\">Bearer of the legacy of Trauma Bear<br /> Need a dice-roller? Check out <a href=\"http://bit.ly/dicemat\" target=\"_blank\">Dicemat</a>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/43-fata-ku","name":"Fata-Ku","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar43_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2240"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-11T08:17:26-07:00","id":510690,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/507138-would-exigents-suffer-the-great-curse?p=510551#post510551\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Also, I wonder: how much does the UCS know when he's choosing people? It's not like he's omnipotent. How much does he know about then when he grants them Exaltation?</div> </div> </div> </div>I've had this idea before... I can't quite remember the precise way I articulated it when it first came to me, but it was something like the Unconquered Sun possessing a depth of senses and breadth of mind that is capable of encompassing your entire life story and a whole heap of details of your inner life with a single glance, but that doesn't necessarily mean he understands you or can't be surprised by you.<br /> <br /> I think it came to me when I was considering points such as, unless a historical personage left behind a diary or autobiography (and even then, sometimes) we can only ever really speculate on their motivations and the reasoning behind their actions. When studying history, we're looking for context more than we are answers; we can never really tell why Gaius Julius Caesar gathered all of the power he did or was so lenient with his enemies or any of the rest, even if we can factually establish the environment and background in which he did those things.<br /> <br /> And also when I was thinking of the idea that many or most or all of us contain a rich inner life of imagination and reflections and responses and motives that constantly underlies us as people but is probably never really seen even by our closest loved ones and that we couldn't really tell even if we had the words to convey it because it's just too big.<br /> <br /> So from there I have this idea that a god like the Sun could know those things, could see the total of what you are and... perhaps &quot;assess&quot; is better a word than &quot;judge&quot;, and he makes decisions based off of that*.<br /> <br /> But still with this idea that he doesn't necessarily understand <i>why</i> you have these desires or qualities (not as a matter of him being distant or alien, just being enough of a person to be unable to fully integrate the personality of somebody else). So he could look at somebody like Caesar and get <i>what</i> his motivation or inclination is, but not personally understand why that should matter to him.<br /> <br /> But it's still in terms of him being able to see something worthy and grand in you, and wanting to see what you'll make of the power to chase it (even if he can be surprised and even unnerved or angered by the result, although I would say provoking the latter would be more difficult than in a human).<br /> <br /> That and the idea that there may be certain consequences he is less concerned about; I would say that the Unconquered Sun wouldn't really Choose a Hernan Cortes who was deliberately setting out to enslave and brutalise hundreds of thousands of people, but he would Choose one who was going on an adventure to Mexico to raid for treasure and stand astride a great civilization and pursue the riches of the land, even if that will logically and perhaps inevitably have consequences leading to the enslavement and brutalisation of hundreds of thousands of people (not because that was the point or that the people doing it are terrible, but because there's a complex chain of circumstances in which personal debts + untapped minerals + large numbers of readily exploited people is an equation that seems to solve itself).<br /> <br /> I wouldn't say that the Unconquered Sun is indifferent so much as... that's not necessarily looking far beyond you (although there will be a bit of assessment when the widespread enslavement ultimately comes around, even if he might still be taking a kind of big picture perspective on it).<br /> <br /> As for how he can know who to look at without being omniscient... I'd say it's a bit like Makarios finding people who'll trade with him without needing to randomly cycle through everybody in the world. It's just something kind of essential to the world and the god; his gaze naturally and unconsciously falling upon the things and the people that warrant it, because those are just how certain things are connected and intersect on an intrinsic and ineffable level. It's like... when you're the god of certain acts and personalities of heroism, you can be incarnate in those places because for a being of Essence things that are categorical can relate to you and your senses the way light and matter interact with a normal human.<br /> <br /> * I've also got this idea that even in the Bureau of Destiny, these things aren't really part of your thread or the general records of your life, or at least not all of them are, and although there are gods like Jupiter who might know them if they should look by and large they disappear from the world when you die, except for some impressions they leave on your next life.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-11T08:20:23-07:00","id":510692,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Valles</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/507138-would-exigents-suffer-the-great-curse?p=510427#post510427\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I hate the great curse as a narrative plot point because it's used as an excuse to ignore the fact that the First Age was organized on political principles we know to be shitty and easily improved upon and shuts out the possibility of actually using those improvements in game.</div> </div> </div> </div>Removing the Curse would only remove the <b>guaranteed, unavoidable failure</b> and destruction of Creation and humanity. The characters would still be left to grapple with human nature and its combination with Exaltation. A better world would be possible, not guaranteed. Who is saying otherwise?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">She/Her. I am literal-minded and write literally. If I don't say something explicitly, please never assume I implied it. The only exception is if I try to make a joke.</span></span></span></div> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">My point of view may be different from yours but is equally valid.</span></span></span><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1x1ycoxJF0G9niMt5D3Pp7owZ7tw8AJvL?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted-cWoD-ArM url mega-library</a>. Exalted <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/663334-random-name-generator\" target=\"_blank\">name-generators</a>.","edited":{"userid":896,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","user":"Erinys","date":". 05-11-2015, 11:32 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","name":"Erinys","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar896_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4235"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-11T08:55:54-07:00","id":510746,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Valles</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/507138-would-exigents-suffer-the-great-curse?p=510427#post510427\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I hate the great curse as a narrative plot point because it's used as an excuse to ignore the fact that the First Age was organized on political principles we know to be shitty and easily improved upon</div> </div> </div> </div>We should not know so much.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Erinys</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Removing the Curse would only remove the </span></span></span><b>guaranteed, unavoidable failure</b><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\"> and destruction of Creation and humanity.</span></span></span></div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\"><br /> <br /> I like the Great Curse, but I don't really see the case for it portraying an inevitable doom for the Exalted.<br /> <br /> Articulating as reason as to why is not helped by the shortcomings of the prior mechanics to it, so I'll have to reserve assessments for when the new rules are out.</span></span></span><br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-11T09:22:21-07:00","id":510765,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Erinys</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/507138-would-exigents-suffer-the-great-curse?p=510692#post510692\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Removing the Curse would only remove the <b>guaranteed, unavoidable failure</b> and destruction of Creation and humanity.</div> </div> </div> </div>Still disagree that guaranteed and unavoidable failure is an actual Thing due to the Curse. To the degree it has been presented as such in the books, that stuff is actively toxic. There are plenty of ways to get a Good End without even diagnosing the Curse. <br /> <br /> There are a plethora of reasons for the Usurpation that don't have to point back at the curse. Using some 2e setting points, I don't see things like Wyldhand, which is called out as one of the great Deliverative excesses, as being something even curse-driven. IRL we certainly did the same kinds of things with Pacific atomic testing for decades. It's not unreasonable to expect that the Exalted would perform the same kinds of weapon testing with their innovations. I think that's a strongly implied parallel at the least. Similarly with notions like eugenics and performing experiments on living people. Humans are fully capable of that without being prompted by an outside supernatural force upon them. <br /> <br /> And if Grawbowski intended it to be a hopeless setting because Great Curse, well, he's just wrong that it should be that. <br /> <br /> Human drama and humans being corrupted by being able to wield power is about a million times more interesting than &quot;hurr burr we could all get along if not for that mean old curse!&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":3420,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","user":"Zelbinnean","date":". 05-11-2015, 12:24 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-11T09:29:54-07:00","id":510780,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zelbinnean</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/507138-would-exigents-suffer-the-great-curse?p=510765#post510765\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To the degree it has been presented as such in the books, that stuff is actively toxic.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hence why I dislike it. Same reason I dislike the &quot;thousand dooms.&quot;<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zelbinnean</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/507138-would-exigents-suffer-the-great-curse?p=510765#post510765\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Human drama and humans being corrupted by being able to wield power is about a million times more interesting than &quot;hurr burr we could all get along if not for that mean old curse!&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Again with this non-argument. I already addressed this. Nobody is saying any of that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">She/Her. I am literal-minded and write literally. If I don't say something explicitly, please never assume I implied it. The only exception is if I try to make a joke.</span></span></span></div> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">My point of view may be different from yours but is equally valid.</span></span></span><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1x1ycoxJF0G9niMt5D3Pp7owZ7tw8AJvL?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted-cWoD-ArM url mega-library</a>. Exalted <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/663334-random-name-generator\" target=\"_blank\">name-generators</a>.","edited":{"userid":896,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","user":"Erinys","date":". 05-11-2015, 12:34 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","name":"Erinys","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar896_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4235"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-11T12:56:03-07:00","id":511060,"title":"","content":"Re: Solar, upthread, I'm not unsympathetic, but if the Great Curse includes unwelcome genre assumptions for your group and game then you... take it out.<br /> <br /> As a whole I have not seen any evidence it presents unwelcome genre assumptions for the community of Exalted as a whole.<br /> <br /> (Although a lot of members of the community were introduced to Exalted via conceptions that ignored it being a game about mighty, cursed heroes in the first place, as is on I think literally the first page of the first book written about the game.)<br /> <br /> Re: if meritocracy is a &quot;shitty principle&quot; (JayTee, maybe, if you're still reading), mainly because it interests me.<br /> <br /> Talent in government certainly isn't a *bad* principle.<br /> <br /> At the same time, personal merit, is, I think a lot less important than the combination of<br /> <br /> - Accountability<br /> - Interpersonal relationships : People working well together as a group, even if their individual merit is low<br /> - Replaceability : If your system is dependent on the skill of the meritorious, what happens when your merititious candidate dies unexpectedly or decides to hold the system to ransom, because he holds all the cards?<br /> - The Rule of Law rather than the whims of the powerful<br /> - Predictability in government (to allow people to make plans) : Are the most talented always the most predictable in their action? Predictable actions allow others than the ruler to make plans, and create a stable society independent of the government. <br /> - Continuity of government : Sometimes it's better to be mediocre in terms of raw talent and have lots of experience and contacts to fall back on than just being a great raw talent and not having anything else much going for you<br /> - The consent of the governed<br /> <br /> Meritocracy isn't necessarily in conflict with all of these, but you can't just dismiss them in favour of merit.<br /> <br /> There are also issues of inherent (though not always unsurmountable) challenge particular to meritocracy like:<br /> <br /> - Destructive competition among the talented: If you give everything to the best, disaffected second bests often end up feeling frozen out of the process and so becoming disruptive. Big problem for your society, especially when they outnumber the best and work together.<br /> <br /> There's also a potential for a process of stakes raising possible among would be elites, who are motivated to try to and increase their merit to gain power, even when it isn't actually ultimately productive in improving performance in government. Especially their merit &quot;on paper&quot;.<br /> <br /> Finally, you can also add to that that in a meritocracy, those who gain power through merit are encouraged to kick away the ladder, so their position isn't threatened. Or knobble potential competitors. On an individual level if you're the king because merit, you don't have an incentive for any underling to have more merit than you, because then you're not the king. Whereas if you're just the king just because you probably don't care if some other dude is the Greatest Knight on Life (and if fact, if he is, you just got a useful resource to call on).<br /> <br /> - Defining merit : This has at least threefold issues <br /> <br /> a) in the procedures for defining merit risk rewarding known quantitites which can easily and be conventionally measured as merit than unknown quantities or qualities which are hard to measure, while fuzzier measures of merit risk criticism and morale problems from a lack of transparency and fairness and at the same time <br /> b) in a system where those with merit get power, people have strong incentives to try and shift the frame of merit to mean &quot;Whatever I personally am good at&quot;.<br /> c) When defining merit, you may wish to choose the reliably talented over the erratically brilliant. This tradeoff is a challenge itself to define.<br /> <br /> - Diversity of experience : The best may only really have experience of being the best; they may not know what its like to lose, to be downtrodden, to be unspectacular, to come from a place and time that doesn't allow you to develop the skills to be the best, amongst other things. That's all got some tradeoff value against talent.<br /> <br /> And there are probably more potential problems and other important principles that may conflict than I've listed.<br /> <br /> Re: whether Grabowski intended the game to be a hopeless setting, I think (perhaps as part of the Grabowski cult) he intended it personally to be stirringly tragic, and generally wasn't big on the secret truths of the setting over personal taste and whatever you feel like doing with it. Really. The following are his over ten year old opinions expressed on a forum (as evidence goes it's what we have <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> ):<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://exalted.xi.co.nz/wiki/Thus_Spake_Zargrabowski/ConditionOfCreation\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://exalted.xi.co.nz/wiki/Thus_Spake_Zargrabowski/ConditionOfCreation\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://exalted.xi.co.nz/wiki/Thus_Spake_Zargrabowski/ConditionOfCreation\" target=\"_blank\"> http://exalted.xi.co.nz/wiki/Thus_Spake_Zargrabowski/ConditionOfCreation </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://exalted.xi.co.nz/wiki/Thus_Spake_Zargrabowski/SanctityOfGameWorld\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://exalted.xi.co.nz/wiki/Thus_Spake_Zargrabowski/SanctityOfGameWorld\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://exalted.xi.co.nz/wiki/Thus_Spake_Zargrabowski/SanctityOfGameWorld\" target=\"_blank\"> http://exalted.xi.co.nz/wiki/Thus_Spake_Zargrabowski/SanctityOfGameWorld </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-11T14:36:21-07:00","id":511131,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Fata-Ku</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/507138-would-exigents-suffer-the-great-curse?p=510558#post510558\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Part of the problem, imo, is that if the point of the mechanic is to get Players to roleplay the tragic hubris of their characters, then Limit should be something the Players <i>want</i> to play.<br /> As it stands, it's built more like a punishment than an opportunity.<br /> <br /> Something that the player controls (but the character doesn't) along the lines of &quot;You can spend one wp to bolster an intimacy for a time, your character is overcome and overwhelmed by it, gaining [bonus dice?] to actions that support it and ignoring everything else&quot; already seems that it would serve that purpose a lot better, and it could emulate existing Limit Breaks rather easily (being overcome with Honor = Foolhardy Contempt; being overcome with Hatred for the Realm = Berserk Anger; Overcome with Love for Living Things = Compassionate Martyrdom or Heart of Tears, etc.)<br /> <br /> (It's clearly not a perfect solution, just an example off the top of my head to get discussion going)</div> </div> </div> </div>Thought about this during my classes, and have come to the conclusion that the buildup nature of current Limit does have redeeming qualities, it's more the what than the how that was poorly executed. So I've been pondering a more interesting solution:<br /> <br /> (yes, I realize that I'm essentially talking to myself.)<br /> <br /> Still working off the spend-a-wp-to-gain-benny mechanic that related to virtues: roll [dice representative of intimacy] separately. Successes add directly to the roll as well as the Limit track. If Limit track is filled by this, double the bonus for that action and regain that many (meaning Intimacy successes x 2) willpower points; The Intimacy overcomes the character for [essence] scenes and all actions supporting it enjoy the rolled bonus as extra dice. All actions that don't receive an equivalent penalty.<br /> (Not sure about the second part though. Might be a bit convoluted, having the same result count as successes in one situation and dice in others... but is essentially IAM otherwise)<br /> <br /> The point is to have something that is representative of the Great Curse, <i>and</i> that players find awesome and rewarding to use, adjusting reward level to reflect the desired frequency of use. (too good of a reward and Solars are all obsessed psychopaths, too little and the Great Curse is basically non-existant. Coming from Mage, I like seeing my players devolve unintentionally into nightmarish caricatures of human nature and see in awed and horrified hindsight what they have truly accomplished and become. So I prefer the former.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:lucida sans unicode\">Bearer of the legacy of Trauma Bear<br /> Need a dice-roller? Check out <a href=\"http://bit.ly/dicemat\" target=\"_blank\">Dicemat</a>.</span>","edited":{"userid":43,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/43-fata-ku","user":"Fata-Ku","date":". 05-11-2015, 05:38 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/43-fata-ku","name":"Fata-Ku","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar43_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2240"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-11T14:50:19-07:00","id":511173,"title":"","content":"Ghosthead, your thoughts on meritocracy were a very interesting read, so I want to say thanks for that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2034-jaytee","name":"JayTee","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2034_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1805"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-11T15:46:00-07:00","id":511256,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/507138-would-exigents-suffer-the-great-curse?p=510746#post510746\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">We should not know so much.</div> </div> </div> </div>On the contrary, I find it an implicit statement in even the most basic discussion of the 'Solar Concept' - IE, the initial starting statements about the Solar Exalted and the current age tells us that they were...<br /> <br /> 1. Unquestionably in charge<br /> 2. Often worshiped, such that shadows of it are visible centuries later in the current era<br /> 3. Often feared, such that the imprint of that terror is stamped deeply into the fabric of the societies 'closest' to that era<br /> <br /> We also know that Exalted is a setting that draws on ancient and classical history, periods where 'absolute autocrat with divine imprimatur' was the default political system. Attempting to assume that the Solars of the First Age were anything else is, I think... silly.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I\u00e4! I\u00e4! Moe fthagn!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/280-valles","name":"Valles","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar280_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"677"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-11T16:04:28-07:00","id":511276,"title":"","content":"All too much.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-11T16:09:48-07:00","id":511278,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ghosthead</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/507138-would-exigents-suffer-the-great-curse?p=511060#post511060\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Re: Solar, upthread, I'm not unsympathetic, but if the Great Curse includes unwelcome genre assumptions for your group and game then you... take it out.<br /> <br /> As a whole I have not seen any evidence it presents unwelcome genre assumptions for the community of Exalted as a whole.<br /> <br /> (Although a lot of members of the community were introduced to Exalted via conceptions that ignored it being a game about mighty, cursed heroes in the first place, as is on I think literally the first page of the first book written about the game.)</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't like taking stuff out of game systems. Games should be designed holistically, with each element of the system contributing to the wider game. I also never really feel that Rule Zero is worth bringing up in a discussion about game rules; yes I could change it. I could write my entire own system and setting. I don't want to, though, that's why I am spending money on this book.<br /> <br /> My problem is less that the genre assumptions are unwelcome, and more that the genre assumptions become a really core part of the story whether you like it or not, because the Great Curse is such a powerful force upon your character that you can't really just ignore it's influence. Which would be okay, I think, if the Great Curse actually felt vaguely enjoyable to interact with (giving you bonuses, perhaps for voluntarily allowing your character to act irrationally), it actually just feels like a total punishment that the game arbitrarily hands out every now and again in the same of genre emulation.<br /> <br /> Genre emulation is fine, clumsily and crudely enforced genre emulation without any respect for the actual game being played is not. I mostly hate the Great Curse as a design element, I think it sucks in the setting as well to be quite honest, but my real beef with it has always been how much it shits all over your games as a player and a GM.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ghosthead</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/507138-would-exigents-suffer-the-great-curse?p=511060#post511060\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Re: whether Grabowski intended the game to be a hopeless setting, I think (perhaps as part of the Grabowski cult) he intended it personally to be stirringly tragic, and generally wasn't big on the secret truths of the setting over personal taste and whatever you feel like doing with it. Really. The following are his over ten year old opinions expressed on a forum (as evidence goes it's what we have <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> ):<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://exalted.xi.co.nz/wiki/Thus_Spake_Zargrabowski/ConditionOfCreation\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://exalted.xi.co.nz/wiki/Thus_Spake_Zargrabowski/ConditionOfCreation\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://exalted.xi.co.nz/wiki/Thus_Spake_Zargrabowski/ConditionOfCreation\" target=\"_blank\"> http://exalted.xi.co.nz/wiki/Thus_Spake_Zargrabowski/ConditionOfCreation </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <a href=\"http://exalted.xi.co.nz/wiki/Thus_Spake_Zargrabowski/SanctityOfGameWorld\" target=\"_blank\">http://exalted.xi.co.nz/wiki/Thus_Sp...ityOfGameWorld</a></div> </div> </div> </div>Grabowski's love of a tragic end to all things is all well and good for him but I don't particularly care to play in it. A game where everything I build turns to shit is pretty fucking unsatisfying to play.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/117-solar","name":"Solar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar117_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1267"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-11T16:13:37-07:00","id":511282,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/507138-would-exigents-suffer-the-great-curse?p=511276#post511276\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">All too much.</div> </div> </div> </div>So you want us to know...what about them exactly? &quot;These are the Solar Exalted, they exist&quot;?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/598-couch","name":"Couch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar598_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"330"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-11T16:19:22-07:00","id":511285,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Valles</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/507138-would-exigents-suffer-the-great-curse?p=511256#post511256\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">We also know that Exalted is a setting that draws on ancient and classical history, periods where 'absolute autocrat with divine imprimatur' was the default political system. Attempting to assume that the Solars of the First Age were anything else is, I think... silly.</div> </div> </div> </div>And considering the Primordial (callous, inflexible autocracy, slavery, mass-killing on a whim) and Dragon-King (lots of violence, people sacrifice, slavery) models they had to work with, we shouldn't be surprised either.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">She/Her. I am literal-minded and write literally. If I don't say something explicitly, please never assume I implied it. The only exception is if I try to make a joke.</span></span></span></div> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">My point of view may be different from yours but is equally valid.</span></span></span><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1x1ycoxJF0G9niMt5D3Pp7owZ7tw8AJvL?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted-cWoD-ArM url mega-library</a>. Exalted <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/663334-random-name-generator\" target=\"_blank\">name-generators</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","name":"Erinys","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar896_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4235"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-11T22:16:40-07:00","id":511677,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zelbinnean</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/507138-would-exigents-suffer-the-great-curse?p=510528#post510528\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Meriting power in no way makes one a good person.<br /> <br /> I don't like the SunJesus portrayal insofar as it creates the implication that UCS would only Exalt capital-G Good people. During the Primordial War I imagine that people who would get the job done were Chosen, people for whom the ends could easily justify the means, which could and did involve genocide of people and species who were loyal to the Primordials.<br /> <br /> The Unconquered Sun's favor isn't a good bellweather for anything other than &quot;this person is, on some level, willing to wield terrible cosmic power.&quot;<br /> <br /> Frankly I don't think UCS scared about the quality of people who would ultimately ruled Creation. He wanted his rebellion to win. He wanted the Primordials overthrown and himself as King of Heaven. The excesses of the Exalted ultimately grew to a point where they lost his favor but it's not as if he could ever suppress the human nature of his Chosen.</div> </div> </div> </div>I wasn't a fan of SunJesus either but... here's what I'm thinking.<br /> <br /> The Unconquered Sun put the Solars in charge. He knew they were the big dogs (in 2nd edition he literally put them in charge but even in a 3rd edition where that could be changed he still would have known that they were the head honchos of Creation). It is odd if he knew that and then once the Primordial War had ended, he had chosen to continue Exalting the sort of people who would abuse their power.<br /> <br /> Basically during the Primordial War he would have Exalted people who would use that power however they could. I absolutely agree with that. He didn't need an army of Paladins - what he needed was an army of merciless warriors who were willing to do whatever it took to destroy the Primordials. But <i>after</i> the Primordial War, after he named the Solars as the new rulers of Creation (or at least after he was aware that they were the rulers of Creation if his &quot;Mandate of Heaven&quot; is no longer a thing in Third Edition) he would have known that what Creation needed was not a bunch of completely ruthless warriors willing to do whatever they could to get ahead, but rather compassionate and merciful rulers.<br /> <br /> So it seems strange if he would have continued to Exalt the former rather than the latter (though it would certainly explain why Creation had so many problems in the First Age when the world was more peaceful and didn't need merciless warriors and yet he kept Exalting people like Achilles and Lu Bu to be the leaders of this new world). In 2nd edition this could easily be explained due to the fact that the Unconquered Sun had absolutely no control over who Exalted. But, this is being changed come Third Edition, with the Unconquered Sun having some level of say in who gets Exalted and who doesn't.<br /> <br /> Having a bunch of Buddha's and Gandhi's running around would still cause problems, but it would certainly have changed the tone of the First Age quite a bit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":741,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","user":"AnubisXy","date":". 05-12-2015, 01:33 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-11T22:24:29-07:00","id":511678,"title":"","content":"While the Deliberative gave too much power to the Solars, you couldn't reasonably have anything democracy-like when Exalted have super-social powers: you'd just end up with some subset of the Solars (the ones who invested in social skills and Charms) in charge anyway.<br /> <br /> I think about the best you could do is some sort of &quot;tribune of the plebeians&quot; representation for non-Exalted people...<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5488-goldfaction","name":"goldfaction","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"90"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-11T22:25:15-07:00","id":511679,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zelbinnean</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/507138-would-exigents-suffer-the-great-curse?p=509450#post509450\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;Congrats, all the magic that induces Limit as collateral to resisting it, like <i>all UMI in the 2e system</i>, you're now passively, perfectly immune to.&quot;<br /> <br /> This is totally broken to hell and back, if you can't see that I really don't know what to tell you.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, I meant stuff like Sanity-Eroding Diatribe or whatever that Abyssal Charm is that makes mortals go crazy and gives Exalts Limit.<br /> <br /> An unCursed Exalt would still have to spend Willpower to resist UMI, just wouldn't get Limit.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> You want to let Exalts excise their humanity and only gain benefits from it? </div> </div> </div>Not excise their humanity, improve it <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The &quot;flaw&quot; in human nature is nothing less than the actual notion of &quot;what it means to be human&quot; itself. </div> </div> </div>I'm not sure that I agree with that.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Making the Exalted inherently less human and more &quot;infallible&quot; or at the very least, with cheap <i>mechanical</i> access to being capital-G Good without any kind of draw is a toxic notion that has no place in the kind of setting that Creation is supposed to be, i.e. a realistic one with a basis in how human beings actually behave. Exalted is fundamentally a story about human beings and the nature of power. Once you start removing those bits, it is no simply longer Exalted. </div> </div> </div>Well, it wouldn't be quite that easy. I mean, Exalted's setting doesn't have objective morality, so I'm not necessarily talking about &quot;capital-G Good&quot;. Just... less subject to irrational and destructive behavior.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5488-goldfaction","name":"goldfaction","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"90"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-12T01:15:12-07:00","id":511795,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/507138-would-exigents-suffer-the-great-curse?p=511677#post511677\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It is odd if he knew that and then once the Primordial War had ended, he had chosen to continue Exalting the sort of people who would abuse their power.</div> </div> </div> </div>It really isn't.<br /> <br /> First, because just about anyone you'd care to name would, if given illimitable power and 3,000+ years to use it, find reason to abuse it at least once.<br /> <br /> Second, because no system is perfect to begin with, so abuse of one's power to bend the rules is hardly always a bad thing. <br /> <br /> Third, the Sun can't <i>not</i> Exalt someone he's going to Exalt. If he casts his gaze down on Creation and sees a great hero, you really think he can stop himself from passing down the divine fire because he thinks the guy might do something bad twenty years down the road?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> he would have known that what Creation needed was not a bunch of completely ruthless warriors willing to do whatever they could to get ahead, but rather compassionate and merciful rulers. </div> </div> </div>&quot;Nearly all men can stand adversity, but if you want to test a man's character, give him power.&quot; -Abraham Lincoln<br /> <br /> You can't really be sure how someone is going to behave after you Exalt them. I bet that even if the Sun shut his eyes to everyone with a Compassion below five that Creation would still end up in the same basket.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> So it seems strange if he would have continued to Exalt the former rather than the latter\u2026 </div> </div> </div>Nah, see, part of your mistake is that even during the War, he Exalted <i>heroes</i>. Not &quot;completely ruthless warriors,&quot; but also not &quot;rather compassionate and merciful rulers.&quot; He never changed his selection process for either period.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> But, this is being changed come Third Edition, with the Unconquered Sun having some level of say in who gets Exalted and who doesn't. </div> </div> </div>Now <i>that's</i> an odd interpretation of what we've been given.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Having a bunch of Buddha's and Gandhi's running around would still cause problems, but it would certainly have changed the tone of the First Age quite a bit. </div> </div> </div>Prove me wrong.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-12T01:57:44-07:00","id":511843,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/507138-would-exigents-suffer-the-great-curse?p=511795#post511795\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Third, the Sun can't <i>not</i> Exalt someone he's going to Exalt. If he casts his gaze down on Creation and sees a great hero, you really think he can stop himself from passing down the divine fire because he thinks the guy might do something bad twenty years down the road?</div> </div> </div> </div>As much as I disliked JesusSun I <i>really</i> hated the idea of a &quot;RoboSun&quot; whose actions were so heavily predefined by his Virtues that he practically couldn't prevent himself from undertaking certain actions.<br /> <br /> I think the Unconquered Sun would be aware that if he Exalts someone like Lu Bu or Achilles during peacetime, there's going to be big problems that wouldn't be as likely to occur if he Exalted people with more pacifistic, peaceful or merciful tendencies.<br /> <br /> Admittedly this does tend to minimize the need for a Great Curse since the problem in the First Age wasn't so much &quot;power eventually corrupts even the best of people&quot; as it was, &quot;the Unconquered Sun is putting assholes in charge who <i>started off</i> as giant dicks even before they got a taste of power and were naturally only going to get worse.&quot;<br /> <br /> At the same time though it also changes up the narrative of the gameline quite a bit and casts a lot of the blame for the fall of the First Age on the Unconquered Sun. Officially the First Age fell because the Great Curse. But if we tone the Great Curse down as some people have suggested, and if we have the idea that the Unconquered Sun isn't a robot and does have some influence in Exalting people, that's basically where we end up - the First Age went to shit because the Unconquered Sun chose to Exalt people, people he knew were going to rule Creation, even knowing those people were going to turn it into a toilet bowl.<br /> <br /> So in light of all that, &quot;RoboSun&quot; who functions as a computer program (IF Sun sees hero AND IF Exaltation is available THEN Exalt) and has no control or influence over who actually gains Exaltation is probably the better than a Sun who is largely responsible for the fall of the First Age, but at the same time I just personally detest the presentation of the Unconquered Sun as a robot.<br /> <br /> Which is ultimately why the Great Curse is pretty vital to the story of the First Age - because without it, you either end up with the Unconquered Sun shouldering too much responsibility for how things ended up going (because he was choosing to Exalt people like, say, Haveash) or you end up with &quot;RoboSun&quot; who bares no responsibility because he absolutely cannot prevent himself from Exalting the people who were pretty obviously going to turn Creation into a shithole.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":741,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","user":"AnubisXy","date":". 05-12-2015, 05:01 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-12T02:28:03-07:00","id":511850,"title":"","content":"Did I say the Sun was defined by his Virtues like a robot? No. Let me double-check. No.<br /> <br /> But the Sun is defined by <i>who and what he is</i>. Can you not be you? Does that make <i>you</i> a robot?<br /> <br /> I don't think bots are permitted on this forum; they usually get banned when the mods discover them\u2026 &gt;.&gt;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-12T02:48:47-07:00","id":511853,"title":"","content":"You asked if I thought the Unconquered Sun could prevent himself from Exalting someone because the guy might do something bad 20 years down the road.<br /> <br /> If the Unconquered Sun is incapable of choosing to withhold Exaltation from someone he knows will wield his gifts to terrible ends, then he is &quot;robot-like&quot; in that he has an automated &quot;If/Then&quot; statement about Exalting people. In this case he doesn't &quot;choose&quot; to Exalt someone, but rather automatically Exalts someone who meets a certain criteria.<br /> <br /> That's basically just like 2nd edition where you had &quot;automated Exaltations,&quot; that would simply Exalt someone who held the right criteria and (so far as we know) didn't have the capability to deliberately choose or exclude someone from Exaltation.<br /> <br /> I don't like the Unconquered Sun being presented like that.<br /> <br /> So my answer is, yes, the Unconquered Sun <i>can</i> choose to withhold Exaltation from someone or he can choose to bestow it on them. When he grants the Exaltation to someone, it's not the result of some &quot;autonomic response&quot; but rather a deliberate choice that he makes.<br /> <br /> Now in in 2nd edition you didn't really need a Great Curse because the Exaltations simply Exalted whomever they felt like, so it was only natural in the First Age you'd end up with a number of Solar god-kings who were giant assholes.<br /> <br /> But in 3rd edition, where the Unconquered Sun has a choice in the matter, then you do need a Great Curse or it puts too much responsibility on the Sun for how things went down in the First Age - if only he had done a better job of choosing or vetting people to receive his blessings then the First Age might not have gone down the way it did. With the inclusion of the Great Curse however, it's not really the Unconquered Sun's fault since the corruption and fall of the Solar Exalted is not something he could have prevented or changed by picking different people.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-12T03:28:20-07:00","id":511861,"title":"","content":"Nice excluded middle there. If the Sun can't help who he falls in love with, and thus chooses the occasional asshole, he <i>must</i> be a robot. I can't agree with that logic, but I also violently reject the other notion that the Sun <i>must</i> be able to only choose perfect rainbow princesses and it's just that mean ol' Great Curse stopping Creation in the First Age from becoming Happytopia.<br /> <br /> The Sun isn't a robot, but he won't do what he won't do, either. If you argue that makes him a robot or like a robot or an autonomous Exaltation delivery system or what the fuck else ever, I can't stop you from making that argument, but consider how much of a &quot;choice in the matter&quot; you have in <i>your</i> day-to-day life. If the Sun doesn't choose his Solars, how do <i>you</i> make any choices at all?<br /> <br /> I could certainly <i>use</i> Mountain Dew Baja Blast instead of water to make my Kraft Mac and Cheese, but I get the feeling it'd turn out pretty terribly. I <i>have</i> both Baja Blast and water, but I only ever <i>choose</i> to use water. Does this mean I'm a robot?<br /> <br /> And so what if the Sun's &quot;responsible&quot; for some of the badness that happened in the First Age? I wouldn't accept anything less! He's the goddamned King of Heaven! Without absolute omniscience, he's going to occasionally make bad choices, no matter how insightful he is, <i>and those are at least partially his fault</i>. No, the presence of the Great Curse doesn't absolve him of it, either.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":177,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","user":"TheCountAlucard","date":". 05-12-2015, 06:51 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-12T03:53:51-07:00","id":511867,"title":"","content":"The word &quot;choose&quot; means that you have the option of doing one thing or another. Yeah, you do choose to use Baja Blast instead of water (though if you do use the Mountain Dew you might try to add in some crunched up Cool Ranch Doritos on top).<br /> <br /> If the Unconquered Sun is capable of Exalting people who aren't assholes, but goes ahead and Exalts assholes anyway, then that's a choice. But if the Unconquered Sun <i>can't help</i> but Exalt people who are assholes, then he isn't making a choice in the matter.<br /> <br /> So if we're going with the idea that the Sun is capable of choosing whom he Exalts, then the Great Curse is important in the narrative of the First Age to explain why things went to hell (since the alternative is that the Unconquered Sun is mostly at fault for choosing to Exalt the people who dragged Creation to the brink).<br /> <br /> On the other hand, if the Sun &quot;just can't help it,&quot; then the Great Curse isn't as necessary from a narrative standpoint (just like it wasn't entirely necessary in 2nd edition with automated Exaltations) because it was inevitable that you would end up with people who would be more prone to corruption and dragging Creation down than if someone were making conscientious decisions about who Exalts and who doesn't.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-12T04:05:38-07:00","id":511876,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/507138-would-exigents-suffer-the-great-curse?p=511867#post511867\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> If the Unconquered Sun is capable of dating people who aren't assholes, but goes ahead and dates assholes anyway, then that's a choice. But if the Unconquered Sun <i>can't help</i> but date people who are assholes, then he isn't making a choice in the matter.</div> </div> </div> </div>Relationships and attraction are complicated.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Oh, wait... the exact same point was made just a moment ago... and roundly ignored...<br /> <br /> Darn it, I dislike wasting my time.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-12T04:09:41-07:00","id":511877,"title":"","content":"I personally prefer the theory that the Unconquered Sun chooses to exalt people he thinks have the potential to do great and amazing things, but he is not infallible and not Jesus. Even in peace time some of his choices will be people not exactly perfect for peaceful utopia - gladiators, soldiers, ambitious petty officers - because those people have as much potential for greatness as the last few Sun Tzus and the like in particular because there is always the potential for strife and chaos.<br /> <br /> Furthermore, his insight should not be so great as to know that if this person is exalted, then in five hundred years they will purge all sweet innocent puppies from Creation because of events that occur in the interim. He looks at their past and their heart as it exists and measures who they have been without power, and attempts to use that as a yard stick for who they will be with unimaginable power.<br /> <br /> It's not perfect but it's the best he can know without abrogation of free will.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/756-meianno-yuurei","name":"Meianno Yuurei","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar756_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-12T04:32:29-07:00","id":511888,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/507138-would-exigents-suffer-the-great-curse?p=511876#post511876\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Relationships and attraction are complicated.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Oh, wait... the exact same point was made just a moment ago... and roundly ignored...<br /> <br /> Darn it, I dislike wasting my time.</div> </div> </div> </div>If you can't choose who you fall in love with, and if just like that the Unconquered Sun can't choose who he Exalts then... well, he pretty clearly <i>isn't</i> choosing who he Exalts.<br /> <br /> Anyway, the point I was getting at is that if the Unconquered Sun does in fact choose who Exalts, then you need the Great Curse to fill a role in the narrative or else the responsibility for the way things went down lays pretty heavily on his shoulders. If the Unconquered Sun isn't choosing which person Exalts, then the need for the Great Curse isn't as large and you can push it out of the way or even remove it entirely.<br /> <br /> In 2nd edition the Unconquered Sun had little to no say so in who Exalted so there was less of a need for the Great Curse. In Third Edition that could change (we don't know; maybe he still doesn't really have a choice in the matter) and depending how it does the narrative role of the Great Curse could be quite a bit more important, and therefore harder to remove it or push it aside than it was in the previous edition.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-12T04:36:05-07:00","id":511890,"title":"","content":"I keep thinking in terms of things like in the Lucifer comics when the Morningstar coerces Izanami into returning his wings, and she vengefully plants extra feathers in them saying something to the effect of &quot;when the time comes, he will find himself alone and friendless and will not see dangers and treachery coming&quot;, or in Hellboy the way the titular character needs to labour under a heavy burden of responsibility and doom that he can't simply disregard but doesn't control him either.<br /> <br /> The idea of a curse that works with and follows along your flaws and failings and capabilities, rather than creating them wholecloth, and sharpens their edges against you.<br /> <br /> Although sometimes I think even that much is too much of a concession, and that it's simpler to just go straight with the idea of cursed heroes.<br /> <br /> The idea that the only thing to do with a curse is remove it is so... narrow.<br /> <br /> Best revenge is living well, and all.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-12T04:53:18-07:00","id":511895,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>goldfaction</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/507138-would-exigents-suffer-the-great-curse?p=511679#post511679\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just... less subject to irrational and destructive behavior.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is per se less human.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-12T05:16:04-07:00","id":511908,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/507138-would-exigents-suffer-the-great-curse?p=511890#post511890\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Although sometimes I think even that much is too much of a concession, and that it's simpler to just go straight with the idea of cursed heroes.<br /> <br /> The idea that the only thing to do with a curse is remove it is so... narrow.<br /> <br /> Best revenge is living well, and all.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree, I'd love to see that be an option.<br /> <br /> Unfortunately the previous editions, the gameline flat out said things like the Great Curse being the reason the First Age went to hell, or that the Great Curse &quot;blinded&quot; the Sidereal Exalted and made them go with the Bronze Prophecy (that sidebar is probably the single thing I hate the most that's ever been published in the gameline) or that the Great Curse condemns the Exalted to ruin what they care for, then removing, negating or otherwise limiting the Curse becomes the only thing to do when your characters discover it, because it's the reason everything fell apart and the reason why everything will fall apart again no matter what else you try and do.<br /> <br /> Hopefully whatever role the Great Curse plays in 3rd edition, it won't be as quite as important, pivotal and defining in fall Creation's Ages and therefore give a bit more room to play around with.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-12T05:29:21-07:00","id":511921,"title":"","content":"Let's play with another metaphor: beauty pageants.<br /> <br /> The judge is responsible for choosing the winner. He has a set of criteria that he must abide by; he can't just turn around and point at his wife in the audience and declare her the winner, he can only choose the people that entered the pageant, even if his wife was more beautiful and talented and can say she wants world peace with a more soulful expression. He still makes a choice, based off what he observes in the contestants, and importantly, he can still end up regretting his decision afterward.<br /> <br /> But hey, feel free to argue that he's a soulless robot, too, or whatever.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-12T05:48:30-07:00","id":511930,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/507138-would-exigents-suffer-the-great-curse?p=511908#post511908\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u2026then removing, negating or otherwise limiting the Curse becomes <b>the only thing to do </b>when your characters discover it\u2026</div> </div> </div> </div>Have you read <i>Hellboy</i>? Like, at all?<br /> <br /> I'll take &quot;keep on trying in spite of the curse&quot; for 500, Alex.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":177,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","user":"TheCountAlucard","date":". 05-12-2015, 08:53 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-12T05:53:15-07:00","id":511934,"title":"","content":"Part of the reason I prefer the Curse to be undiscoverable and incurable is how making it either discoverable or curable, or both, will skew stories towards that narrative. That just gets old. Accomplishing great things despite your burdens is more interesting to me than every story turning into &quot;genius Carl Jung Twilight discovers Curse, forces party on quest to cure their soul-cancer.&quot;<br /> <br /> Causes all the same narrative problems as the Reclamation and Island Five.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-12T05:56:52-07:00","id":511937,"title":"","content":"People in the first Exalted game I ever played in found out how my character was driven to act irrationally in the face of a chance to prove himself <i>in the first session</i>.<br /> <br /> More than a year's gaming later, he was still as crazy as ever. He was never cured of his Great Curse. No characters, in <i>any</i> of the games I've played or ran, have cured the Great Curse, though a fair number of them discovered it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":177,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","user":"TheCountAlucard","date":". 05-12-2015, 08:59 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-12T05:57:31-07:00","id":511938,"title":"","content":"If Jeffery Dahmer is the only guy available for the Unconquered Sun to give an Exaltation to, and he <i>has</i> to pick Hitler, then the Unconquered Sun doesn't have a choice.<br /> <br /> But if the Unconquered Sun has several choices, then presumably he isn't going to pick Jeffery Dahmer. If the Unconquered Sun picks Jeffery Dhamer anyway, even though he had &quot;less terrible&quot; people to choose from, and Solar Dhamer goes around using his powers to commit evil, then the Unconquered Sun is kind of a rat bastard for not picking someone else.<br /> <br /> Of course, it's certainly possible that the only people the Sun can choose from at a given time are Jeffery Dahmer, Adolf Hitler and Charles Manson, and importantly the Unconquered Sun can't choose <i>not</i> to Exalt someone. But if we go with the idea that the reason that the First Age fell apart wasn't because of a Great Curse but because the Sun consistently had to pick people to Exalt from a pool of corrupt humans and rarely ever had a chance to choose decent people, then that kind of says something about Exaltation and makes you question what sort of criteria it runs off of.<br /> <br /> Either way though, the gameline is probably better off with the idea of a Great Curse ultimately being responsible for the fall of the First Age, rather than the idea that the Unconquered Sun decided to give the Solars responsibility for Creation but then picked people who wouldn't be able to handle the responsibility or that he was, at best, forced to choose against his will from various people that he knew couldn't handle the responsibility.<br /> <br /> Far better, I think, to say that the Unconquered Sun generally did his best to pick people who he knew wouldn't be terrible for the future of Creation, but that pesky Great Curse ended up ruining things.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":741,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","user":"AnubisXy","date":". 05-12-2015, 09:00 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-12T06:04:34-07:00","id":511942,"title":"","content":"Better to say &quot;UCS picks heroes. Heroes don't have to be good people. Heroes frequently have big and unpredictable personalities which is part of what makes them heroes: they buck the easy and predictable trend of just being normal. UCS is not omniscient and doesn't exactly know much about the people he is Choosing except that they are heroes who will wield his power rather than let it sit around stagnant.&quot;<br /> <br /> I much prefer that to either &quot;UCS robotically picks assholes&quot; or &quot;UCS only picks nice and good people and that mean old Curse cocks it up&quot;<br /> <br /> Quoting on my phone is hard so I'll just say, Anubis, I reject that the setting is improved if the Curse is the reason that the First Age fell, as opposed to notions like &quot;power corrupts&quot; and &quot;sometimes good people do evil things for what they believe to be the right reasons.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":3420,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","user":"Zelbinnean","date":". 05-12-2015, 09:07 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-12T06:22:30-07:00","id":511952,"title":"","content":"You know, it's funny, I've always been a firm proponent of the idea that being Exalted doesn't mean you should be so above petty things like the desire for money.<br /> <br /> Yet, having read Debt and seen all of the interesting arguments and facts it presents about the context in which money may have or has been developed and sought, and all of the implications this has into social organisation and personal motivations and international relations and war, and it makes me think...<br /> <br /> Why not? Why <i>wouldn't</i> the Exalted have been above it all? Not because they're transcendent and enlightened but because, for their power, how easily their needs can be met.<br /> <br /> I mean, one says &quot;oh, we shouldn't need the Great Curse to bring down the Old Realm, because we can already see that it has all of these basic institutional weaknesses&quot;, and I'm still now wondering <b>why</b>. It's not as if the Exalted were just dropped in on a scenario in which all of these systems and weaknesses had already gotten off the ground and so you had people perpetuating them thoughtlessly because it was all they had ever known. Within this setting, <i>human civilization</i> began under the scenario of the Exalted being around, which is a pretty big leg up on anything it had in real life. Maybe the Realm was very dissimilar to our contemporary world, but only perhaps mildly dissimilar to various other societies throughout history, and I'm still left asking why it should ever have been in any way similar to us at all. The conditions in which human civilization originated are not incidental, and yet within this setting they're completely turned on their head.<br /> <br /> I think of some of Grabowski's statements to the effect of &quot;when you have the (Solar) Exalted, you don't really need a society based on harnessing and coordinating the labour of massive numbers of people&quot; and I ask &quot;then why would the concept of empire have ever been a thing?&quot; I'm not doubting the idea that Grabowski's statement is accurate in the setting, but there are other hints and motifs of the First Age that don't seem as though they would have logically emerged from such conceits (which, as I'll get to, I think is kind of by design).<br /> <br /> One could make the argument of &quot;oh, well, you'll never be devoid of people who are just greedy and selfish and violent (or even need to relentlessly innovate)&quot;, but... I don't buy it. The anthropological and historical and psychological evidence continues to mount that people who have their needs met and are sufficiently divorced from social conditioning to think that their needs are lesser than the relentless pursuit of more tend to be, as I think the scientific terminology goes, &quot;pretty chill&quot;. At the very least, there's a lot that is dependent on a context that stretches back through a loooooong lineage of scarcity and struggle and dependence.<br /> <br /> But the Exalted don't seem to have ever been.<br /> <br /> Another thing that started growing on my mind between reading that book and watching Age of Ultron was the idea of the villains of the movieverse Iron Man. How in each case they're people who are part of the abundantly wealthy and secure military-industrial complex, who already each have more money than God, and yet their plots in each film are focused on grandiose schemes in pursuit of <i>even more</i> money, which they will then spend on... what? I'm not too critical of it within the context of its own narrative (beyond how it might kind of validate Ultron's critique of &quot;want to save the world, but don't want it to change&quot;), but imagine if it was transplanted into a setting that was more concerned with validating the logical background and context of certain motivations.<br /> <br /> If you had the Mandarin in Exalted, why would he want to escalate the War on Terror to create even greater purchase orders for weaponry?<br /> <br /> Imagining the origins of human civilization with the presence of people like the Exalted, from whence would ever have come the motivation to pursue things that, in real life, come from a long long long history of want and limit? If we assume (drawing on all available evidence) that such social developments and personal motivations are not paradigmatic to humans and inevitable.<br /> <br /> From... the Neverborn?<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> (This is not to say that, if there had never been a Great Curse, the Exalted would have been incapable of making bad, short-sighted decisions, just... the motivation and the consequences and the response might have been in so many ways different. I mean, different beyond my capacity to imagine, because it's trying to model a human personality almost completely devoid of everything I can reference, but still... mental and physical limitations might still be a thing, and yet I continue to find it hard to imagine that a human race with the advantage of the Exalted from the very beginning would be in so many ways better if there wasn't something tugging at them to make mistakes approximating our conditions of doing the best we can)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-12T06:25:21-07:00","id":511956,"title":"","content":"You know who else knew with a conviction that everyone he loved would die, that everything he built would pass into dust, and that there wasn't a damned thing he could do about it?<br /> <br /> <i>Fucking Conan</i>. <br /> <br /> And I think that's plenty good.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-12T06:35:10-07:00","id":511961,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/507138-would-exigents-suffer-the-great-curse?p=511938#post511938\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But if the Unconquered Sun has several choices, then presumably he isn't going to pick Jeffery Dahmer.</div> </div> </div> </div>What if L'il' Jeffy is, like, ten years old at the time?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If the Unconquered Sun picks Jeffery Dhamer anyway, even though he had &quot;less terrible&quot; people to choose from, and Solar Dhamer goes around using his powers to commit evil, then the Unconquered Sun is kind of a rat bastard for not picking someone else. </div> </div> </div>Anyone can become something on the order of Jeff. Anyone. Possibly even worse.<br /> <br /> His criteria is that the person in question will use that power. Sometimes that power will be used in a way that provides a net good; sometimes it won't. And sometimes that net good will involve a lot of atrocities being committed. If he could restrict his search parameters to only cover people who would never misuse the power, the results wouldn't be anything human, and indeed, might not be <i>anything</i> that would use the power at all.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-12T06:40:26-07:00","id":511964,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zelbinnean</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/507138-would-exigents-suffer-the-great-curse?p=511942#post511942\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Better to say &quot;UCS picks heroes. Heroes don't have to be good people. Heroes frequently have big and unpredictable personalities which is part of what makes them heroes: they buck the easy and predictable trend of just being normal. UCS is not omniscient and doesn't exactly know much about the people he is Choosing except that they are heroes who will wield his power rather than let it sit around stagnant.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>The only real issue is, if the Unconquered Sun has witnessed what the Exalted have done over the years, to the point that he actively turned his back on Creation, then why does he continue to pick people that way? Why doesn't he take a little more time or a little more care? Maybe he simply doesn't really give much of a rats ass about what the Exalted do (as long as it doesn't affect him and they're not taking his name in vain). Or maybe he's simply incapable of choosing to withhold his blessing from people who won't use it wisely.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zelbinnean</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/507138-would-exigents-suffer-the-great-curse?p=511942#post511942\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Quoting on my phone is hard so I'll just say, Anubis, I reject that the setting is improved if the Curse is the reason that the First Age fell, as opposed to notions like &quot;power corrupts&quot; and &quot;sometimes good people do evil things for what they believe to be the right reasons.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>If we go with the idea that the First Age fell because power corrupts, then the Exalted setting is kind of at a dead end.<br /> <br /> The Exalted wield vast amounts of power. Any system you create will have the Exalted at the head. If corruption through power is so inevitable and so thorough that the only way to save Creation was to <i>murder all of the Solars and lock them away for eternity</i> then, well, there's not many places you can take this. The only way you can prevent the Solars from becoming corrupt and cocking up Creation again (like they did before) is to make sure that they can't hold any power.<br /> <br /> I'm not a huge fan of the Great Curse but at least with that there's a sense that it can be fixed and improve things. If we go with the idea that the First Age fell because the Unconquered Sun wasn't very careful in who he picked, then maybe there's a chance you can get him to pick better people. But I'm definitely not fond of the idea that the best way to save Creation was the Bronze Vision because &quot;power corrupts.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":741,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","user":"AnubisXy","date":". 05-12-2015, 09:45 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-12T06:47:37-07:00","id":511968,"title":"","content":"How could you choose more carefully? How could you start striking applicants off your list because they're not perfect, and still have a list afterward?<br /> <br /> And yes, &quot;are not perfect&quot; and &quot;will not turn into Jeffrey Dahmer&quot; are not synonymous, but when you give them the sheer amount of power that Exaltation confers, the line starts to get pretty fuzzy.<br /> <br /> And no, I'm not saying it all boils down to &quot;power corrupts,&quot; I'm saying that you don't know how someone will react to being powerful while they're still weak. It might even be that you <i>can't</i> know. The amount of power we're dealing with here is something like a crucible; it'll melt you down and we can all see what you really are.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":177,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","user":"TheCountAlucard","date":". 05-12-2015, 09:51 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-12T07:07:31-07:00","id":511974,"title":"","content":"I wouldn't expect Jeffrey Dahmer to be Exalted, but only because he's a serial killer, and that means he's super boring.<br /> <br /> I mean, what is the argument here? That a god would never Choose somebody who might go on to kill huge numbers of people? Are all circumstances in which somebody does that equivalent?<br /> <br /> Is being responsible for the deaths of large numbers of people not something that can exist in a context beyond how much you get off on killing people?<br /> <br /> Or is everybody who ever voted for a President who they should have known would order drone strikes a bastard as well?<br /> <br /> I'm not saying such things should be condoned, but they're still different in a manner that means something.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-12T07:21:30-07:00","id":511980,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/507138-would-exigents-suffer-the-great-curse?p=511974#post511974\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I wouldn't expect Jeffrey Dahmer to be Exalted, but only because he's a serial killer, and that means he's super boring.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think Anubis went with him because Anubis wanted to refer to someone horrible without jumping straight to Hitler (though Hitler <i>does</i> seem to be the example Anubis was originally going to go with, judging by some of the edits in the post). I merely continued with Dahmer because Anubis used him as an example.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-12T08:40:24-07:00","id":512015,"title":"","content":"Isator Levi, your points about the civilization Exalted would logially have built is very good, and not something that has ever occurred to me before. I almost completely agree with you, although I have one caveat: the human race had a long history of pre-civilization want and privation and oppression coloring their psyches. The Exalted themselves were born in those oppressed human societies scraping by at the absolute bottom of the pecking order of intelligent life. That's not to say that the Solar Exalted, or for that matter all the Exalted, weren't capable of changing human society drastically, because clearly they are. Just building civiilzation, where none had ever existed before, was such a feat. It still should not have remotely resembled anything we have in the real world, and the organizing principles would not have had anything to do with most of our familiar modes of scarcity.<br /> <br /> Money might still have been a thing in order to prop up the Order-Conferring Trade Pattern, but a lot of the other shit we have in our civilization... probably not. It would have been different enough that we can't necessarily imagine it. I'm sure some sci-fi authors have tried to write post-scarcity societies. But the First Age really seems like something that shouldn't be given details in the books because they'll inevitably fall flat and be too familiar.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/507138-would-exigents-suffer-the-great-curse?p=511930#post511930\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Have you read <i>Hellboy</i>? Like, at all?<br /> <br /> I'll take &quot;keep on trying in spite of the curse&quot; for 500, Alex.</div> </div> </div> </div>In 2e the Great Curse is written to be impossible to suppress, resist, or heroically succeed in spite of it. The mechanics reinforce this: using your strong will and virtue to fight the Curse <b><i>makes it worse</i></b>. The books make it clear that if you try to succeed heroically despite the Curse, it will <b><i>inevitably</i></b> fuck up everything you did and you <i><b>can't do anything about it</b></i> no matter what. There is no question whatsoever of heroically struggling to overcome your faults, because the game hammers in that this is categorically impossible and your character has no chance whatsoever.<br /> <br /> It's like Greek Tragedy: the heroes can fight against their fatal flaws and try to avoid ruining everything, but they ruin everything anyway because the gods fated them to do so, and they can't do anything about it because gods &gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; mortals. Oedipus and his parents and his foster parents all put everything they had into avoiding his curse, and everything they did inevitably caused him to kill his father and screw his mother. It was inevitable from the beginning. The man had no actual choice in the matter. That's what the Great Curse is modeled on.<br /> <br /> I'd probably hate the Great Curse less if it wasn't written this way in 3e.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">She/Her. I am literal-minded and write literally. If I don't say something explicitly, please never assume I implied it. The only exception is if I try to make a joke.</span></span></span></div> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">My point of view may be different from yours but is equally valid.</span></span></span><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1x1ycoxJF0G9niMt5D3Pp7owZ7tw8AJvL?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted-cWoD-ArM url mega-library</a>. Exalted <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/663334-random-name-generator\" target=\"_blank\">name-generators</a>.","edited":{"userid":896,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","user":"Erinys","date":". 05-12-2015, 11:56 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","name":"Erinys","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar896_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4235"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-12T08:41:55-07:00","id":512016,"title":"","content":"I was sort of under the impression that the vastly powerful and incomprehensible KING OF THE GODS might work on a mindset that is not, in fact, based in human conceptualization.<br /> <br /> I was equally under the impression that this godly being, this divine incarnation of the sun, might not be doing every thing it does with full and conscious attention to the act. That meaning that while the UCS may well in one way or another choose to Exalt someone, he may do so unconsciously, driven by subconscious instinct as to who qualifies as &quot;hero&quot; in his mind, without foreknowledge of the future and what that person may turn out to be later.<br /> <br /> I was also under the impression that gods don't have to make decisions based on a human mindset in the first place, and that ascribing directly human motives (BUT HE'S SMARTER THAN THAT GUYS OMG! arguments, for example, when referring to beings who may well be sharply intelligent but alien or driven by different motives than humans) to even human-like gods tends to lessen them, and that the new edition of Exalted would like to do quite the opposite of that.<br /> <br /> I'm not even remotely sure how this argument even got started, seeing how it began from a thread asking if the Exigents would suffer from the Curse (My money: yes, because the What We Know page seemed to say they existed before and some fought against the Primordials), but I do think it's getting a little scary in this thread, how hard some folks are pushing for the idea that just because a being is powerful and intelligent, that it must necessarily operate on the exact levels humans understand, just bigger somehow.<br /> <br /> Imagine what you look like to a dog, for example, with your comprehensive understanding of cause and effect and use of complex tools and higher reasoning, how you might, should that dog be able to articulate the concept, seem terribly powerful somehow.<br /> <br /> Imagine how that dog might yet be confused that you can't smell that that girl over there likes you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5771-krata-lightblade","name":"Krata Lightblade","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5771_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"72"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-12T09:22:35-07:00","id":512047,"title":"","content":"Wish I could like that post more than once, Krata. <br /> <br /> It's easy to overly anthropomorphize UCS because he has a humanoid form. It's easy to ascribe alien thought processes to the Primordials because of their complicated soul structure. But you're absolutely right that just because he's mostly humaniform, UCS in no way needs to approach the world from a human outlook. He can hold himself bound by cosmic virtues and also not be an asshole in picking people like Lyta, Ophiucus Ses, and even Havesh. <br /> <br /> Maybe in a way he picks the heroes Creation needs, not the ones it deserves. <br /> <br /> I don't think UCS Choosing implies the level of conscious control as, say, picking out a car where you have a lot of time to do research, accrue evidence, etc. I think it's been said that once the power of Solar Exaltation came into the world, UCS forfeited a degree of control over it. Not all control, but he isn't able to call back the power he threw out into the world. He can't stop Exalting people. And it's questionable that he would ever want to. <br /> <br /> It's possible more care in Choosing simply isn't possible because that's how Exaltation works: it's a miracle and a mystery, not something easily turned on and directed with perfect foresight and control. And it's certainly very possible that UCS doesn't operate on normative human morality. He certainly turned his back on a world that needed him where I think most humans with that power, seeing an extinction level event occurring, would intervene - for the greater good or their own benefit, it doesn't matter, I think most would intervene given the power to do so. <br /> <br /> And from Perfect Soul's Exaltation scene it seems to be as much about a right moment as it is about a right person. Maybe even more so. <br /> <br /> Honestly a number of these problems with UCS arise out of the hyper focus he was given in late 2e. &quot;Why would UCS Choose assholes when he hostages himself for the sake of a single mortal's life,&quot; people probably ask. &quot;That makes him at best a robot and at worst a dick, right?&quot;<br /> <br /> My response is &quot;that story should never have been canon because it fucks up all kinds of much more important setting assumptions.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-12T09:27:33-07:00","id":512048,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/507138-would-exigents-suffer-the-great-curse?p=511980#post511980\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think Anubis went with him because Anubis wanted to refer to someone horrible without jumping straight to Hitler (though Hitler <i>does</i> seem to be the example Anubis was originally going to go with, judging by some of the edits in the post). I merely continued with Dahmer because Anubis used him as an example.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> You know, people can talk about Hitler, and he was undeniably a pretty terrible person, but it's not as if Hitler invented anti-semitism, or quasi-scientific ideas about the systematic extermination of entire populations for some vaguely defined or poorly understood greater good.<br /> <br /> I mean, with the Holocaust... it can be really difficult to read about the Holocaust (not just for reasons of being able to stomach it, a lot of the information was deliberately or accidentally destroyed as the administration broke down and was subjected to heavy shelling at the end of the war, and apart from how a lot of the people who were involved didn't exactly have reason to be clear and honest afterwards most of them were executed in short order), but one thing one can get from doing so is a sense of just how disorganised it was. It comes across as less a master plan of ultimate evil and more this kind of series of attempts to actually follow up on odious rhetoric in a period of severe resource shortages and poor administrative communication and oversight and an extremely tumultuous period that all kind of crashed into each other and picked up massive amounts of momentum.<br /> <br /> I in no way mean that as an exoneration, a kind of &quot;oops, now how did this Holocaust get here&quot;, just the sense of it being the culmination of big, complex events with a lot of preamble that are hard to really grasp in their entirety and so need to be reduced down to easily grasped abstractions, more than the projects of specific individuals.<br /> <br /> I'm not sure where I'm going with this... I suppose at least one thing I could take is to suggest a world in which Hitler is Exalted (by the Unconquered Sun, at least) doesn't necessarily work at least because the social context into which Hitler is slotted isn't really present, and to the extent that any similar ones do in the setting, maybe they're... not entirely evident from a certain human perspective.<br /> <br /> I mean, look at say... Genghis Khan. <i>We</i> know that his conquests resulted in the deaths of possibly up to 40 million people, but I'm not sure <i>he</i> would have (it's not as if he was killing them all personally), and even if you told him I don't think he would have really been able to grasp how much that is. I mean, I doubt any of us even can, not really. I could put forward that, to him, the scale of how many people that you're impressive because you killed them (again, existing within a context in which that thing is brought on and assessed for reasons more complex than &quot;because you're an evil murder-boner haver) kind of tops out at 100 yurts (a 5) and then everything above that is a 6, because the difference between 10,000 and ten million people is still &quot;more than I can personally know in my lifetime&quot;.<br /> <br /> I don't know; I just feel as though there's a way to preserve the idea of being Chosen of the Sun without the idea that every consequence of your actions is necessarily something that can be known ahead of time or judged by the standards of... us (no qualifiers).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-12T09:38:44-07:00","id":512059,"title":"","content":"If you want to play a cursed hero, that's fine. That's a very cool narrative. Exalted should totally allow those narratives.<br /> <br /> But with the Great Curse, you have to play that narrative. You cannot play a Solar without the great curse.<br /> <br /> That's... not cool","signature":"","edited":{"userid":117,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/117-solar","user":"Solar","date":".  bit much, yeah 05-12-2015, 02:11 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/117-solar","name":"Solar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar117_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1267"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-12T09:52:18-07:00","id":512086,"title":"","content":"I don't know if saying &quot;it's bullshit&quot; is really correct. <br /> <br /> I mean, the game and its authors are not somehow obliged to provide you with the option to play a non-cursed hero if the themes of the game revolve around heroes who are victims of their own heroism in the manner of the Greek epics, any more than, say, the L5R RPG is obliged to make gaijin characters playable within the social strictures of that setting, or One Ring is obliged to make orcs or Maiar playable. <br /> <br /> At the same time there must be more fun ways to model being cursed to epic hubris etc than effectively being under some irresistible Compulsion spell, right?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-12T09:55:21-07:00","id":512091,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zelbinnean</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/507138-would-exigents-suffer-the-great-curse?p=512086#post512086\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">At the same time there must be more fun ways to model being cursed to epic hubris etc than effectively being under some irresistible Compulsion spell, right?</div> </div> </div> </div>Let's hope. I can't recall if the Devs said they were reworking the Limit/Curse mechanics to encourage players to use limit breaks, instead of forcing it.<br /> <br /> I also hope that Sidereals have actual mechanics to encourage them to act out their Curse this time around.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">She/Her. I am literal-minded and write literally. If I don't say something explicitly, please never assume I implied it. The only exception is if I try to make a joke.</span></span></span></div> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">My point of view may be different from yours but is equally valid.</span></span></span><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1x1ycoxJF0G9niMt5D3Pp7owZ7tw8AJvL?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted-cWoD-ArM url mega-library</a>. Exalted <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/663334-random-name-generator\" target=\"_blank\">name-generators</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","name":"Erinys","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar896_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4235"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-12T10:22:52-07:00","id":512110,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Solar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/507138-would-exigents-suffer-the-great-curse?p=512059#post512059\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you want to play a cursed hero, that's fine. That's a very cool narrative. Exalted should totally allow those narratives.</div> </div> </div> </div>What does a non-cursed hero look like? Can you name even one?<br /> <br /> Anyone who does something to be a hero is going to make some enemies, earn some hatred. People or gods or monsters or great forces come into conflict with them. If they didn't they wouldn't be heroes.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Solar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/507138-would-exigents-suffer-the-great-curse?p=512059#post512059\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But with the Great Curse, you have to play that narrative. You cannot play a Solar without the great curse.</div> </div> </div> </div>Excepting, of course, in Second Edition when you could; playing a redeemed Abyssal or a Solar who was the reincarnation of a redeemed Abyssal was hardly the default, but an understanding ST might very well allow one if you talked to them about it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Solar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/507138-would-exigents-suffer-the-great-curse?p=512059#post512059\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's bullshit.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's silly.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-12T11:18:17-07:00","id":512151,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/507138-would-exigents-suffer-the-great-curse?p=512110#post512110\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What does a non-cursed hero look like? Can you name even one?<br /> <br /> Anyone who does something to be a hero is going to make some enemies, earn some hatred. People or gods or monsters or great forces come into conflict with them. If they didn't they wouldn't be heroes.<br /> <br /> Excepting, of course, in Second Edition when you could; playing a redeemed Abyssal or a Solar who was the reincarnation of a redeemed Abyssal was hardly the default, but an understanding ST might very well allow one if you talked to them about it.<br /> <br /> That's silly.</div> </div> </div> </div>Having enemies =/= cursed. Come on, the exalted are cursed, literally driven to madness. There's a massive difference between &quot;I have enemies&quot; and &quot;I am subject to an undetectable, incurable insanity which I was imposed upon me malevolently by another&quot;<br /> <br /> And both of those options are massively outlying cases (in the setting there's good odds that those Solar Exaltations don't even exist) which aren't even allowed by the rules without poking at them.<br /> <br /> Loads of heroes aren't cursed. Loads of heroes who directly inspire exalted aren't cursed. Conan, for one. Like, you could probably argued he's cursed by something, yeah, if you twist the word curse to the point where it's literally meaningless.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/117-solar","name":"Solar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar117_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1267"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-12T11:25:43-07:00","id":512155,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Erinys</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/507138-would-exigents-suffer-the-great-curse?p=512015#post512015\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">the human race had a long history of pre-civilization want and privation and oppression coloring their psyches.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm inclined to view the relationship between prehistoric humans in the setting and various non-human races (as well as the ancient Lintha) as not quite following this model.<br /> <br /> More kind of... distant.<br /> <br /> I mean, the Dragon Kings are supposed to have had human &quot;slaves&quot;, but I can't really imagine what they would do with them (apart from the occasional sacrifice to the Sun), because they also had their own labour saving magic.<br /> <br /> If I'm on a roll of taking cues from Debt, I would be inclined to view the Dragon Kings as having human slaves as a form of high prestige currency or unit of account, one in which ownership of and rights to them is traded and managed in the course of tracking various forms of interpersonal relations and transactions, while the actual people themselves stay where they are (confined to certain reservations as a matter of not wanting your prestige property to go running off). Also stuff where you just have them standing around your home to attention for decorative purposes (as well as the occasional entertainment, such as fighting).<br /> <br /> In that case, sacrificing them to the Sun is like a kind of propitiation, like tossing your gold into a river as an offering to your god.<br /> <br /> Similar for the Lintha (they don't really need labour slaves, they've got those Primordial-powered copper automatons), with the addition of them having Melnibone-style weird torture fetishes (as well as some theft from rival Dragon Kings). A bit more unpleasant, but I don't see it as particularly widespread; I imagine the ancient Lintha as only having numbered in the few hundred thousand, maybe a couple million at most, and only a minority of those being the kind of aristocracy that is actually privileged to own such prestige slaves. A lot of people end up escaping to or being abandoned on the Western islands (upon which they return to forager lifestyles), and that's how humans ever got out there.<br /> <br /> But even so, such slaves not only form a minority of humans, they only come from a fairly specific spot with the coastal lands of the Southwest (which is where not many Dragon Kings live anyway, and not the kinds very inclined to keep human slaves in the first place). I picture the vast majority of prehistoric humans as being in the East and South(east).<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-12T11:38:15-07:00","id":512167,"title":"","content":"IDK, I've played more than enough RPGs to know that, in a game with a permissive, let alone an abstract, Morality system, most players will either play their stated morality to the hilt, with no grey area choices, or ignore the system entirely. While Limit Breaks were obviously an attempt to make moral/ethical dilemmas have visceral consequences, they still, IMHO, were a mechanical Band-aid, particularly when the power differential was skewed heavily toward Exalts, particularly Solars and their lost brethren. Hopefully, if the rumors are true, immediate, non-metaphysical consequences for bad behavior, like torch-wielding mobs, with or without Immaculate Monks, or angry Deities, at the head, will be a viable eventuality.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Crunch isn't a hobby; it's a calling.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1959-hexmeister-vic","name":"Hexmeister Vic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1959_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"764"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-12T12:03:53-07:00","id":512184,"title":"","content":"Humans were ruled over by the Dragon Kings, for the most part, and few escaped, at least according to the 1e Player's Guide (which is mostly all I have to go on). But they were oppressed in the sense of having nothing to call their own that wasn't the low-quality leavings of vastly more powerful beings that could kill, torture, or eat them with total impunity. Some spirits and behemoths probably did those things on a whim. Primordials certainly did. Dragon Kings apparently didn't see anything wrong with killing humans, or grasp why this would upset humans at all. And Lintha were probably not the worst of the non-humans -- consider the Mazriki, who fed upon fear. Humans were prey for darn-near everything.<br /> <br /> And they probably lived in privation and terror simply because of all that, and because the world itself was less hospitable to humans physically and metaphysically. Even absent outside oppression, they would have lived no better than the hunter-gatherers who were our own real ancestors -- not necessarily horribly, if they could find some decently fertile land that nobody else wanted, but not a post-scarcity paradise of 100% leisure, nor freedom from random man-eating monsters.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">She/Her. I am literal-minded and write literally. If I don't say something explicitly, please never assume I implied it. The only exception is if I try to make a joke.</span></span></span></div> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">My point of view may be different from yours but is equally valid.</span></span></span><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1x1ycoxJF0G9niMt5D3Pp7owZ7tw8AJvL?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted-cWoD-ArM url mega-library</a>. Exalted <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/663334-random-name-generator\" target=\"_blank\">name-generators</a>.","edited":{"userid":896,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","user":"Erinys","date":". 05-12-2015, 03:08 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","name":"Erinys","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar896_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4235"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-12T13:12:16-07:00","id":512240,"title":"","content":"Mental health is a very sensitive subject, so hope I don't make too many missteps with the following...<br /> <br /> Conan isn't cursed.... but I wonder how many modern shrinks would actually pronounce him a psychologically healthy specimen, with no &quot;inappropriately&quot; extreme personality traits?<br /> <br /> Likewise for Hercules, Elric, Qin Shi Huang, Achilles... all those standard Solar inspiration guys(another model for a Solar might include a certain Galilean fellow who talked about being the son of God).<br /> <br /> I don't know if you can really go into looking at the heroes and villains of pulp, epic and history, the way Exalted intends to tell stories about them, with a modern view of sanity and insanity that places extreme passions and boundless ambition and fatalistic bouts of depression as &quot;insanity&quot;, because then you would end up questioning the kind of protagonists that are intended, or ascribing them as &quot;ill&quot;, whether they are actually like that due to the exaggerating effects of a curse or not. (Hope this doesn't seem like I'm getting all &quot;Dianetics! Don't trust psychiatrists!&quot; on you).<br /> <br /> Like I say, I'm all for the Exalted as heroes, all of them, who labour under a curse, no optionality and choice on that without you breaking from the canon and deciding to defeat it or excise it from the setting in your game, because that is what they have been since the first second of day one. It *should* be a default topic that is always there and in your face unless you decide for it not to be, consciously, I think.<br /> <br /> I do hope though that the mechanics Rob Vance has written up for it in 3e really intentionally allow measures of personal growth, for heroes to conquer and defeat a manifestation of it, even if they will never be clean of it, for heroes to grow spiritually in ways that allow them to put it more at bay. People will love it more if it is a challenge they can do, even if making it totally defeatable should be so obviously a thing to do that people always just do it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-12T16:32:01-07:00","id":512388,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Solar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/507138-would-exigents-suffer-the-great-curse?p=512151#post512151\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Having enemies =/= cursed.</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually, it kinda <i>is</i>. The most basic meaning of the word &quot;curse&quot; is to wish harm on someone. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Come on, the exalted are cursed, literally driven to madness. </div> </div> </div>True, that's the particular stripe of curse that they've been painted.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> There's a massive difference between &quot;I have enemies&quot; and &quot;I am subject to an undetectable, incurable insanity which I was imposed upon me malevolently by another&quot; </div> </div> </div>Is this other who imposed this dread condition\u2026 an enemy? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Loads of heroes aren't cursed. </div> </div> </div>You've yet to successfully name one, let alone &quot;loads,&quot; so pardon me for not taking that on faith.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Loads of heroes who directly inspire exalted aren't cursed. Conan, for one. </div> </div> </div>Hahahaha!<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Robert E. Howard, Beyond the Black River</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Conan moved out of the shadows, scowling. &quot;What the devil are you doing here?\u2014Crom!&quot;<br /> <br /> He half crouched, the flesh prickling along his spine. It was not Balthus who was emerging from the other side of the glade. A weird glow burned through the trees. It moved toward him, shimmering weirdly\u2014a green witchfire that moved with purpose and intent.<br /> <br /> It halted some feet away and Conan glared at it, trying to distinguish its fire-misted outlines. The quivering flame had a solid core; the flame was but a green garment that masked some animate and evil entity; but the Cimmerian was unable to make out its shape or likeness. Then, shockingly, a voice spoke to him from amidst the fiery column.<br /> <br /> &quot;Why do you stand like a sheep waiting for the butcher, Conan?&quot;<br /> <br /> The voice was human but carried strange vibrations that were not human.<br /> <br /> &quot;Sheep?&quot; Conan's wrath got the best of his momentary awe. &quot;Do you think I'm afraid of a damned Pictish swamp devil? A friend called me.&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;I called in his voice,&quot; answered the other. &quot;The men you follow belong to my brother; I would not rob his knife of their blood. But you are mine. O fool, you have come from the far gray hills of Cimmeria to meet your doom in the forests of Conajohara.&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;You've had your chance at me before now,&quot; snorted Conan. &quot;Why didn't you kill me then, if you could?&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;My brother had not painted a skull black for you and hurled it into the fire that burns for ever on Gullah's black altar. He had not whispered your name to the black ghosts that haunt the uplands of the Dark Land. But a bat has flown over the Mountains of the Dead and drawn your image in blood on the white tiger's hide that hangs before the long hut where sleep the Four Brothers of the Night. The great serpents coil about their feet and the stars burn like fireflies in their hair.&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;Why have the gods of darkness doomed me to death?&quot; growled Conan.<br /> <br /> Something\u2014a hand, foot or talon, he could not tell which, thrust out from the fire and marked swiftly on the mold. A symbol blazed there, marked with fire, and faded, but not before he recognized it.<br /> <br /> &quot;You dared make the sign which only a priest of Jhebbal Sag dare make. Thunder rumbled through the black Mountain of the Dead and the altar-hut of Gullah was thrown down by a wind from the Gulf of Ghosts. The loon which is messenger to the Four Brothers of the Night flew swiftly and whispered your name in my ear. Your race is run. You are a dead man already. Your head will hang in the altar-hut of my brother. Your body will be eaten by the black- winged, sharp-beaked Children of Jhil.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Like, you could probably argued he's cursed by something, yeah, if you twist the word curse to the point where it's literally meaningless. </div> </div> </div>No, it's you who's twisted the word &quot;curse&quot; around to the point where it can only apply to exactly one thing in all of existence, which makes it pretty useless as a word.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":177,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","user":"TheCountAlucard","date":". 05-12-2015, 08:39 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-12T18:41:17-07:00","id":512442,"title":"","content":"To Solar:<br /> <br /> I entirely understand your point, and your reluctance to accept the Great Curse as a thing. I entirely understand the personal reasons for it you outlined earlier in the thread. I also understand that you might at this moment feel antagonized, so let me first assure you that's not my intent before I make my point.<br /> <br /> I entirely agree that the Great Curse has not been modeled well mechanically. I don't necessarily agree with you on why it is not modeled well--I suspect that were you and I presented with alternate models we would disagree quite a bit on which is more acceptable. You have stated, in a roundabout sort of way, that you don't care for the Great Curse because it models mental illness that take control of one's character away from the player. I'm sure you have other reasons too, but I'd like to use this one as a specific point.<br /> <br /> I used to play D&amp;D quite heavily, and while I still enjoy the game itself on occasion, I have found over the years that it encourages a specific style of play that I do not care for. I have made this point in other venues before: D&amp;D presents a combat simulator with a few extraneous rules added on, and from the very beginning the game has intended to model a very specific &quot;kick in door, kill monsters, get loot, achieve plot coupon, get XPs&quot; style of game. It CAN be played in other ways, but the way the rules are designed and the way the books are presented, this is the game as it is clearly intended and this is the game that a new player sees when they pick up and play the game, sans experience with other games. This tends to color the experience and the actions of new players, as they tend to take up the mantle of whatever they idealize their character as, be it the superintelligent wizard of ultimate power, the brave and unflappable fighter, the shifty rogue, whatever. The point is that they idealize these characters, because the game supports it and in fact in some ways almost tells you to.<br /> <br /> By the same token, other games are presented differently. Vampire: the Masquerade presents a setting full of political intrigue and the slow, inexorable slide into monstrosity, and while many players eschew focusing too heavily on that latter part, it is nonetheless presented front and center as one of the primary themes of the game. Mage: the Ascension is a game of creativity and discovery, where the primary focus is on learning and exploring a world you are just beginning to understand.<br /> <br /> Exalted, on the other hand, attempts to model, via the Great Curse, a world where heroes are tragic and flawed. It forces you to accept, from the first time you build your character, that your character will, on occasion, act in ways that are counterproductive or detrimental to their goals and those of their allies. It is an attempt--an attempt that I believe did not succeed entirely, but that still nonetheless has merit--to tell the player who first picks up Exalted that your character, no matter how great, epic, and 'perfect' they may be, has flaws, and that those flaws will express themselves whether you want them to or not, because this is a game ABOUT flawed heroes and the mistakes they make, not a game about perfectly succeeding at every task one after another with no complication, even if your magic kind of supports trying to do exactly that. But that's the point of a flawed hero: no matter how powerful you are, it is your own failures that will bring you down in the end, if nothing else does.<br /> <br /> I've spoken on this topic before, on the old forums. The existence of the Great Curse is important precisely BECAUSE it makes it clear that one of the core central questions of the game is how will you learn to manage those flaws, given that those who came before you fell to them?<br /> <br /> I can entirely understand, as I said, why you might not personally like it. Why you, and others, may feel it is unnecessary for the game, even. But you are all experienced roleplayers, I presume, who have also played quite a bit of Exalted. You have made your decisions about whether you want to represent that flawed and tragic heroism in your games, and if so how you want to go about it. Perhaps you feel that you can do so without an external curse involved, perhaps you feel you don't want to do so at all. Both of those are valid viewpoints.<br /> <br /> But the existence of the Curse, in some form or another, is important to the game itself because it makes the statement, right up front, that your heroes are not flawless, they are not perfect, even if they believe they are, and they are going to have moments where they act in ways that may even come off as scary or monstrous or weak sometimes. Whether you use the Curse or not, whether you like how it is implemented or not, I believe, personally, that having it as a part of the game, even if it is not as well mechanically represented as I might personally like, is important, because that statement is part of what forms the core of Exalted's theme, of heroes that can do great things, but that sometimes, great things can be horrible things all at the same time.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5771,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5771-krata-lightblade","user":"Krata Lightblade","date":".  Minor point needed clarifying. 05-12-2015, 09:43 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5771-krata-lightblade","name":"Krata Lightblade","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5771_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"72"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-12T18:57:16-07:00","id":512454,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zelbinnean</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/507138-would-exigents-suffer-the-great-curse?p=511895#post511895\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is per se less human.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hmm, okay, I think we're hitting into a fundamental philosophical disagreement then.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5488-goldfaction","name":"goldfaction","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"90"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-12T19:01:00-07:00","id":512455,"title":"","content":"Kind of a tangent but I'm not an experienced player. I have only ever had a chance to play 2 sessions of Exalted, at a convention, with a pre-gen. I don't know if I will ever get another chance to play the game in my life. But I didn't have any limit breaks in those two sessions, nor did I gain much limit. I got way more milage out of playing up my character's near-total lack of Temperance, and getting my circle into trouble that way. Unlike a limit break, I had actual control over how this manifested, and my character's free will didn't suddenly evaporate for X scenes. He just acted on his counterproductive priorities, and annoyed the high-Temperance Eclipse a lot.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">She/Her. I am literal-minded and write literally. If I don't say something explicitly, please never assume I implied it. The only exception is if I try to make a joke.</span></span></span></div> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">My point of view may be different from yours but is equally valid.</span></span></span><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1x1ycoxJF0G9niMt5D3Pp7owZ7tw8AJvL?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted-cWoD-ArM url mega-library</a>. Exalted <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/663334-random-name-generator\" target=\"_blank\">name-generators</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","name":"Erinys","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar896_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4235"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-12T19:14:22-07:00","id":512459,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>goldfaction</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/507138-would-exigents-suffer-the-great-curse?p=512454#post512454\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hmm, okay, I think we're hitting into a fundamental philosophical disagreement then.</div> </div> </div> </div>I guess, though I don't get how it's contentious to say &quot;if regular humans frequently act irrationally and destructively (which, objectively, they do), and if Solars can magically modify themselves to act irrationally and destructively much less frequently than regular humans do, then Solars who modify themselves thusly per se act less human.&quot; I think that's a sound logical proof.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-12T19:16:28-07:00","id":512460,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Erinys</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/507138-would-exigents-suffer-the-great-curse?p=512455#post512455\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">my character's free will didn't suddenly evaporate for X scenes.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah this is a real problem with previous iterations of Limit Break. If it wants to model the tragic flaws of heroes it should be an urge to act certain ways that are <i>hard </i>to resist, or penalze you if you choose to resist, but aren't basically character-takeover mechanics in the same vein as D&amp;D's Dominate Person.<br /> <br /> In the same breath I hated Partial Control mechanics, because if you want characters to have epic tragic flaws, the last thing you should give them is a milquetoast cop-out for those flaws.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-12T19:22:09-07:00","id":512462,"title":"","content":"It doesn't help that each virtue gets a grand total of 2-3 sample flaws in the corebook. Since mine was a pre-gen at a convention, the ST felt limited to use the corebook flaws, so I had one that made no sense at all for my character. I enjoyed getting into character with him, so much so that I took his character sheet home. But if his limit had broken? I would have shrugged and handed control over to the ST because I could not have figured out how to play out that limit break for that character.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">She/Her. I am literal-minded and write literally. If I don't say something explicitly, please never assume I implied it. The only exception is if I try to make a joke.</span></span></span></div> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">My point of view may be different from yours but is equally valid.</span></span></span><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1x1ycoxJF0G9niMt5D3Pp7owZ7tw8AJvL?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted-cWoD-ArM url mega-library</a>. Exalted <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/663334-random-name-generator\" target=\"_blank\">name-generators</a>.","edited":{"userid":896,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","user":"Erinys","date":". 05-12-2015, 10:42 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","name":"Erinys","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar896_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4235"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-12T20:08:00-07:00","id":512497,"title":"","content":"My apologies, then Erinyes, but the statement I made I do believe still remains: while mechanically represented poorly, the inclusion of the concept in some mechanical form does force players to acknowledge the idea one way or another.<br /> <br /> It could stand to be handled better, absolutely. But supporting the theme of &quot;heroes with tragic flaws&quot; (I'm using that phrase as a paraphrase for more complicated ideas, mind you) right up front during character creation is important.<br /> <br /> Admittedly, Erinyes, I feel your introduction might've been a bit different than the norm, since I tend to feel most people who get into a game are introduced by friends or pick up the book and read it themselves first, and in those cases the mechanics of character creation tells the person a lot, consciously or not, about what kinds of character they're going to be playing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5771-krata-lightblade","name":"Krata Lightblade","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5771_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"72"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-12T20:21:29-07:00","id":512502,"title":"","content":"Hm... well I got the 1e corebook years before I ever had that chance to play.<br /> No need to apologize btw!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">She/Her. I am literal-minded and write literally. If I don't say something explicitly, please never assume I implied it. The only exception is if I try to make a joke.</span></span></span></div> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">My point of view may be different from yours but is equally valid.</span></span></span><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1x1ycoxJF0G9niMt5D3Pp7owZ7tw8AJvL?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted-cWoD-ArM url mega-library</a>. Exalted <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/663334-random-name-generator\" target=\"_blank\">name-generators</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","name":"Erinys","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar896_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4235"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-13T00:13:58-07:00","id":512685,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/507138-would-exigents-suffer-the-great-curse?p=512388#post512388\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Actually, it kinda <i>is</i>. The most basic meaning of the word &quot;curse&quot; is to wish harm on someone.<br /> <br /> True, that's the particular stripe of curse that they've been painted.<br /> <br /> Is this other who imposed this dread condition\u2026 an enemy? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> You've yet to successfully name one, let alone &quot;loads,&quot; so pardon me for not taking that on faith.<br /> <br /> Hahahaha!<br /> <br /> No, it's you who's twisted the word &quot;curse&quot; around to the point where it can only apply to exactly one thing in all of existence, which makes it pretty useless as a word.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, look. I disagree pretty much entirely with what you're saying, don't really care that you disagree with what I am saying, and I think your definition of curse is entirely useless.<br /> <br /> I also think you're being antagonistic and it's winding me up. So I am dropping this subject with you right now.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/117-solar","name":"Solar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar117_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1267"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-13T00:27:19-07:00","id":512688,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Solar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/507138-would-exigents-suffer-the-great-curse?p=512685#post512685\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I disagree pretty much entirely with what you're saying\u2026</div> </div> </div> </div>You're welcome to disagree with me.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Solar</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u2026don't really care that you disagree with what I am saying\u2026</div> </div> </div> </div>Congratulatons! <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Solar</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u2026and I think your definition of curse is entirely useless.</div> </div> </div> </div>Disagreeing with the dictionary is less fine by me, because it makes discussion difficult; don't go jumping out any windows to try and argue the definition of gravity.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dictionary.com, &quot;curse&quot;</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">1. the expression of a wish that misfortune, evil, doom, etc., befall a person, group, etc.<br /> 2. a formula or charm intended to cause such misfortune to another.</div> </div> </div> </div>Don't see anything about undetectable incurable insanity imposed by the death-utterances of the Makers of All That Is.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Solar</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u2026it's winding me up. So I am dropping this subject with you right now.</div> </div> </div> </div>I thought you said you didn't care.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":177,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","user":"TheCountAlucard","date":". 05-13-2015, 03:32 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-13T00:30:12-07:00","id":512690,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Krata Lightblade</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/507138-would-exigents-suffer-the-great-curse?p=512442#post512442\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To Solar:<br /> <br /> I entirely understand your point, and your reluctance to accept the Great Curse as a thing. I entirely understand the personal reasons for it you outlined earlier in the thread. I also understand that you might at this moment feel antagonized, so let me first assure you that's not my intent before I make my point.<br /> <br /> I entirely agree that the Great Curse has not been modeled well mechanically. I don't necessarily agree with you on why it is not modeled well--I suspect that were you and I presented with alternate models we would disagree quite a bit on which is more acceptable. You have stated, in a roundabout sort of way, that you don't care for the Great Curse because it models mental illness that take control of one's character away from the player. I'm sure you have other reasons too, but I'd like to use this one as a specific point.<br /> <br /> I used to play D&amp;D quite heavily, and while I still enjoy the game itself on occasion, I have found over the years that it encourages a specific style of play that I do not care for. I have made this point in other venues before: D&amp;D presents a combat simulator with a few extraneous rules added on, and from the very beginning the game has intended to model a very specific &quot;kick in door, kill monsters, get loot, achieve plot coupon, get XPs&quot; style of game. It CAN be played in other ways, but the way the rules are designed and the way the books are presented, this is the game as it is clearly intended and this is the game that a new player sees when they pick up and play the game, sans experience with other games. This tends to color the experience and the actions of new players, as they tend to take up the mantle of whatever they idealize their character as, be it the superintelligent wizard of ultimate power, the brave and unflappable fighter, the shifty rogue, whatever. The point is that they idealize these characters, because the game supports it and in fact in some ways almost tells you to.<br /> <br /> By the same token, other games are presented differently. Vampire: the Masquerade presents a setting full of political intrigue and the slow, inexorable slide into monstrosity, and while many players eschew focusing too heavily on that latter part, it is nonetheless presented front and center as one of the primary themes of the game. Mage: the Ascension is a game of creativity and discovery, where the primary focus is on learning and exploring a world you are just beginning to understand.<br /> <br /> Exalted, on the other hand, attempts to model, via the Great Curse, a world where heroes are tragic and flawed. It forces you to accept, from the first time you build your character, that your character will, on occasion, act in ways that are counterproductive or detrimental to their goals and those of their allies. It is an attempt--an attempt that I believe did not succeed entirely, but that still nonetheless has merit--to tell the player who first picks up Exalted that your character, no matter how great, epic, and 'perfect' they may be, has flaws, and that those flaws will express themselves whether you want them to or not, because this is a game ABOUT flawed heroes and the mistakes they make, not a game about perfectly succeeding at every task one after another with no complication, even if your magic kind of supports trying to do exactly that. But that's the point of a flawed hero: no matter how powerful you are, it is your own failures that will bring you down in the end, if nothing else does.<br /> <br /> I've spoken on this topic before, on the old forums. The existence of the Great Curse is important precisely BECAUSE it makes it clear that one of the core central questions of the game is how will you learn to manage those flaws, given that those who came before you fell to them?<br /> <br /> I can entirely understand, as I said, why you might not personally like it. Why you, and others, may feel it is unnecessary for the game, even. But you are all experienced roleplayers, I presume, who have also played quite a bit of Exalted. You have made your decisions about whether you want to represent that flawed and tragic heroism in your games, and if so how you want to go about it. Perhaps you feel that you can do so without an external curse involved, perhaps you feel you don't want to do so at all. Both of those are valid viewpoints.<br /> <br /> But the existence of the Curse, in some form or another, is important to the game itself because it makes the statement, right up front, that your heroes are not flawless, they are not perfect, even if they believe they are, and they are going to have moments where they act in ways that may even come off as scary or monstrous or weak sometimes. Whether you use the Curse or not, whether you like how it is implemented or not, I believe, personally, that having it as a part of the game, even if it is not as well mechanically represented as I might personally like, is important, because that statement is part of what forms the core of Exalted's theme, of heroes that can do great things, but that sometimes, great things can be horrible things all at the same time.</div> </div> </div> </div>I just feel that the system of the Great Curse takes so much away from the characters and the setting, though. Like, I understand that people want to play flawed, tragic heroes (some want tragedy more than others, mind, flaws =/= tragic), but at the same time, I imagine that not a lot of those people actually know what it's like to not be stable, emotionally, and to not know why that is the case. The Great Curse, to me, basically is the affliction of your character with emotional instability at the point of Exaltation. Much as it can be dressed up as the mythic passion of a demigod, it's still essentially a form of emotional instability which your character will never be rid of.<br /> <br /> That is not fun. I have that, in real life, and it was not worth the build points I got back. I don't mind playing a flawed character, because I get that Exalted is very much about flawed characters. What I mind is the way that the system takes control away from your character and forces, clumsily, for you to act in certain ways because your character is demonstrably anything between slightly to very unstable, even if you never intended them to be that. That's not something that the genre demands, by the way, that's something that the Great Curse demands.<br /> <br /> The Great Curse plays various roles in the game. It provides an excuse for the excesses of the First Age and Usurpation without making them a statement on the human condition, and it forces people to play &quot;flawed, tragic&quot; (read: emotionally unstable) characters in some vein of genre emulation. I don't think either of those things require the Great Curse at all, and again I kind of feel that if I wanted to play a game where my character has wildly uncontrolled emotional reactions then I'd step outside my front door. It's not nice, it's not fun, and it's not needed. I tend to be able to tolerate systems like the Great Curse in most games, but the Great Curse itself has always been just a big hot mess; in concept, in execution and in the gameplay it results in.<br /> <br /> If the Great Curse in 3e doesn't take away control of your character from you, I'll be considerably more amenable to it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/117-solar","name":"Solar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar117_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1267"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-13T00:31:29-07:00","id":512691,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/507138-would-exigents-suffer-the-great-curse?p=512688#post512688\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You're welcome to disagree with me.<br /> <br /> Congratulatons!<br /> <br /> Disagreeing with the dictionary is less fine by me, because it makes discussion difficult; don't go jumping out any windows to try and argue the definition of gravity.<br /> <br /> I thought you said you didn't care.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't. Emotionally, you have vexed me. Rationally, I do not care to continue this one single bit.<br /> <br /> I am dropping this with you again now","signature":"","edited":{"userid":117,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/117-solar","user":"Solar","date":". 05-13-2015, 03:34 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/117-solar","name":"Solar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar117_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1267"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-13T00:34:30-07:00","id":512695,"title":"","content":"So what you're saying is, you don't care\u2026 but it's winding you up?<br /> <br /> Something about that doesn't feel right.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-13T01:01:53-07:00","id":512715,"title":"","content":"I think we're playing different games, Solar, 'cuz I wish I'd gotten points back for the flaws I wound up with in my character creation.<br /> <br /> ..Sorry, I've a weird sense of humor sometime.<br /> <br /> Regardless, I entirely understand your point, and as I said I entirely agree that the way it's handled now is... less than ideal.<br /> <br /> I simply feel that while I agree that nothing in the Exalted canon necessarily requires the Great Curse and cannot be done without it (barring Curse-interactive Charm mechanics, for you pedants out there), I do feel that the statement it makes to a new player who picks up the books fresh for the very first time is a valuable one, whether that player understands that statement consciously or not.<br /> <br /> I'd also like to see it be a great deal less &quot;so you turned down a fight at 9 Limit, lol now you fight everything&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5771-krata-lightblade","name":"Krata Lightblade","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5771_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"72"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-13T01:23:40-07:00","id":512720,"title":"","content":"A system that does not make you do anything but rewards you for choosing for your character to be irrational was posited earlier in the thread, I think that could be good.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/117-solar","name":"Solar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar117_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1267"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-13T03:33:57-07:00","id":512789,"title":"","content":"I feel as though shortcomings and failings, whether they be from intrinsic character qualities such as curses or matters of being harangued or manipulated, should fit logically into the scene and the characterisation, but I find the idea that bad things happening to characters should be compensated or players consenting to go along with them being rewarded to be odd in this kind of system in genre.<br /> <br /> Not in all of them, mind, I think highly of the World of Darkness idea of getting Beats when the player opts in to making their failures worse or experience psychological breaks, or the level of collaboration inherent to things like Afflictions and Wounds in Nobilis.<br /> <br /> But for Exalted... I just feel as though a hit is a hit, and you need to roll for it.<br /> <br /> I still take the developers at their word when they say that the Great Curse isn't going to be as abrupt and inorganic as it was in prior Editions.<br /> <br /> I'd also like it if, in terms of description and function, it leaned closer to the idea of a mythically integrated tendency for extreme personality, overconfidence or obsession, or self-defeating decisions (for a given value of self-defeat, such as managing to conquer the empire by walking over the ruins of broken relationships) rather than a kind of quasi-mental illness.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-13T03:48:45-07:00","id":512794,"title":"","content":"[QUOTE=Erinys;n512184<br /> <br /> And they probably lived in privation and terror simply because of all that, and because the world itself was less hospitable to humans physically and metaphysically. Even absent outside oppression, they would have lived no better than the hunter-gatherers who were our own real ancestors -- not necessarily horribly, if they could find some decently fertile land that nobody else wanted, but not a post-scarcity paradise of 100% leisure, nor freedom from random man-eating monsters.[/QUOTE]<br /> <br /> Forager societies weren't post-scarcity, no, but a lot of modern anthropological evidence is finding that they may have been a lot better off then they have typically been given credit for.<br /> <br /> Matters of better nutrition, more diverse diet, generally healthy lifestyle, good interpersonal relationships, and a lot of free time in which to devise and engage in music, art, storytelling, games and sex.<br /> <br /> Not a paradise, but what is (and why should I want it)?<br /> <br /> I'm just finding myself compelled by the idea that the difference between humans before and after the Exalted is less &quot;Hebrews in and out of Egypt&quot; and more &quot;humans during and after the Ice Age&quot;, in which the existence and reign of certain monster peoples and their desire to use (non-Kimbery bred) humans as a kind of currency is standing in for environmental conditions in terms of preventing certain population concentrations that allow for particular kinds of developments.<br /> <br /> I mean, maybe a degree of oppression, but kind of in the form of &quot;if we built watchtowers and walls to help forecast dangerous weather or keep out unwanted animals, the Dragon Kings would be annoyed at us messing up their arrangements of us, assuming they don't just incidentally clear away our constructions with their powers in pursuit of their own things&quot;.<br /> <br /> (But they still employ tools like fur scrapers and sewing needles and shovels and hammers and ladders and wedges and levers and ropes and pulleys and all kinds of things that are unobtrusive enough that the Dragon Kings just view them as quaint while Autochthon falls in love over them)<br /> <br /> In contrast to the Age of Sorrows, in which there's a whole huge background of ideas and institutions and developed products in which the easiest way to compete and deal with Dragon Kings is probably to offer to sell them a fancy mask and come up with a secret society that they can pay to join, fostering a sense of dependence.<br /> <br /> That, incidentally, is the kind of thing I mean when I say I think the legacy of the Exalted created a more substantive way for humans to compete with gods and monsters then giving them the ability to manipulate Essence.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-13T07:31:14-07:00","id":512902,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/507138-would-exigents-suffer-the-great-curse?p=512794#post512794\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Forager societies weren't post-scarcity, no, but a lot of modern anthropological evidence is finding that they may have been a lot better off then they have typically been given credit for.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah, <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Original_affluent_society\" target=\"_blank\">that's the term</a>; not &quot;post scarcity&quot; but affluent/refined form of subsistence.<br /> <br /> Just imagine, if people had ever been able to sustain the infrastructure for constructing ziggurats in honour of their gods and elevation of the priesthood without the need for converting large sections of the populace into dedicated farmers to provide the necessary food surplus, what kind of society could have resulted?<br /> <br /> We don't know in Exalted, because their heroes were cursed! They wind up with an uncomfortably close approximation of the mess that we're in.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-13T08:23:34-07:00","id":512933,"title":"","content":"One last re:Solar\u2026<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Solar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/507138-would-exigents-suffer-the-great-curse?p=512685#post512685\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I also think you're being antagonistic\u2026</div> </div> </div> </div><i>You're </i>the one who entered into this particular discussion with, and I quote\u2026<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Solar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/507138-would-exigents-suffer-the-great-curse?p=512059#post512059\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's bullshit.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u2026in regard to an element of the game that at least some of us obviously like (albeit perhaps less so the execution). <i>I'm</i> antagonistic?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":177,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","user":"TheCountAlucard","date":". 05-13-2015, 11:53 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-13T09:31:21-07:00","id":512998,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/507138-would-exigents-suffer-the-great-curse?p=512789#post512789\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I feel as though shortcomings and failings, whether they be from intrinsic character qualities such as curses or matters of being harangued or manipulated, should fit logically into the scene and the characterisation, but I find the idea that bad things happening to characters should be compensated or players consenting to go along with them being rewarded to be odd in this kind of system in genre.<br /> <br /> Not in all of them, mind, I think highly of the World of Darkness idea of getting Beats when the player opts in to making their failures worse or experience psychological breaks, or the level of collaboration inherent to things like Afflictions and Wounds in Nobilis.<br /> <br /> But for Exalted... I just feel as though a hit is a hit, and you need to roll for it.<br /> <br /> I still take the developers at their word when they say that the Great Curse isn't going to be as abrupt and inorganic as it was in prior Editions.<br /> <br /> I'd also like it if, in terms of description and function, it leaned closer to the idea of a mythically integrated tendency for extreme personality, overconfidence or obsession, or self-defeating decisions (for a given value of self-defeat, such as managing to conquer the empire by walking over the ruins of broken relationships) rather than a kind of quasi-mental illness.</div> </div> </div> </div>I definitely agree with you in the sense that I have always believed that system very much matters (this goes both ways, though; I've never been persuaded that losing control of your character in Exalted is okay because that's what Vampire does, we aren't playing Vampire after all).<br /> <br /> However, I don't think Exalted should be taking away control of your character because &quot;a hit is a hit&quot; either. Losing control sucks, it takes you out of the game, it always makes a game prone to impromptu disaster, and it feels like a punishment, a negative gameplay experience. In a horror game that can work, in an exciting mythic fantasy game it doesn't for me. And even in those horror games; death rage is known to werewolves, managing it shapes their society and behavior.<br /> <br /> The great curse always had the tone of a cheap trick to me. Your character is literally driven crazy by this, but you can't solve it, you can't avoid it, you can't even detect that it exists! Managing it feels like metagaming, but not managing it can shit all over you at the worst time. Much as tragic heroes are cool to read about, they can be pretty tiresome and unenjoyable to play, especially when they are the only option!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/117-solar","name":"Solar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar117_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1267"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-13T12:06:23-07:00","id":513194,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/507138-would-exigents-suffer-the-great-curse?p=512388#post512388\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Actually, it kinda <i>is</i>. The most basic meaning of the word &quot;curse&quot; is to wish harm on someone.</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually it kinda <i>isn't.</i> A square is a rectangle, a rectangle is not a square. If you are cursed, you probably have an enemy. If you have an enemy, it does not mean you are cursed.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Is this other who imposed this dread condition\u2026 an enemy? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> </div> </div> </div>Doesn't matter.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> You've yet to successfully name one, let alone &quot;loads,&quot; so pardon me for not taking that on faith. </div> </div> </div>Achilles.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> No, it's you who's twisted the word &quot;curse&quot; around to the point where it can only apply to exactly one thing in all of existence, which makes it pretty useless as a word. </div> </div> </div>Not really. Solar's definition is much closer than yours.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/697-arteliex","name":"Arteliex","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar697_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"591"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-13T12:35:55-07:00","id":513232,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/507138-would-exigents-suffer-the-great-curse?p=512695#post512695\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So what you're saying is, you don't care\u2026 but it's winding you up?<br /> <br /> Something about that doesn't feel right.</div> </div> </div> </div><b><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Please leave the thread.</span></b><br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-13T15:02:11-07:00","id":513344,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Arteliex</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Achilles.</div> </div> </div> </div> He kind of is, given certain Greek ideas behind fate and the cosmic reasoning for the downfall of heroes. That's part of why they're a big inspiration behind the Great Curse in general. <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Solar</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've never been persuaded that losing control of your character in Exalted is okay because that's what Vampire does, we aren't playing Vampire after all</div> </div> </div> </div> I don't think it should be about losing control of your character, but I do think there can be a measure of definition in what one controls their character to do. I mean, even if you take out the Great Curse, that's going to be present in the social system, which I think may be the hook for the Great Curse anyway. I mean, what if instead of periodically losing control of your character, it played out like having an ephemeral force that could leverage one of your Intimacies to persuade you to do ill-advised things that still play off of the character's personality and aspirations, something that actual characters can do anyway?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-13T15:15:42-07:00","id":513351,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Arteliex</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/507138-would-exigents-suffer-the-great-curse?p=513194#post513194\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Achilles.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Right, because prophecy of an early death is not<i> at all</i> like a curse.<br /> <br /> Only hero I can think of with no curse of any kind is Diomedes, but that was kind of his whole thing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>SWTOR Referal: <a href=\"http://www.swtor.com/r/JQ2nqy\" target=\"_blank\">http://www.swtor.com/r/JQ2nqy</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/414-gallus","name":"Gallus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar414_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"886"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-13T15:33:08-07:00","id":513361,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Arteliex</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/507138-would-exigents-suffer-the-great-curse?p=513194#post513194\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Achilles.</div> </div> </div> </div>While we are at it:<br /> <br /> Herakles: Killed his family while drunk<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252525\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Yudhisthira: Lost his kingdom, brothers, and wife in a rigged dice game. (Many rolls involved)</span></span></span><br /> <br /> Sun Wukong: Lets start with wreaking heaven and let the rest of the story stand for itself.<br /> <br /> Gilgamesh: Kills Humbaba and generally pisses of the gods because of his pride leading to the death of his best friend<br /> <br /> Norse Gods in general: Bet Freya to some unknown builder because they didn't think he could build Valhala in three months. Then lost.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1144,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1144-exthalion","user":"Exthalion","date":". 05-14-2015, 02:35 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1144-exthalion","name":"Exthalion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1144_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2306"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-13T15:59:32-07:00","id":513377,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/507138-would-exigents-suffer-the-great-curse?p=513344#post513344\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> He kind of is, given certain Greek ideas behind fate and the cosmic reasoning for the downfall of heroes. That's part of why they're a big inspiration behind the Great Curse in general. I don't think it should be about losing control of your character, but I do think there can be a measure of definition in what one controls their character to do. I mean, even if you take out the Great Curse, that's going to be present in the social system, which I think may be the hook for the Great Curse anyway. I mean, what if instead of periodically losing control of your character, it played out like having an ephemeral force that could leverage one of your Intimacies to persuade you to do ill-advised things that still play off of the character's personality and aspirations, something that actual characters can do anyway?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm definitely willing to admit that a lot of my problems with the Great Curse stem from it's awful mechanics in the previous editions which led to very poor gameplay experiences. I won't say that I think without those poor mechanics I'd be okay with it as a setting element, I wouldn't, because I feel is does nothing for the setting but rather takes away from the responsibility that the Exalted have for their actions, from their agency (as an Exalted you have, arguably, less control over yourself than a mortal does in many ways) and from the vision of a future you might have. However, I'd be considerably more amenable towards it as a gameplay element if it wasn't, for once, written very poorly as a mechanic.<br /> <br /> Grabowski seems far more enamoured with the Curse than I really claim to see the reasoning behind. But he's making the game, I suppose, now me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/117-solar","name":"Solar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar117_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1267"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-13T16:28:39-07:00","id":513447,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Solar</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">their agency</div> </div> </div> </div> Agency is a funny thing. Like what I said before, about how Hitler can be held responsible for the Holocaust and yet was not the inventor of anti-semtism. It gets quite ambiguous when applied to something in which the morality is not so clear cut, such as imperialism or modern capitalism. For that matter, factors in which our physiology and environment affects the output of our neurology. Agency might be more of a comfortable philosophical concept than a factual one, and even if it is factual, it is constantly compromised by intrinsic and extrinsic factors. <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Solar</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">But he's making the game</div> </div> </div> </div> Not this game, surely? I mean, a prior one...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-13T16:38:16-07:00","id":513459,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/507138-would-exigents-suffer-the-great-curse?p=513447#post513447\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not this game, surely? I mean, a prior one...</div> </div> </div> </div>Geoff Grabowski <i>is</i> on the &quot;developers and key personnel&quot; list in the Ex3 kickstarter description...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:lucida sans unicode\">Bearer of the legacy of Trauma Bear<br /> Need a dice-roller? Check out <a href=\"http://bit.ly/dicemat\" target=\"_blank\">Dicemat</a>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/43-fata-ku","name":"Fata-Ku","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar43_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2240"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-13T16:52:00-07:00","id":513467,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Fata-Ku</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/507138-would-exigents-suffer-the-great-curse?p=513459#post513459\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Geoff Grabowski <i>is</i> on the &quot;developers and key personnel&quot; list in the Ex3 kickstarter description...</div> </div> </div> </div>True, but in more of an advisory capacity than he was before. With the caveat that these quotes are veeeery aged, here's what's in <a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalted_3E:What_We_Know#Geoff_Grabowski\" target=\"_blank\">his section</a> on the Wiki:<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>EX3 What We Know Wiki</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>(hatewheel)</b><br /> I have Geoff doing the chapter fiction for the 3e core.<br /> <br /> <b>(hatewheel)</b><br /> You can consider me the lead developer of 3e. 3e is my direction, my designs for Creation, and my book ideas. I construct my hypotheses with, and draw on the advice of Holden, but at the end of the day it is my conclusions that drive the direction of this game and my outlines that will be sent out to the writers. Grabowski offers invaluable support as someone who has been through the fire and has handled developmental crises from every angle conceivable. He has already given me a ton of valuable advice as well as support in terms of liking my ideas and warning me about the pitfalls and obstacles he faced when he was in my position.<br /> <br /> <b>(hatewheel)</b><br /> That said, Geoff has already had some pretty great input on the Liminals. Specifically capitalizing on the name Chernozem, he suggested a bit of lore that was pure classic Exalted style, and I am going to run with it.<br /> <br /> <b>Q: (Morally ambiguous science)</b><br /> Say, if Geoff Grabowski is coming back with the new edition, does this mean that the fears of Liminals conflicting with his original vision will be unnecessary?<br /> <b>A: (Holden)</b><br /> Oh, he doesn't know about them. We throw a tarp over them and whistle nervously every time he walks by. More seriously, 3e isn't about recreating Geoff's old vision of the game. It's not what we're after and it's not what he's after.<br /> <br /> <b>(Holden)</b><br /> For those curious, Geoff is onboard getting this book put together and launched smoothly, and is lending his legendary talents to the project, but he's not the architect of 3e (although so far he's been enthusiastic about the direction we're taking things in). We're no more interested in selling you First Edition again than we are in selling you Second Edition again-- that would be a big waste of everyone's time and money, I think we can all agree!<br /> <br /> <b>Q: (MissMaddy)</b><br /> What is the formal role of Grabowski on the team?<br /> <b>A: (John M\u00f8rke)</b><br /> He is offering advice, looking over drafts, and doing some writing. I had him write up the money and religion sections of the core. I also had him do some fiction. I am now wrangling him into naming all the new Solar Charms.</div> </div> </div> </div></div></div> </div> </div> (Spoiled for space)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalted_3E:What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">The EX3 What We Know Wiki</a>, courtesy of Marin and JMobius<br /> <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com\" target=\"_blank\">Nishkriya, the EX3 Freelancer Quotes Tracker</a>, courtesy of Anathema and Moonwolf<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The White Wolf Forum Archive</a>, courtesy of The Dark Wizard and Sanctaphrax (see <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/PhilippeSaner?u=159709\" target=\"_blank\">its Patreon</a>) <hr />Arrghus: There's also the Shepherd of the North Star, busily guiding the one thing in all the heavens that <i>doesn't move</i>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","name":"Gaius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-13T16:57:12-07:00","id":513472,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/507138-would-exigents-suffer-the-great-curse?p=513447#post513447\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Agency is a funny thing. Like what I said before, about how Hitler can be held responsible for the Holocaust and yet was not the inventor of anti-semtism. It gets quite ambiguous when applied to something in which the morality is not so clear cut, such as imperialism or modern capitalism. For that matter, factors in which our physiology and environment affects the output of our neurology. Agency might be more of a comfortable philosophical concept than a factual one, and even if it is factual, it is constantly compromised by intrinsic and</div> </div> </div> </div>Much as the whole discussion of what makes us make the decisions we do (and whether they are, indeed, decisions at all) is very interesting, I think we need to keep our eyes on the ball here. This is a <i>game</i>, a game that people want to play and enjoy. Semantic debates about the nature of whether you <i>really</i> decided to make your character do that think don't really help the game. You might as well say that a game of 40K is totally pre-determined based on all of the factors involved; yeah that's a philosophical point which is quite interesting, but it's no reason not to try and play anyway. The difference between character determination and agency and the lack thereof can be very much measured in a practical sense; how much control do you have over the thoughts and feeling of your character?<br /> <br /> Exalted very much takes agency away from your character when you are unable to actually say &quot;my character feels like this,&quot; and not even infrequently! Some agency removal is acceptable, others are not. I don't, typically, mind systems that model things such as fear (though I often find them trite and uninspiring), and in some games that lack of agency seems suitable. In Exalted, however, it does not. I dislike it when my character goes crazy and kills someone despite my distinct desire not to do that. If I am playing Werewolf, sure, but not in Exalted. On a setting level, the Great Curse basically says &quot;well, you might think you can do all this, but you'll eventually fall to madness and fail.&quot; I... don't really want to play that game? That game sounds like an exercise in watching my efforts just turn to shit, if I wanted to watch my efforts turn to shit, I'd try writing screenplays (zing!)<br /> <br /> Yeah, you can approach the Great Curse from a point of view of &quot;well it's not like, in a deterministic universe, you have any agency whatsoever.&quot; At the same time, that's traditionally seen as not a very <i>useful</i> statement for any kind of reasonable discussion.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/117-solar","name":"Solar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar117_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1267"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-13T17:54:50-07:00","id":513515,"title":"","content":"You say it it limits player agency? I say, &quot;<b><i>Good.</i></b>&quot; I will also point out that its does so with <i>greatly</i> varying degrees and intervals. In fact, the Virtues did more to limit a players agency than the Great Curse. You only had so much Willpower to let you do what you want. It should be noted the Virtues are not in 3e.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>SWTOR Referal: <a href=\"http://www.swtor.com/r/JQ2nqy\" target=\"_blank\">http://www.swtor.com/r/JQ2nqy</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/414-gallus","name":"Gallus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar414_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"886"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-13T18:14:32-07:00","id":513554,"title":"","content":"I think with the comparisons with mental illness we're sort of touching on the core difficulty here - ancient mythic vs. modern scientific-esque conceptions of humanity and the world. The two don't necessarily mesh, or at least need an oblique way of looking at things to mesh.<br /> <br /> Similarly with the question of whether it's redundant with the human tendency for power to corrupt.... not exactly, I think. Rather, the Great Curse is human flaws as seen through the lens of myth and tragedy, as seen through the lens of a game.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5488-goldfaction","name":"goldfaction","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"90"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-13T18:19:37-07:00","id":513556,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zelbinnean</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/507138-would-exigents-suffer-the-great-curse?p=512459#post512459\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I guess, though I don't get how it's contentious to say &quot;if regular humans frequently act irrationally and destructively (which, objectively, they do), and if Solars can magically modify themselves to act irrationally and destructively much less frequently than regular humans do, then Solars who modify themselves thusly per se act less human.&quot; I think that's a sound logical proof.</div> </div> </div> </div>It actually depends on what you mean by &quot;less human&quot;, If you mean &quot;farther from the average of all humans&quot;, definitely! If you mean &quot;farther from the ideal of being human&quot; in an Aristotelian or Platonic sense, I would strongly disagree.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5488-goldfaction","name":"goldfaction","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"90"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-13T18:19:46-07:00","id":513557,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Solar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/507138-would-exigents-suffer-the-great-curse?p=513472#post513472\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In Exalted, however, it does not. I dislike it when my character goes crazy and kills someone despite my distinct desire not to do that. If I am playing Werewolf, sure, but not in Exalted.</div> </div> </div> </div>I consider this more of an issue with implementation than with the overall &quot;you're a cursed hero&quot; conceit. There are certainly ways to make that conceit interesting while also not forcing something equivalent to Frenzy, which unfortunately past eds basically did. And some of the Limit Breaks are just plain awful from a gameplay perspective (looking at you, Ascetic Drive).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Solar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/507138-would-exigents-suffer-the-great-curse?p=513472#post513472\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">On a setting level, the Great Curse basically says &quot;well, you might think you can do all this, but you'll eventually fall to madness and fail.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>This is again a really frustrating narrative conceit that has shit-all mechanical support, which given the superheavy mechanical system for Exalted is incredibly frustrating (&quot;<i>this</i> is what you chose to go rules-light on?!&quot;). Which is unfortunate since it's the greater setting-level thing that is the overwhelming narrative problem than the actual Limit Break episodes. At the same time, the narrative-level curse is only a practical problem for games if your ST is a fiat-happy dick; the individual Break-level is likely to be far more disruptive to actual play.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":3420,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","user":"Zelbinnean","date":". 05-13-2015, 09:22 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-13T18:25:36-07:00","id":513561,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gallus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/507138-would-exigents-suffer-the-great-curse?p=513351#post513351\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Right, because prophecy of an early death is not<i> at all</i> like a curse.<br /> <br /> Only hero I can think of with no curse of any kind is Diomedes, but that was kind of his whole thing.</div> </div> </div> </div>While being told that you will die early is tragic, its hardly a curse. There would be many mortals in Creation that could get their destiny read, and it may tell them they will die soon. They aren't cursed though, its just their lot in Fate.<br /> <br /> The Exalted, on the other hand, were actually cursed, magically, by the creators. I think there's quite a bit of difference there.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/697-arteliex","name":"Arteliex","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar697_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"591"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-13T20:14:17-07:00","id":513665,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Arteliex</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/507138-would-exigents-suffer-the-great-curse?p=513561#post513561\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> While being told that you will die early is tragic, its hardly a curse. There would be many mortals in Creation that could get their destiny read, and it may tell them they will die soon. They aren't cursed though, its just their lot in Fate.<br /> <br /> The Exalted, on the other hand, were actually cursed, magically, by the creators. I think there's quite a bit of difference there.</div> </div> </div> </div>If you ignore all of the themes and concepts of fate in Greek mythos, then yes. The closest analog to Greek fate in Exalted is Samsara, not Destiny. <i>Nothing</i> changes fate in Greek mythos, not even the gods themselves. A mortal's Destiny can be change by an Exalted farting at the right time (it's a thing that actually happend, don't ask).<br /> <br /> Achilles fate was to die, and even the greatest magics could do nothing to stop it.<br /> <br /> A terrible, unavoidable fate, is very much<i> like</i> a curse. Which is why I used a (sarcastic) simili.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>SWTOR Referal: <a href=\"http://www.swtor.com/r/JQ2nqy\" target=\"_blank\">http://www.swtor.com/r/JQ2nqy</a>","edited":{"userid":414,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/414-gallus","user":"Gallus","date":". 05-13-2015, 11:20 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/414-gallus","name":"Gallus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar414_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"886"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-13T21:41:41-07:00","id":513788,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>goldfaction</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/507138-would-exigents-suffer-the-great-curse?p=513554#post513554\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think with the comparisons with mental illness we're sort of touching on the core difficulty here - ancient mythic vs. modern scientific-esque conceptions of humanity and the world. The two don't necessarily mesh, or at least need an oblique way of looking at things to mesh.<br /> <br /> Similarly with the question of whether it's redundant with the human tendency for power to corrupt.... not exactly, I think. Rather, the Great Curse is human flaws as seen through the lens of myth and tragedy, as seen through the lens of a game.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> What if the Exalted didn't have a Great Curse, but still had Limit Break. That is, the Exalted are superhuman in many respects, and just as their minds and physical bodies are often &quot;supercharged with Essence&quot; so too are their emotions. When one of the Exalted gets angry, their anger is like a burning bonfire, their love is runs as deep as the ocean and their oaths of loyalty are sharper than blades. Just as the physical and mental states of the Exalted are often above those of ordinary mortals, so too are their emotions. <br /> <br /> So the Exalted still have the concept of &quot;Limit&quot; based around their emotions, but this isn't because of some horrific Curse cast on them, but rather because having those sorts of difficult to control emotions and passions is just part of what comes with being Exalted. It's not something that can be (or should be viewed as being able to be) &quot;fixed&quot; or &quot;cured.&quot; Being incredibly passionate is simply something that the Exalted naturally are. <br /> <br /> It's a way of retaining the mythical conceit of epic humans being driven by passions while removing the baggage that comes with the idea that the Exalted suffer from an unnatural curse and the idea that it can (or even <i>needs</i> to be) fixed or cured. <br /> <br /> That's basically how I have run things in quite a few of my games since I had some players who adamantly disliked the narrative of the Great Curse in the Exalted setting, and while I didn't necessarily like the mechanics of Limit Break, I did like the basic concept, so I wanted to retain it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-13T22:20:37-07:00","id":513798,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zelbinnean</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is again a really frustrating narrative conceit that has shit-all mechanical support, which given the superheavy mechanical system for Exalted is incredibly frustrating (&quot;this is what you chose to go rules-light on?!&quot;).</div> </div> </div> </div> I would put it on about the same level as constructing the infrastructure to support an Age of wonders; it has to rely mostly on player goals and input and ST creativity more than mechanical operation, because it's supposed to operate over the course of centuries. Which is the kind of thing that I feel should make it super easy to portray a character who manages to keep the Great Curse relatively in check, because whether or not it destroys them is a narrative thing rather than a mechanical one. That's why several Shards are able to remain consistent with the idea of the Great Curse while having their Solars go in entirely different directions.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-14T00:10:09-07:00","id":513913,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zelbinnean</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/507138-would-exigents-suffer-the-great-curse?p=513557#post513557\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> And some of the Limit Breaks are just plain awful from a gameplay perspective (looking at you, Ascetic Drive).</div> </div> </div> </div>And some are pretty mild (Heart of Flint, IIRC, doesn't really do much).<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5488-goldfaction","name":"goldfaction","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"90"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-14T00:11:31-07:00","id":513926,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/507138-would-exigents-suffer-the-great-curse?p=513788#post513788\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's a way of retaining the mythical conceit of epic humans being driven by passions while removing the baggage that comes with the idea that the Exalted suffer from an unnatural curse and the idea that it can (or even <i>needs</i> to be) fixed or cured.</div> </div> </div> </div>Could certainly work, but if it were made canon, then you remove the <i>possibility</i> of fixing it for those who want to.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5488-goldfaction","name":"goldfaction","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"90"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-14T01:00:02-07:00","id":513949,"title":"","content":"Some would call that as big a feature as making the infernal exalted not even the tiniest bit involved with the idea of the yozi escaping; the loss of the ability to tell stories of preventing that escape is greatly outweighed by the benefit of making other stories tellable. The narrative conceit that &quot;fixing the single biggest problem in creation&quot; should be a relatively simple task (simpler than creating a society of exalted that governs itself properly to prevent the abuses of the first age rather than enable them), enough that a player can expect to accomplish it in a game, which by extension... basically becomes another version of the thousand dooms problem. &quot;Oh you want to create a creation spanning trade network that's cute I want to fix the world in perpetuity get on my level&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/756-meianno-yuurei","name":"Meianno Yuurei","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar756_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-14T01:05:16-07:00","id":513950,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>goldfaction</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/507138-would-exigents-suffer-the-great-curse?p=513926#post513926\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Could certainly work, but if it were made canon, then you remove the <i>possibility</i> of fixing it for those who want to.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> It's pretty safe to say an idea like that wouldn't be made canon. 3rd edition is almost ready to be published and I haven't heard anything about removing the Great Curse. So something like this might be an option for people who don't like the narrative role the Great Curse plays, but still think the concept of Limit Break, once divorced from the Great Curse, is workable.<br /> <br /> So in the above case there isn't anything <i>too</i> fix. The Exalted are just innately more emotional than normal humans (just like they're innately stronger and tougher than normal humans). I guess you could &quot;fix&quot; the problem by emotionally stapling or otherwise stunting an Exalt's emotions, but that would be like trying to make it so that Exalt's can't soak lethal damage.<br /> <br /> This would also ensure that the idea of Exalted being heroes with grand emotions isn't <i>unnatural</i> and therefore needs to be fixed. I guess one could argue that feeling emotions more strongly than normal is a flaw, but it wouldn't automatically be viewed a flaw in the eyes of the Exalted nor something they would necessarily <i>want</i> to fix; &quot;Hi, it's problematic that you love your husband <i>too</i> much, so just met me fix that problem for you. You'll still love your husband when I'm done, only just a little less than you do right now.&quot;<br /> <br /> When you present the Exalted's powerful emotions as the result of an outside Curse cast on them by the enemies of Creation (epic heroes with cursed passions), then it's only natural for players who read that to think, &quot;Gee. That's <i>bad</i>. We need to fix that problem.&quot; But if you present their powerful emotions as simply a natural part of being Exalted (epic heroes with epic passions) it doesn't necessarily come across as an issue in need of fixing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":741,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","user":"AnubisXy","date":". 05-14-2015, 06:08 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-14T08:47:08-07:00","id":514181,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/507138-would-exigents-suffer-the-great-curse?p=513788#post513788\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What if the Exalted didn't have a Great Curse, but still had Limit Break.</div> </div> </div> </div>That could work... but do they still throw tantrums with WMD? Are they still inevitably fated to destroy everything they worked for, and wreck the world?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">She/Her. I am literal-minded and write literally. If I don't say something explicitly, please never assume I implied it. The only exception is if I try to make a joke.</span></span></span></div> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">My point of view may be different from yours but is equally valid.</span></span></span><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1x1ycoxJF0G9niMt5D3Pp7owZ7tw8AJvL?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted-cWoD-ArM url mega-library</a>. Exalted <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/663334-random-name-generator\" target=\"_blank\">name-generators</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","name":"Erinys","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar896_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4235"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-14T09:13:55-07:00","id":514201,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Erinys</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/507138-would-exigents-suffer-the-great-curse?p=514181#post514181\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That could work... but do they still throw tantrums with WMD? Are they still inevitably fated to destroy everything they worked for, and wreck the world?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> The former yes, but only insofar as if Heracles had a WMD on him when he started going berserk he might have set the thing off. Herakles and Achilles are two of the major sources of the inspiration for the idea of Limit Break.<br /> <br /> Definitely no to the later however. There's no sense of inevitability or doom, so the Exalted aren't fated to destroy everything. It's just that after the Exaltation they love deeper and rage brighter. And sometimes that's definitely bad and can cause problems. But sometimes it can also be good when their great passions push them to protect the people they care about.<br /> <br /> <br /> As an aside, the way I use Limit Break in my campaigns is, I keep track of player's Limit. Sometimes they'll say, &quot;Oh! I get a Limit point from that!&quot; but often times I'll just make a note when I think their character is feeling some intense frustration.<br /> <br /> Then, when it feels like their character would be &quot;approaching his limit&quot; I pull the player aside at the end of the session, inform them that their character will Limit Break during the next session or two. Then I ask <i>which</i> Limit Break they want their character to experience (since it's more fun that way than just having a single Limit every single time). Then, in the next session or two, I set a scene where their character experiences the Limit that they chose.<br /> <br /> I find that since players get to choose which Limit Break they enter, and since I make sure that that it's going to be worked into the story, it makes it feel less punishing than the standard rules since the players know that I'm using it to advance the story, and it's not there to hurt the character or their story.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-14T09:23:14-07:00","id":514207,"title":"","content":"Overall that looks like a better way to handle limit.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">She/Her. I am literal-minded and write literally. If I don't say something explicitly, please never assume I implied it. The only exception is if I try to make a joke.</span></span></span></div> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">My point of view may be different from yours but is equally valid.</span></span></span><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1x1ycoxJF0G9niMt5D3Pp7owZ7tw8AJvL?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted-cWoD-ArM url mega-library</a>. Exalted <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/663334-random-name-generator\" target=\"_blank\">name-generators</a>.","edited":{"userid":896,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","user":"Erinys","date":". 05-14-2015, 01:12 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","name":"Erinys","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar896_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4235"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-14T10:35:11-07:00","id":514300,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>goldfaction</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/507138-would-exigents-suffer-the-great-curse?p=513913#post513913\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> And some are pretty mild (Heart of Flint, IIRC, doesn't really do much).</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> And some make no sense with the context you Limit Break in. If my character is betrayed by someone he trusted for a long time, he's going to be angry, or sad, or both..If his Virtue Flaw was Berserk Anger or Heart of Tears, this would be okay, but since I chose Compassionate Martyrdom his rage and sadness at that betrayal go into... helping oppressed innocents? ...What?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Life before Death, Strength before Weakness, Journey before Destination.&quot;<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#0000FF\">&quot;I will protect those who cannot protect themselves&quot;</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4172-marros56","name":"Marros56","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4172_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"143"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-14T10:56:31-07:00","id":514339,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Marros56</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/507138-would-exigents-suffer-the-great-curse?p=514300#post514300\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> And some make no sense with the context you Limit Break in. If my character is betrayed by someone he trusted for a long time, he's going to be angry, or sad, or both..If his Virtue Flaw was Berserk Anger or Heart of Tears, this would be okay, but since I chose Compassionate Martyrdom his rage and sadness at that betrayal go into... helping oppressed innocents? ...What?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah I think having particular triggers wouldn't be bad but the nature of the actual Break outburst needs to fit the context of what triggers it, and currently it does not.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-14T11:25:33-07:00","id":514349,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/507138-would-exigents-suffer-the-great-curse?p=508654#post508654\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, maybe they shouldn't be &quot;uncursed&quot;. Maybe the curse is dormant. Maybe the curse is twisted into resonance.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree with this.<br /> Making Abyssals uncursed seemed like a false attempt to make their redemption more relevant but really I think the Neverborn wanting their own Exalts should really have been a move in response to the long-term <b>failure</b> of the Great Curse, that while it can twist the Exalted it can only do so in ways that reflect their true nature.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/535-bastet","name":"Bastet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar535_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"337"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-14T22:45:17-07:00","id":514836,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Meianno Yuurei</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/507138-would-exigents-suffer-the-great-curse?p=513949#post513949\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Some would call that as big a feature as making the infernal exalted not even the tiniest bit involved with the idea of the yozi escaping; the loss of the ability to tell stories of preventing that escape is greatly outweighed by the benefit of making other stories tellable.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't know. I think the &quot;choking out other stories&quot; aspect of the Reclamation was a combination of people's responses to it* and Return of the Scarlet Empress. Without the silly ROTSE marriage plot, I got the feeling that letting out the Yozis would have a timescale of centuries (taking over all of Creation and totally rearranging its geomancy to be indistinguishable from <i>the living body of a Yozi</i>, a much bigger change IMO than the First Age Solars' expanding of Creation) to millennia (getting to E10 to use Oath-Shattering Strike, if that worked, or turn into a Yozi).<br /> <br /> *Which is mostly, IMO, because Malfeas as a setting is just so interesting, despite a few chapters of MoEP:Infernals attempt to turn it into &quot;pointless evil and nothing more&quot;.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5488-goldfaction","name":"goldfaction","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"90"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-14T22:51:31-07:00","id":514837,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Meianno Yuurei</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/507138-would-exigents-suffer-the-great-curse?p=513949#post513949\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The narrative conceit that &quot;fixing the single biggest problem in creation&quot; should be a relatively simple task (simpler than creating a society of exalted that governs itself properly to prevent the abuses of the first age rather than enable them), enough that a player can expect to accomplish it in a game, which by extension... basically becomes another version of the thousand dooms problem. &quot;Oh you want to create a creation spanning trade network that's cute I want to fix the world in perpetuity get on my level&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, I don't think it's necessarily within the scope of a normal game. IMO it's up there on the highest end of goals with &quot;permanently eliminate the Neverborn somehow&quot; and &quot;get the Incarnae off of the Games of Divinity&quot; (or, for Abyssals or Fair Folk, &quot;destroy all of Creation&quot;). <br /> <br /> And I think the thousand dooms thing is more a matter of perception than what's actually canon. Admittedly I don't own every 2E book, but I always got the feeling that the Deathlords and Yozi escape were on a timeline of &quot;centuries&quot; rather than &quot;right now&quot; (760+ years between the Great Contagion and Thorns, and the Deathlords are even older than that...) and that the Fair Folk invasion was &quot;could be tomorrow, but could be ten thousand years or never&quot;.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5488-goldfaction","name":"goldfaction","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"90"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-15T01:07:46-07:00","id":514879,"title":"","content":"I don't hate this idea from Anubis; I do think if you keep the current Limit Break, even divorced from the Curse, it's hard to get away from the fact that Limit Break is meant to be bad, intentionally. <br /> <br /> If you still have a special mechanical attention to the downside of heroic passion, and not a special mechanic for the positive sides, I think you're still going to get quite a lot of people going &quot;It's almost like these passions are in fact some kind of.... curse, or something&quot;.<br /> <br /> At the same time, there is also the potential that the more you make the Exalted grander in all senses in their passion than mortals, rather than specifically cursed, that could affect the dehumanisation or trivialisation of mortals that sometimes crops up, by positioning mortals as beings of generally flat and petty emotion compared to the Chosen. I'm not so certain about this one.<br /> <br /> Things to consider in the balance.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-15T02:09:32-07:00","id":514919,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>goldfaction</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/507138-would-exigents-suffer-the-great-curse?p=514837#post514837\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Oh, I don't think it's necessarily within the scope of a normal game. IMO it's up there on the highest end of goals with &quot;permanently eliminate the Neverborn somehow&quot; and &quot;get the Incarnae off of the Games of Divinity&quot; (or, for Abyssals or Fair Folk, &quot;destroy all of Creation&quot;). <br /> <br /> And I think the thousand dooms thing is more a matter of perception than what's actually canon. Admittedly I don't own every 2E book, but I always got the feeling that the Deathlords and Yozi escape were on a timeline of &quot;centuries&quot; rather than &quot;right now&quot; (760+ years between the Great Contagion and Thorns, and the Deathlords are even older than that...) and that the Fair Folk invasion was &quot;could be tomorrow, but could be ten thousand years or never&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, the problem with the Deathlords was certainly &quot;given these printed stats several of them can definitely destroy Creation right now with a single Combo, but they haven't, and there's not a good narrative reason for a couple of them not to, so there's a ton of cognitive dissonance here.&quot; <br /> <br /> Especially post DOTFA with high-Essence Solar Charms being mechanically implemented.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-15T02:29:20-07:00","id":514923,"title":"","content":"Thinking of the original question, my answer would be based on comparing Exigents to existing Exalted; if an Exigent is using power to pursue their own dreams or fulfil some integral function, a Great Curse makes sense.<br /> <br /> Liminals aren't Exigents, but I don't think a Curse fits for them, because I don't think their narrative of melancholy contemplation of their own identity and dragging the unquiet dead back into their graves requires or is suited to a tendency towards self-destructive and short-sighted extremes.<br /> <br /> I think Abyssals might implicitly go with an idea that they're a kind of fulfilment of the premise of the Great Curse, past the point of expression of the person. They even kind of reverse the dynamic, the desire to do and be something dragging back and shaping the course of the inexorable doom of the person and the world.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-15T03:45:55-07:00","id":514934,"title":"","content":"I sorta hope Liminals need to deal with something like Prometheans' Disquiet.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-15T08:10:21-07:00","id":515180,"title":"","content":"The devs said Liminals specifically don't have Disquiet or create wastelands.<br /> <br /> But I expect that, on a personal scale, most Liminals are creepier than many Infernals. They only have past life memories for what it's like to be or act human.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">She/Her. I am literal-minded and write literally. If I don't say something explicitly, please never assume I implied it. The only exception is if I try to make a joke.</span></span></span></div> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">My point of view may be different from yours but is equally valid.</span></span></span><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1x1ycoxJF0G9niMt5D3Pp7owZ7tw8AJvL?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted-cWoD-ArM url mega-library</a>. Exalted <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/663334-random-name-generator\" target=\"_blank\">name-generators</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","name":"Erinys","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar896_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4235"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-15T08:24:24-07:00","id":515213,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Erinys</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/507138-would-exigents-suffer-the-great-curse?p=515180#post515180\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The devs said Liminals specifically don't have Disquiet or create wastelands.</div> </div> </div> </div>Indeed. That said, the elaboration on their anima banners suggests they just might have something in that vein:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Holden</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">They don't have a Disquiet mechanic like Prometheans, and don't generate anything like the Wasteland Effect.<br /> I do strongly suggest you put down anything fragile and take a seat before they start flaring their anima, though.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Erinys</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">But I expect that, on a personal scale, most Liminals are creepier than many Infernals. They don't even know what it's like to be or act human.</div> </div> </div> </div>I dunno. Chernozem do have memories from the people whose bodies make them up, which would leave many of them with some idea. Matching that against someone who throws around the power of a realm that most in Creation find inherently unsettling... I would really see it depending on the person and Exalts in question.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalted_3E:What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">The EX3 What We Know Wiki</a>, courtesy of Marin and JMobius<br /> <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com\" target=\"_blank\">Nishkriya, the EX3 Freelancer Quotes Tracker</a>, courtesy of Anathema and Moonwolf<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The White Wolf Forum Archive</a>, courtesy of The Dark Wizard and Sanctaphrax (see <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/PhilippeSaner?u=159709\" target=\"_blank\">its Patreon</a>) <hr />Arrghus: There's also the Shepherd of the North Star, busily guiding the one thing in all the heavens that <i>doesn't move</i>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","name":"Gaius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-15T08:33:36-07:00","id":515221,"title":"","content":"But I mean they're patched together from corpses, swap out body parts, and have underworld powers. They're gonna be creepy anyway.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">She/Her. I am literal-minded and write literally. If I don't say something explicitly, please never assume I implied it. The only exception is if I try to make a joke.</span></span></span></div> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">My point of view may be different from yours but is equally valid.</span></span></span><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1x1ycoxJF0G9niMt5D3Pp7owZ7tw8AJvL?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted-cWoD-ArM url mega-library</a>. Exalted <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/663334-random-name-generator\" target=\"_blank\">name-generators</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","name":"Erinys","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar896_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4235"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-15T08:50:14-07:00","id":515226,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Erinys</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/507138-would-exigents-suffer-the-great-curse?p=515221#post515221\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But I mean they're patched together from corpses, swap out body parts, and have underworld powers. They're gonna be creepy anyway.</div> </div> </div> </div>Just saying, that seems like a good foundation for a Limit thing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-15T09:06:16-07:00","id":515239,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zelbinnean</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/507138-would-exigents-suffer-the-great-curse?p=515226#post515226\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just saying, that seems like a good foundation for a Limit thing.</div> </div> </div> </div>I've always felt that the powers that be needed to have some overriding narrative control over their own realms, which leads me to posit that not having a Great Curse, or its analogues in Creation would create an interesting plot point, regarding what those given powers want with Creation itself. If no one has overriding narrative control of Creation, then it becomes a tremendously powerful tactical asset for those that can gain that control.<br /> <br /> I guess what I'm saying is that the Great Curse should be universal or not at all, at least in Creation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Crunch isn't a hobby; it's a calling.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1959-hexmeister-vic","name":"Hexmeister Vic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1959_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"764"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-15T10:31:53-07:00","id":515272,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Erinys</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/507138-would-exigents-suffer-the-great-curse?p=515221#post515221\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But I mean they're patched together from corpses, swap out body parts, and have underworld powers. They're gonna be creepy anyway.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not saying there's nothing creepy about Liminals, just as I wouldn't say there's nothing creepy about Infernals. They're different flavors of creepy. If your stance is that the majority of Creation's people would find most Liminals creepier than most Infernals, I'd contest that: different people are going to have different predilections for which is creepier. I don't see a generalization one way or the other working out, absent further information.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalted_3E:What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">The EX3 What We Know Wiki</a>, courtesy of Marin and JMobius<br /> <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com\" target=\"_blank\">Nishkriya, the EX3 Freelancer Quotes Tracker</a>, courtesy of Anathema and Moonwolf<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The White Wolf Forum Archive</a>, courtesy of The Dark Wizard and Sanctaphrax (see <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/PhilippeSaner?u=159709\" target=\"_blank\">its Patreon</a>) <hr />Arrghus: There's also the Shepherd of the North Star, busily guiding the one thing in all the heavens that <i>doesn't move</i>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","name":"Gaius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-15T11:07:03-07:00","id":515304,"title":"","content":"Now I'm wondering, what would Alchemicals with the Great Curse be like...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-15T13:48:30-07:00","id":515416,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/507138-would-exigents-suffer-the-great-curse?p=515304#post515304\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Now I'm wondering, what would Alchemicals with the Great Curse be like...</div> </div> </div> </div>I want to say Clarity is problematic enough but I'd actually like to see stuff beyond &quot;turns into a city&quot; because that's not really practical in 99.9% of games.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-15T14:20:06-07:00","id":515442,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zelbinnean</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">I want to say Clarity is problematic enough</div> </div> </div> </div> Say whaaaat? <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zelbinnean</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd actually like to see stuff beyond &quot;turns into a city&quot; because that's not really practical in 99.9% of games</div> </div> </div> </div> I don't see how this follows.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-15T17:25:52-07:00","id":515618,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zelbinnean</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/507138-would-exigents-suffer-the-great-curse?p=515416#post515416\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I want to say Clarity is problematic enough</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/507138-would-exigents-suffer-the-great-curse?p=515442#post515442\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Say whaaaat?</div> </div> </div> </div>Only if they keep they Alchemicals within Autocthonia, which with EX3's stated focus being Creation, will be unlikely. Personally, I think that Clarity works better in Autocthonia then in creation, for the reasons stated above. <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zelbinnean</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/507138-would-exigents-suffer-the-great-curse?p=515416#post515416\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">but I'd actually like to see stuff beyond &quot;turns into a city&quot; because that's not really practical in 99.9% of games.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/507138-would-exigents-suffer-the-great-curse?p=515442#post515442\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't see how this follows.</div> </div> </div> </div>One has very little to do with the other, RAW. We may see some stronger, more compelling reasons to want to make the transition in the next edition, as well as some compelling counterarguments. Real question is how much of a magitech-centric splat is going to survive a magitech-light edition?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Crunch isn't a hobby; it's a calling.","edited":{"userid":1959,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1959-hexmeister-vic","user":"Hexmeister Vic","date":". 05-15-2015, 08:39 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1959-hexmeister-vic","name":"Hexmeister Vic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1959_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"764"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-15T17:51:54-07:00","id":515647,"title":"","content":"I should clarify; I don't see how talking about elder Alchemicals has anything to do with the demerits of Clarity.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-15T18:04:26-07:00","id":515654,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hexmeister Vic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/507138-would-exigents-suffer-the-great-curse?p=515618#post515618\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Real question is how much of a magitech-centric splat is going to survive a magitech-light edition?</div> </div> </div> </div>They did pretty fine in 1e.<br /> <br /> Alchie themes don't need to be &quot;magitech&quot; as that term of art was used in 2e. Not all steampunk and clockwork is magitech. Magitech is a very specific thing. And Alchies had a very strong presentation mechanically last ed, and with their setting, that worked perfectly fine. <br /> <br /> I'm not too worried. Alchies have consistently been amazing. Lunars and Sids, on the other hand...I think everyone is holding their breath for them, especially the former.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/507138-would-exigents-suffer-the-great-curse?p=515442#post515442\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Say whaaaat? I don't see how this follows.</div> </div> </div> </div>I probably shouldn't have posted while tired at work, haha.<br /> <br /> Clarity does represent a control mechanic though, that forces your personality to change over time in the long term. That seems to be to be just as problematic to me as a control mechanic that mandates certain behavior, even if only for short periods.<br /> <br /> Cities, eh, more of a corollary complaint. Mandatorily turning into a Guntank and then into a city as you gain more enlightenment is kind of a pain.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-15T18:10:00-07:00","id":515658,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zelbinnean</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/507138-would-exigents-suffer-the-great-curse?p=515416#post515416\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I want to say Clarity is problematic enough but I'd actually like to see stuff beyond &quot;turns into a city&quot; because that's not really practical in 99.9% of games.</div> </div> </div> </div>Don't be afraid to dream bigger, darling.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Neall Raemonn Price</span><br /> Beleaguered Scion Developer</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","name":"Neall","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1204"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-15T18:14:48-07:00","id":515661,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zelbinnean</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Clarity does represent a control mechanic though, that forces your personality to change over time in the long term.</div> </div> </div> </div> I know, right? You try playing a strictly logical, analytical, utilitarian character who only goes for the most efficient methods of constructing those hospitals in pursuit of their Compassion 5, but the fact that such a character logically knows that they'll be at their most efficient when channeling that high Compassion for dice bonuses, which then goes and reduces their Clarity and renders them susceptible to the insinuation of human relationships again, it's so irritating. <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zelbinnean</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mandatorily turning into a Guntank and then into a city as you gain more enlightenment is kind of a pain.</div> </div> </div> </div> Will it help when the game is more honest about how you're never really going to have Essence above 5?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-15T18:16:04-07:00","id":515662,"title":"","content":"I think the main thing that makes me like Clarity in a way that I don't like the Limit mechanics is how Clarity is a thing that you manage, rather than a thing that just happens. If your character doesn't like Clarity, there are things that they can do to reduce it and keep it at an acceptable level for them, whereas you are explicitly forbidden from ever recognizing that the Great Curse is a thing. Infernals similarly have the ability to recognize and manage their Torment, but Clarity has the additional good quality of being a bit of carrot together with the stick. There are benefits for having high Clarity that might make you want to have it sometimes despite the penalties. Ultimately it's made your choice how much you want to engage with Clarity or fight it off, and if you want to fight it off you can win.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/598-couch","name":"Couch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar598_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"330"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-15T18:18:03-07:00","id":515663,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/507138-would-exigents-suffer-the-great-curse?p=515304#post515304\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Now I'm wondering, what would Alchemicals with the Great Curse be like...</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd basically invert how Clarity is normally gained/lost so that it was gained from social contact and lost through solitude. The immediate result would be a far greater number of Alchemicals being perceived as sociopathic robots.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-15T18:57:08-07:00","id":515681,"title":"","content":"In that vein, it might be interesting for Alchemicals to gain Clarity when they fail a task given to them by mortals or when they're given advice by mortals and don't interpret the context correctly. That's usually how AIs go killbot.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/75951-ex3-why-gods-need-the-exigence\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] Why Gods Need the Exigence</a> - Plot hooks for Exigent characters of various gods.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/113648-ex3-homebrew-solar-charms\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] Homebrew Solar Charms</a> - I can see the future, and it is glorious.<br /> <a href=\"https://glasslibrary.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] The Glass Library</a> - My Exalted Third Edition Blog (Updated 24/04/2016)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/54-tiresias","name":"Tiresias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar54_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2340"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-15T23:39:56-07:00","id":515877,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">The immediate result would be a far greater number of Alchemicals being perceived as sociopathic robots.</div> </div> </div> </div> If somebody is playing high Clarity Alchemicals as sociopaths, then they're doing it wrong. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tiresias</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">In that vein, it might be interesting for Alchemicals to gain Clarity when they fail a task given to them by mortals or when they're given advice by mortals and don't interpret the context correctly. That's usually how AIs go killbot.</div> </div> </div> </div> I... don't get it. Are you saying that their Curse would give them responses that cause them to act like robots more than what they actually are?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-15T23:43:32-07:00","id":515879,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Couch</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">you are explicitly forbidden from ever recognizing that the Great Curse is a thing.</div> </div> </div> </div> Where is this explicit statement? I'd like to review it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-15T23:48:22-07:00","id":515884,"title":"","content":"Don't Solars have a charm that specifically acts as an alert that says &quot;Warning, Solar in Limit Break, steer clear!&quot;? I'm pretty sure at least some of them know it's a thing for that to exist, and to be purchasable.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/themes/stvault/images/affiliatebanner4.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Christopher%20Falco&amp;affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\">Storytellers' Vault supplements (WoD, CoD)</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/FalconianP\" target=\"_blank\">My Patreon! (CofD bonuses include: Fae Sorcery/Technomancy for Vampires, Quick Conversion for Inferno, and more!)</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1130-falco1029","name":"falco1029","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1130_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1045"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-16T02:59:45-07:00","id":516005,"title":"","content":"Yes.<br /> Probably that charm was a bad idea.<br /> (To be fair, the most likely response is for the player party to freak out that some stealthy bad guy is secretly mind-controlling their friend. Like a Sidereal, or maybe a ghost or demon possessing him. It's going to take a while for them to realise it's a 5000 year old curse. Still...)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-16T06:57:44-07:00","id":516140,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/507138-would-exigents-suffer-the-great-curse?p=515877#post515877\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I... don't get it. Are you saying that their Curse would give them responses that cause them to act like robots more than what they actually are?</div> </div> </div> </div>What usually happens when AIs malfunction is that 1) they're told to do X and fail, so they need to find another way to achieve X, and the method with the highest possibility of success is to just kill everyone, or 2) they're told to do X and Y, but X and Y are mutually exclusive, so the AI starts to break down from the contradiction. In both cases, a human would put things in context and &quot;cheat&quot; - they'd try another method, knowing that it might not succeed but that it would still give them a higher chance of success, or they would just ignore the contradiction in their orders. Either way, failure isn't that big a deal. A robot can't do that. To a robot, failure is a fundamental flaw in its programming. <br /> <br /> What I'm saying is that an Alchemical Curse could feed upon the self-doubt Alchemicals feel because of their failures or on the internal conflicts that arise when Alchemicals are unable to relate to mortals. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/75951-ex3-why-gods-need-the-exigence\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] Why Gods Need the Exigence</a> - Plot hooks for Exigent characters of various gods.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/113648-ex3-homebrew-solar-charms\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] Homebrew Solar Charms</a> - I can see the future, and it is glorious.<br /> <a href=\"https://glasslibrary.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] The Glass Library</a> - My Exalted Third Edition Blog (Updated 24/04/2016)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/54-tiresias","name":"Tiresias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar54_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2340"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-16T07:26:51-07:00","id":516181,"title":"","content":"I find comparing that to the fictional depiction of A.I. to be weird.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-16T07:39:18-07:00","id":516184,"title":"","content":"I can't really think of other narrative conventions that would apply to an Alchemical Great Curse. The Solar Great Curse is easy to get inspiration for because it's all over Greek mythology, but I don't think there's much inspiration for Alchemicals outside science fiction, which tends towards malfunctioning AIs. Even if you go further back, do Pinocchio and Frankenstein offer a lot of inspiration for a Great Curse that fits Alchemicals?<br /> <br /> Although I did toy with that idea that the Alchemical narrative should be based mythological weapons like Excalibur a few years back. Maybe that's more useful.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/75951-ex3-why-gods-need-the-exigence\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] Why Gods Need the Exigence</a> - Plot hooks for Exigent characters of various gods.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/113648-ex3-homebrew-solar-charms\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] Homebrew Solar Charms</a> - I can see the future, and it is glorious.<br /> <a href=\"https://glasslibrary.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] The Glass Library</a> - My Exalted Third Edition Blog (Updated 24/04/2016)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/54-tiresias","name":"Tiresias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar54_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2340"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-16T07:46:26-07:00","id":516186,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>falco1029</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/507138-would-exigents-suffer-the-great-curse?p=515884#post515884\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Don't Solars have a charm that specifically acts as an alert that says &quot;Warning, Solar in Limit Break, steer clear!&quot;? I'm pretty sure at least some of them know it's a thing for that to exist, and to be purchasable.</div> </div> </div> </div>Stuff like that is, charitably, questionable design space. <i>At best</i>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-16T12:46:59-07:00","id":516407,"title":"","content":"I don't know Alchemicals as well as many here, still if you wanted a Great Curse for the Alchemicals, I would be tempted to start more with just looking at their Castes role in Autochthonian society, and then their individual virtues and intimacies; that stuff seems really to explain who they are as individuals.<br /> <br /> Maybe look at them from the point of view that more than other Exalted they are Exalted to be champions of their society, and their most tragic downfall would relate to their personal failure in that role, in their role as the myth heroes of their world.<br /> <br /> Their technological aspects are nice, and important, but I feel like if they had failure on a human level and character based due to very human aspects that might hit us hard in the gut.<br /> <br /> You might want to somehow work in the core characteristics of Autochthon's personal vices in there, or subversions of his virtues of Faith, Dogma and Tools.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-16T12:53:29-07:00","id":516422,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ghosthead</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/507138-would-exigents-suffer-the-great-curse?p=516407#post516407\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't know Alchemicals as well as many here, still if you wanted a Great Curse for the Alchemicals, I would be tempted to start more with just looking at their Castes role in Autochthonian society, and then their individual virtues and intimacies; that stuff seems really to explain who they are as individuals.<br /> <br /> Maybe look at them from the point of view that more than other Exalted they are Exalted to be champions of their society, and their most tragic downfall would relate to their personal failure in that role, in their role as the myth heroes of their world.</div> </div> </div> </div>Caste-based curses would be pretty cool. Like an inherent, inevitable bug in the design of each Caste...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-16T15:23:04-07:00","id":516507,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ghosthead</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/507138-would-exigents-suffer-the-great-curse?p=514879#post514879\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you still have a special mechanical attention to the downside of heroic passion, and not a special mechanic for the positive sides, I think you're still going to get quite a lot of people going &quot;It's almost like these passions are in fact some kind of.... curse, or something&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think the upside is represented by some Charms.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zelbinnean</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/507138-would-exigents-suffer-the-great-curse?p=514919#post514919\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> No, the problem with the Deathlords was certainly &quot;given these printed stats several of them can definitely destroy Creation right now with a single Combo, but they haven't, and there's not a good narrative reason for a couple of them not to, so there's a ton of cognitive dissonance here.&quot;<br /> <br /> Especially post DOTFA with high-Essence Solar Charms being mechanically implemented.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, but I'm talking about setting, not mechanics. The DLs could have steamrolled Creation 1500 years ago, mechanically. Setting-wise, their timescale seemed very slow.<br /> <br /> (And the &quot;single combo&quot; thing was only a consequence of &quot;line of sight range&quot; being potentially infinite in a flat world, not something the Charms were actually meant to do.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5488-goldfaction","name":"goldfaction","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"90"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-17T01:33:36-07:00","id":516868,"title":"","content":"The Deathlords are supposed to have made relatively little progress in over a thousand years because they're bad at and disinterested in their vaguely assigned task of killing the world. Problems with Charms weren't as bad as when books started alternately writing them as actually motivated towards destroying the world or unable to resist doing so. Really, putting one of them at the front of an end of the world plot within an individual game is no problem, but it's easier to add on then take away, and the premise of them as schemers for temporal power in a gothic wonderland offers more variety from the outset.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-17T01:43:34-07:00","id":516870,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zelbinnean</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/507138-would-exigents-suffer-the-great-curse?p=516422#post516422\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Caste-based curses would be pretty cool.</div> </div> </div> </div>Honestly, for some of the other Exalted, I don't actually really like the &quot;This is your Caste; this is your Curse&quot; idea, as seems like it cuts down on thinking about how the character's personality diverges from his caste, a little, compared to the Solar approach, of Virtue based curses.<br /> <br /> For an alternate Alchemicals curse, though it feels like it could work because they seem like they really do have Castes in such a defined way that feels like it comes first (&quot;You I have wrought from Orichalcum, and you were made to be bright and to be shining and to lead&quot;).<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-18T15:21:18-07:00","id":518505,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/507138-would-exigents-suffer-the-great-curse?p=515879#post515879\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Where is this explicit statement? I'd like to review it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Apologies in taking a bit to get back to you on this, needed access to my books. A few instances spring to mind:<ul><li>2E Core states that the Curse is unrecognized by the Exalted, echoed by most of the MoEPs. Since one minute they did not suffer from Limit Breaks and suddenly they did, their failure to notice either has to be linked to a compulsion not to or they're just idiots.</li> <li>Similarly, Lunars labor under the misconception that their Limit Breaks are a thing that Luna wants them to have, so either they're incapable of recognizing it or Luna is just an asshole.</li> <li>Also Autochthon, who knew about the Curse but decided not to tell anyone for no particular reason.</li> <li>And Gorol, but Gorol actually did go crazy after that so he gets a pass.</li> <li>Madness-Analyzing Stare &quot;can neither diagnose or aid in curing any aspect of the Great Curse&quot; even though it can tell what your Virtue Flaw is, so there is in fact a warping of perspective occuring.</li> <li>Eye and Seven Despairs' writeup in MoEP: Abyssals notes that as soon as they died all of the Solars were freed from the Curse, instantly realized how horrible they'd been, repented of their sins and entered Lethe. So clearly this is not natural behavior for them. This is the most explicit statement in that regard, as it indicates that if you didn't have the Curse you'd obviously see that you were acting crazy.</li> </ul>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/598-couch","name":"Couch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar598_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"330"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-18T15:26:36-07:00","id":518511,"title":"","content":"I prefer to think of that last one as a specific effect of having the Curse <b><i>removed</i></b>. You experience an epiphany in which every limit break, and everything you've ever, ever done that was influenced or warped by the Curse, flashes through your mind in vivid detail. You realize how the Curse, specifically, has (facilitated the change) from who you were as a mortal, how it has shaped your decisions and demeanor, and how you've departed from the morals and behavior and sanity of your youth. How you react to that is personal -- clearly, the Deathlords didn't decide that repenting of their evil was the answer.<br /> <br /> I think that if the Curse was cured, something like the above would happen. Eventually the Exalted would start investigating and find out at least some of what happened. And I expect that at least a couple elder Sidereals and/or Lunars would kill themselves.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">She/Her. I am literal-minded and write literally. If I don't say something explicitly, please never assume I implied it. The only exception is if I try to make a joke.</span></span></span></div> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">My point of view may be different from yours but is equally valid.</span></span></span><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1x1ycoxJF0G9niMt5D3Pp7owZ7tw8AJvL?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted-cWoD-ArM url mega-library</a>. Exalted <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/663334-random-name-generator\" target=\"_blank\">name-generators</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","name":"Erinys","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar896_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4235"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-18T15:32:27-07:00","id":518519,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Couch</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/507138-would-exigents-suffer-the-great-curse?p=518505#post518505\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Eye and Seven Despairs' writeup in MoEP: Abyssals notes that as soon as they died all of the Solars were freed from the Curse, instantly realized how horrible they'd been, repented of their sins and entered Lethe. So clearly this is not natural behavior for them. This is the most explicit statement in that regard, as it indicates that if you didn't have the Curse you'd obviously see that you were acting crazy.</div> </div> </div> </div>Frankly I consider this to be a truly terrible, wanky cop-out.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Erinys</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/507138-would-exigents-suffer-the-great-curse?p=518511#post518511\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">how you've departed from the morals and behavior and sanity of your youth</div> </div> </div> </div>If you ever had that stuff to begin with. Hell, even if you did, the human mind is incredibly good at rationalization.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":3420,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","user":"Zelbinnean","date":". 05-18-2015, 06:36 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-18T19:15:40-07:00","id":518668,"title":"","content":"Which is why every reaction would be personal, and &quot;repenting of your sins&quot; in no way guaranteed. Some Exalted would no doubt come away with a strong impression that they were naive twats when they were younger.<br /> <br /> Overall it would definitely improve things, but it wouldn't automatically turn every Elder into a wise, Good person.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">She/Her. I am literal-minded and write literally. If I don't say something explicitly, please never assume I implied it. The only exception is if I try to make a joke.</span></span></span></div> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">My point of view may be different from yours but is equally valid.</span></span></span><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1x1ycoxJF0G9niMt5D3Pp7owZ7tw8AJvL?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted-cWoD-ArM url mega-library</a>. Exalted <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/663334-random-name-generator\" target=\"_blank\">name-generators</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","name":"Erinys","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar896_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4235"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}